c":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"GRB 240825A : Early Reverse Shock and Its Physical Implications","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828925","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: As an approved targeting drug, crizotinib has been widely used in the treatment of patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) with anaplastic lymphoma kinase (ALK) rearrangements or c-ros oncogene 1 (ROS1) fusions and has demonstrated remarkable therapeutic effects. However, crizotinib-treated patients frequently experience drug resistance, and there are still some underlying mechanisms, which remain unclear. Autophagy, a cellular process that involves the degradation and recycling of cellular components, has been implicated in the development of drug resistance. In this study, we aim to elucidate the mechanisms of crizotinib resistance involving autophagy dysregulation and identify novel therapeutic targets to overcome this resistance. Methods: We first established a model for crizotinib resistance in HCC78 and H3122 cells. Next, the level of proliferation, apoptosis, autophagy flux, and reactive oxygen species (ROS) of these cells were measured. Subsequently, we analyzed the published single-cell RNA sequencing data from three ALK-rearranged lung cancer organoid samples and performed a metabolomics assay on crizotinib-resistant HCC78 cells. Finally, the therapeutic effects were confirmed in vitro by targeting autophagy flux. Results: Crizotinib induced cell apoptosis and growth arrest by promoting the accumulation of autophagosomes through the inhibition of autophagy flux in ROS1+ or ALK+ NSCLC. In contrast, crizotinib-resistant NSCLC cells showed inactivation of signal transducer and activator of transcription 3 (STAT3) phosphorylation and downregulation of prostaglandin endoperoxide synthase 2 (PTGS2), leading to an increase in the metabolite arachidonic acid (AA). AA further promoted autophagy flux and reduced autophagosome accumulation, driving crizotinib resistance under conditions of drug stress. Moreover, chloroquine (CQ), anti-malaria drug and lysosome inhibitor developed in 1940, could induce cell death in crizotinib-resistant NSCLC by blocking AA-mediated autophagy flux and facilitating autophagosome accumulation, significantly enhancing the treatment efficacy of crizotinib in drug-resistant NSCLC. Conclusions: We discovered a new mechanism of first generation ALK- and ROS1-TKIs resistance, which points to the role of the metabolite AA in resistance to tyrosine kinase inhibitors. It may potentially provide an alternative strategy to overcoming crizotinib resistance in NSCLC treatment by reversing AA-mediated autophagy.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Jie, Hui","Lai, Hongjin","Wang, Zihuai","Yi, Min","Liu, Yi","Urbanska, Edyta Maria","Santoni-Rugiu, Eric","Wei, Shiyou","Chen, Yuhao","Li, Chuan","Wang, Tengyong","Luo, Nanzhi","Liu, Lunxu","Deng, Senyi","Guo, Chenglin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-809118"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Sichuan University"],"keyword":["Non small cell lung cancer NSCLC","tyrosine kinase inhibitors TKIs"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"targeting of arachidonic acid modulated autophagy to enhance the sensitivity of ros000000000001 sup sup or alk sup sup non small cell lung cancer to crizotinib therapy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21037/tlcr-2025-105","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-809118","identifier":[{"id":"40248722","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12000944","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"105001567043","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-13133e46-34b9-4c7e-9b72-56d5b7a7555b"],"keyword":["Non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC)","arachidonic acid (AA)","autophagy flux","crizotinib resistance","tyrosine kinase inhibitors (TKIs)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C0180EDD498790250901D4B051154B64"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/446051389/98150-PB12-8165-R2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21037/tlcr-2025-105","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"sichuan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sichuan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Hui","key":"jiehuipau","last":"Jie","name":"Jie, Hui","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hongjin","key":"laihongjinpau","last":"Lai","name":"Lai, Hongjin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Zihuai","key":"wangzihuaipau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Zihuai","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Min","key":"yiminpau","last":"Yi","name":"Yi, Min","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yi","key":"liuyipau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Yi","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Edyta Maria","key":"urbanskaedytamariapau","last":"Urbanska","name":"Urbanska, Edyta Maria","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Eric","key":"santonirugiuericpau","last":"Santoni-Rugiu","locid":"426bc32e-067f-44fb-9cca-b93d1198a5d4","name":"Santoni-Rugiu, Eric","orcid":"0000-0002-2283-3535","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Shiyou","key":"weishiyoupau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Shiyou","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yuhao","key":"chenyuhaopau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Yuhao","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chuan","key":"lichuanpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Chuan","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tengyong","key":"wangtengyongpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Tengyong","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nanzhi","key":"luonanzhipau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Nanzhi","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lunxu","key":"liulunxupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Lunxu","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Senyi","key":"dengsenyipau","last":"Deng","name":"Deng, Senyi","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chenglin","key":"guochenglinpau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Chenglin","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40248722"],"pub":{"doi":"10.21037/tlcr-2025-105","issn":["22186751","22264477"],"issn_org":["22186751"],"issue":"3","journal":"Translational Lung Cancer Research","pages":"878-896","status":"p","title":"Translational Lung Cancer Research","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105001567043"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-13133e46-34b9-4c7e-9b72-56d5b7a7555b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Targeting of arachidonic acid-modulated autophagy to enhance the sensitivity of ROS1<sup>+</sup> or ALK<sup>+</sup> non-small cell lung cancer to crizotinib therapy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-809118","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Extreme environments foster phylogenetically diverse microorganisms and unique community assembly patterns. Plateau saline marsh lakes represent understudied extreme habitats characterized by dual stressors of high salinity and low temperature. Here, we analyzed the soil bacterial and archaeal diversity in three salt marshes of the Qaidam Basin on the Qinghai-Tibetan Plateau, China. While the bacterial and archaeal alpha diversity showed no significant differences among the three salt marshes, the community composition varied significantly. Notably, soil salinity (indicated by electric conductivity, EC) exerted opposing effects on microbial diversity—suppressing bacterial while promoting archaeal communities. Stochastic processes were the predominant mechanism for both bacterial and archaeal community assembly, where the weights were, in descending order, drift, homogeneous selection, and dispersal limitation. Network analysis revealed predominantly positive co-occurrence patterns within both bacterial and archaeal communities. We did not find a direct relationship between any bacterial or archaeal co-occurrence network properties and soil EC, but there was a significant correlation of network complexity to microbial diversity, which was influenced by EC. Our findings indicate distinct responses of bacterial and archaeal diversity to varying salinity levels, while the underlying assembly processes appear to be conserved in driving shifts in community diversity in plateau salt marsh wetlands.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Zhu, Pengcheng","Wang, Yuhui","Sheng, Wenyi","Yu, Mingyang","Wei, Wei","Sun, Wenlong","Gao, Jian","Xu, Zhenwei","Cao, Ming","Wang, Yuzhi","Liu, Lele","Guo, Weihua"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-816198"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Guo, Weihua","Liu, Lele"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hubei University of Technology","Peking University","Shandong University","Tianshui Normal University"],"keyword":["Community assembly","Microbial interactions","Salt marshes","Soil salinity","Stochastic processes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"salinity effect on soil bacterial and archaeal diversity and assembly in phragmites australis salt marshes in the qaidam basin china","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/microorganisms13061253","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-816198","identifier":[{"id":"105009070436","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12195177","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40572143","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-8faa2097-f009-4175-8303-fdd9c2622aae"],"keyword":["community assembly","microbial interactions","salt marshes","soil salinity","stochastic processes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B21642C74825499371D54C5CD0481EB4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/microorganisms13061253","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"shandong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"hubei university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hubei University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Center for Ecological Dynamics in a Novel Bios