{"abstract":"Embedding semiconductor quantum dots (QDs) into a 2D transition metal dichalcogenide (TMDCs) can significantly modulate the electronic charge transfer and, hence, the nonlinear optical (NLO) properties of the TMDCs. However, the influence of strong interactions within 2D nanostructure-QDs composites on their third-order NLO responses has not been explored thus far. The third-order NLO characteristics of few-layered MoS2 nanosheets embedded with CdSe and CdSe/V2O5 QDs are studied using 35-fs pulses at 400 and 800 nm excitations. It is observed that an alteration of the third-order NLO properties in MoS2 occurs in the presence of QDs. Notably, the MoS2-QDs hybrid system exhibits a significant modulation in third-order nonlinearities, with a substantial multi-fold increase in the figure of merit in the presence of core CdSe QDs and suppression with passivated CdSe/V2O5 QDs. These findings strongly indicate that QD-based hybrid systems with charge transfer channels probably enhance carrier mobility and enable tunable electron transfer dynamics, which can emerge as a viable strategy for tailoring third-order NLO properties in TMDCs, positioning these hybrid materials as promising candidates for optoelectronic applications.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Konda, Srinivasa Rao","Barik, Puspendu","Singh, Subhash","Mottamchetty, Venkatesh","Srivasthava, Amit","Ganeev, Rashid A.","Soma, Venugopal Rao","Guo, Chunlei","Li, Wei"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-816717"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, Central","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Asia, South","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Konda, Srinivasa Rao","Li, Wei","Singh, Subhash"],"country":["Azerbaijan","China","India","Russia","United Arab Emirates","United States","Uzbekistan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","American University of Sharjah","CAS - Changchun Institute of Optics Fine Mechanics and Physics","Indian Institute of Technology Ropar","Tashkent Institute of Irrigation and Agricultural Mechanization Engineers","University of Hyderabad","University of Rochester","Veer Bahadur Singh Purvanchal University","Voronezh State University","Western Caspian University"],"keyword":["CdSe","Nonlinear optical properties","Quantum dots"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"third order nonlinear optical modulation in mos sub 000000000002 sub nanosheets in the presence of cdse and cdse v sub 000000000002 sub o sub 000000000005 sub quantum dots","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105007825444","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-816717","identifier":[{"id":"105007825444","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-d4026243-5df4-41f9-b1db-4e6b99a6a0f2"],"keyword":["CdSe","CdSe/VO","MoS nanosheets","charge transfer mechanism","nonlinear optical properties","quantum dots"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-04F32D0A3AAF230045A8EFE7D49DF38C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"cas changchun institute of optics fine mechanics and physics","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Changchun Institute of Optics Fine Mechanics and Physics","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"in","key":"indian institute of technology ropar","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Indian Institute of Technology Ropar","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ae","key":"american university of sharjah","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"American University of Sharjah","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of rochester","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Rochester","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Physics and Astronomy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"in","key":"veer bahadur singh purvanchal university","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Veer Bahadur Singh Purvanchal University","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"ru","key":"voronezh state university","loc":["Russia","Europe, Non-EU"],"name":"Voronezh State University","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"az","key":"western caspian university","loc":["Azerbaijan","Asia, Central"],"name":"Western Caspian University","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"uz","key":"tashkent institute of irrigation and agricultural mechanization engineers","loc":["Uzbekistan","Asia, Central"],"name":"Tashkent Institute of Irrigation and Agricultural Mechanization Engineers","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"in","key":"university of hyderabad","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"University of Hyderabad","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Srinivasa Rao","key":"kondapau","last":"Konda","name":"Konda, Srinivasa Rao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Puspendu","key":"barikpau","last":"Barik","name":"Barik, Puspendu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Subhash","key":"singhpau","last":"Singh","name":"Singh, Subhash","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Venkatesh","key":"mottamchettypau","last":"Mottamchetty","locid":"fd54a93b-1e9f-421d-ab1a-3b7bf5f08eef","name":"Mottamchetty, Venkatesh","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Amit","key":"srivasthavapau","last":"Srivasthava","name":"Srivasthava, Amit","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7 8 9","corresponding":null,"first":"Rashid A.","key":"ganeevpau","last":"Ganeev","name":"Ganeev, Rashid A.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","corresponding":null,"first":"Venugopal Rao","key":"somapau","last":"Soma","name":"Soma, Venugopal Rao","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Chunlei","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Chunlei","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Wei","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/adom.202402416","issn":["21951071"],"issue":"18","journal":"Advanced Optical Materials","paperid":"2402416","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Advanced Optical Materials","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105007825444"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d4026243-5df4-41f9-b1db-4e6b99a6a0f2"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Third-Order Nonlinear Optical Modulation in MoS<sub>2</sub> Nanosheets in the Presence of CdSe and CdSe/V<sub>2</sub>O<sub>5</sub> Quantum Dots","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-816717","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The prompt emission and afterglow phases of gamma-ray bursts (GRBs) have been extensively studied, yet the transition between these two phases remains inadequately characterized due to limited multiwavelength observational coverage. Among the recent growing samples of fast X-ray transients observed by Einstein Probe (EP), a subgroup of GRBs are captured with long-duration X-ray emission, potentially containing featured evolution from prompt emission to the afterglow phase. In this Letter, we present a detailed analysis of GRB 250404A/EP250404a, a bright, fast X-ray transient detected simultaneously by EP and the Fermi Gamma-ray Burst Monitor in X-rays and gamma rays. Its continuous X-ray emission reveals a long-duration tail, accompanied by distinct spectral evolution manifested by the spectral index alpha X with an initial softening, followed by an evident hardening, eventually reaching a plateau at the value of similar to-2. Early optical and near-infrared observations enable broadband modeling with forward- and reverse-shock components, confirming that the X-ray hardening signals the emergence of the external-shock afterglow. From this spectral hardening, we infer that the prompt phase in soft X-rays lasted similar to 300 s, which is more than 3 times longer than the gamma-ray T90. This well-tracked soft-hard-flat spectral pattern provides a clear indication of afterglow emergence from the fading prompt emission and offers a practical criterion for identifying a distinct population of GRBs among fast X-ray transients, even when the detection of the gamma-ray counterpart or obvious temporal break is absent.","author_count":59,"contributors":["Yin, Yi-Han Iris","Fang, Yuan","Zhang, Bin-Bin","Deng, Chen","Yang, Jun","Chen, Run-Chao","Liu, Yuan","Cheng, Yehao","Xu, Dong","Wang, Xiaofeng","Shen, Rongfeng","Li, Rui-Zhi","Mao, Jirong","Li, Wen-Xiong","Castro-Tirado, Alberto Javier","Lei, Weihua","Fu, Shao-Yu","Yang, Yuan-Pei","Jiang, Shuai-Qing","An, Jie","Chen, Chun","Dong, Zhong-Nan","Du, Guowang","Esamdin, Ali","Fan, Zhou","Feng, Haicheng","Feng, Lu","Fernandez-Garcia, Emilio","Gao, Xing","Gritsevich, Maria","Guo, Wei-Jian","Hu, Jingwei","Hu, You-Dong","Hua, Yanlong","Iskandar, Abdusamatjan","Jin, Junjie","Li, Niu","Li, Xia","Li, Ziwei","Lin, Jia-Qi","Liu, Dezi","Liu, Jinzhong","Liu, Qichun","Liu, Xiaowei","Liu, Xing","Malesani, D.","Perez-Garcia, Ignacio","Sun, Hui","Wu, Xue-Feng","Xiao, Yun-Ao","Xiong, Ding-Rong","Yan, Shengyu","Zhang, Beibei","Zhang, Jinghua","Zhu, Haichang","Zhu, Zipei","Zou, Hu","Yuan, Weimin","Zhang, Bing"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-830253"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["China","Finland","Hong Kong","Russia","Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beijing Normal University","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Guangxi University","Huazhong University of Science and Technology","Nanjing University","Sun Yat-Sen University","The Spanish National Research Council (CSIC)","Tsinghua University","University of Helsinki","University of Hong Kong","University of Málaga","Ural Federal University","Yunnan University"],"keyword":["Absorption","Burst","Einstein probe","Emission","Evolution","Light curves","MODELS","Telescope"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"spectral hardening reveals afterglow emergence in long duration fast x ray transients a case study of grb 000000250404a ep000000250404a","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3847/2041-8213/adf552","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-830253","identifier":[{"id":"105013176099","type":"scopus"},{