{"abstract":"Obsessive–compulsive disorder (OCD) affects ~1% of children and adults and is partly caused by genetic factors. We conducted a genome-wide association study (GWAS) meta-analysis combining 53,660 OCD cases and 2,044,417 controls and identified 30 independent genome-wide significant loci. Gene-based approaches identified 249 potential effector genes for OCD, with 25 of these classified as the most likely causal candidates, including WDR6, DALRD3 and CTNND1 and multiple genes in the major histocompatibility complex (MHC) region. We estimated that ~11,500 genetic variants explained 90% of OCD genetic heritability. OCD genetic risk was associated with excitatory neurons in the hippocampus and the cortex, along with D1 and D2 type dopamine receptor-containing medium spiny neurons. OCD genetic risk was shared with 65 of 112 additional phenotypes, including all the psychiatric disorders we examined. In particular, OCD shared genetic risk with anxiety, depression, anorexia nervosa and Tourette syndrome and was negatively associated with inflammatory bowel diseases, educational attainment and body mass index.","author_count":58,"contributors":["Strom, Nora I.","Gerring, Zachary F.","Galimberti, Marco","Yu, Dongmei","Halvorsen, Matthew W.","Abdellaoui, Abdel","Rodriguez-Fontenla, Cristina","Sealock, Julia M.","Bigdeli, Tim","Coleman, Jonathan R.","Mahjani, Behrang","Thorp, Jackson G.","Bey, Katharina","Burton, Christie L.","Luykx, Jurjen J.","Zai, Gwyneth","Alemany, Silvia","Andre, Christine","Askland, Kathleen D.","Bäckman, Julia","Banaj, Nerisa","Barlassina, Cristina","Nissen, Judith Becker","Bienvenu, O. Joseph","Black, Donald","Bloch, Michael H.","Børte, Sigrid","Bosch, Rosa","Breen, Michael","Brennan, Brian P.","Brentani, Helena","Buxbaum, Joseph D.","Bybjerg-Grauholm, Jonas","Byrne, Enda M.","Cabana-Dominguez, Judit","Camarena, Beatriz","Camarena, Adrian","Cappi, Carolina","Carracedo, Angel","Casas, Miguel","Grove, Jakob","Meier, Sandra","Wang, Ying","Mortensen, Preben Bo","Stein, Dan J.","Børglum, Anders D","Hansen, Bjarne K.","Mors, Ole","Wagner, Michael","Mattheisen, Manuel"],"cuid":["S02-096.42-813853"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Africa","America, Central","America, North","America, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["23andMe Inc","Estonian Biobank"],"corresponding_author":["Mattheisen, Manuel","Strom, Nora I."],"country":["Australia","Brazil","Canada","Germany","Italy","Mexico","Netherlands","Norway","South Africa","Spain","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["(CIBERSAM) Centro de Investigación Biomédica En Red de Salud Mental","Academic Medical Centre","All Global Affiliations","Autonomous University of Barcelona","Bonn University Hospital","Broad Institute","CIBER - Center for Biomedical Research","Center for Biomedical Network Research on Rare Diseases (CIBERER)","Centre for Addiction and Mental Health","Dalhousie University","Department of Veterans Affairs","Duke University","GGNet","Harvard University","Health Research Institute of Santiago de Compostela (IDIS)","Humboldt University of Berlin","IRCCS Fondazione Santa Lucia - Roma","Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","Instituto Nacional de Psiquiatria Ramon de la Fuente","Instituto Nacional de Psiquiatría \"Ramón de la Fuente Muñiz\"","Instituto de Investigación Sanitaria de Santiago de Compostela","Instituto de Salud Carlos III","Johns Hopkins University","Karolinska Institutet","King's College London","Ludwig Maximilian University","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","Massachusetts General Hospital","Massachusetts General Hospital, Boston, Massachusetts, USA.","McLean Hospital","McMaster University","National Institute of Mental Health, Bethesda","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","Oslo University Hospital","Queensland Institute of Medical Research","SJD Barcelona Children's Hospital","SUNY Downstate Health Sciences University","SUNY Downstate Medical Center","South London and Maudsley NHS Foundation Trust","The Hospital for Sick Children","The Hospital for Sick Children, Toronto","U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs","UMC Utrecht Cancer Center","Universidade Federal de Sao Paulo","Universidade de São Paulo","University Hospital of Santiago de Compostela","University of Amsterdam","University of Bergen","University of Bern","University of Bonn","University of Cape Town","University of Illinois at Chicago","University of Iowa","University of Milan","University of North Carolina","University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill","University of Oslo","University of Queensland","University of Santiago de Compostela","University of Toronto","Utrecht University","VA Medical Center","Vall d'Hebron University Hospital","Vanderbilt University","Vita-Salute San Raffaele University","Walter and Eliza Hall Institute of Medical Research","Yale University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-LUND"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-NP-LUND","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genome wide analyses identify 000000000030 loci associated with obsessive compulsive disorder","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41588-025-02189-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.42-813853","identifier":[{"id":"105005408890","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40360802","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12165847","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-f2a4cecd-023e-4360-8dc9-91247e214116","ku-778bc7bc-d4ea-46b0-bcb2-f92331e2f1cf"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8699B79A17F1B