{"abstract":"Vegetated coastal wetlands, also called blue carbon ecosystems, are significant carbon sinks that play a vital role in global climate change mitigation. Understanding the ecological mechanisms of carbon sequestration in these ecosystems is essential to effectively manage and conserve them. This review focuses on macroecological mechanisms of carbon transfer and microecological mechanisms of carbon stabilization in vegetated coastal wetland ecosystems. Macroecological mechanisms include the horizontal and vertical carbon transport coupled to plant ecophysiology and community diversity, while microecological mechanisms include processes related to soil organic matter dynamics, such as decomposition, stabilization, and mineralization. Key scientific issues surrounding these mechanisms include transformation between carbon sink and source, stabilization mechanisms of organic carbon, and environmental effects at multiple time scales. A comprehensive research framework is also presented, which integrates spatial-temporal pattern, macroecological mechanism, microecological mechanism, and ecological engineering. Addressing these key scientific questions within the proposed framework can provide valuable insights into the significant role of biodiversity in blue carbon ecosystems, as well as significant implications for management and conservation of vegetated coastal wetlands under global climate changes.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Liu, Lele","Du, Ning","Eller, Franziska","Ye, Siyuan","Li, Xiaowen","Wei, Jifang","Guo, Yaolin","Brix, Hans","Guo, Weihua"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-805982"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Guo, Weihua"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beijing Normal University","China Geological Survey","Fudan University","Ministry of Natural Resources of the People's Republic of China","Shandong University"],"keyword":["Carbon sink","Climate change","Coastal wetland","Ecological engineering","Sea level rise"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ecological mechanisms of carbon sequestration in vegetated coastal wetland ecosystem exploring the roles of biodiversity and environmental changes","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105003758299","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-805982","identifier":[{"id":"105003758299","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-1f1b3986-80c5-4824-b364-42bd617b6163"],"keyword":["Carbon Sink","Climate Change","Coastal Wetland","Ecological Engineering","Sea Level Rise"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-1B1ACA94F8450619570805168059DE7A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"shandong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Aquatic Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"china geological survey","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China Geological Survey","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"beijing normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Beijing Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"ministry of natural resources of the people s republic of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Ministry of Natural Resources of the People's Republic of China","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"cn","key":"fudan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Fudan University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lele","key":"liulelepau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Lele","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ning","key":"duningpau","last":"Du","name":"Du, Ning","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Franziska","key":"ellerfranziskapau","last":"Eller","locid":"15509be6-9a31-4be1-9fab-9bf9db482917","name":"Eller, Franziska","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Siyuan","key":"yesiyuanpau","last":"Ye","name":"Ye, Siyuan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaowen","key":"lixiaowenpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiaowen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Jifang","key":"weijifangpau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Jifang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Yaolin","key":"guoyaolinpau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Yaolin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans","key":"brixhanspau","last":"Brix","locid":"4068bdb4-1c13-432c-b420-3991683780b5","name":"Brix, Hans","orcid":"0000-0003-2771-2983","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Weihua","key":"guoweihuapau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Weihua","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.32908/jmee.v12.2023102201","issn":["10290427","1061026X"],"issn_org":["1061026X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Marine Environmental Engineering","pages":"35-47","publisher":"Old City Publishing","status":"p","title":"Journal of Marine Environmental Engineering","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105003758299"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1f1b3986-80c5-4824-b364-42bd617b6163"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Ecological Mechanisms of Carbon Sequestration in Vegetated Coastal Wetland Ecosystem : Exploring the Roles of Biodiversity and Environmental Changes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-805982","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Ants originated over 150 million years ago through an irreversible transition to superorganismal colony life. Comparative analyses of 163 ant genomes, including newly generated whole-genome sequences of 145 ant species, reveal extensive genome rearrangements correlated with speciation rates. Meanwhile, conserved syntenic blocks are enriched with co-expressed genes involved in basal metabolism and caste differentiation. Gene families related to digestion, endocrine signaling, cuticular hydrocarbon synthesis, and chemoreception expanded in the ant ancestor, while many caste-associated genes underwent positive selection in the formicoid ancestor. Elaborations and reductions of queen-worker dimorphism and other social traits left convergent signatures of intensified or relaxed selection in conserved signaling and metabolic pathways, suggesting that a core gene set was used to diversify organizational complexity. Previously uncharacterized genetic regulators of caste development were confirmed by functional experiments. This study reconstructs the genetic underpinning of social traits and their integration within gene-regulatory networks shaping caste phenotypes.","author_count":46,"contributors":["Vizueta, Joel","Xiong, Zijun","Ding, Guo","Larsen, Rasmus S.","Ran, Hao","Gao, Qionghua","Stiller, Josefin","Dai, Wei","Jiang, Wei","Zhao, Jie","Guo, Chunxue","Zhang, Xiafang","Zuo, Dashuang","Zhong, Wenjiang","Schiøtt, Morten","Liu, Chengyuan","Zhang, Hailin","Dai, Xueqin","Andreu, Ignasi","Shi, Yue","Tretter, Sandra","He, Ding","Gautam, Shubham","Li, Zelin","Hickey, Glenn","Ivens, Aniek B.F.","Meurville, Marie-Pierre","Hita-Garcia, Francisco","Kass, Jamie M.","Guénard, Benoit","Moreau, Corrie","Paten, Benedict","LeBoeuf, Adria C.","Economo, Evan P.","Chapuisat, Michel","Shik, Jonathan Z.","Ward, Philip S.","Heinze, Jürgen","Schultz, Ted R.","Li, Qiye","Dunn, Robert R.","Sanders, Nathan J.","Liu, Weiwei","Schrader, Lukas","Boomsma, Jacobus J.","Zhang, Guojie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-827753"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["GAGA Consortium"],"corresponding_author":["Boomsma, Jacobus J.","Liu, Weiwei","Schrader, Lukas","Zhang, Guojie"],"country":["China","Germany","Hong Kong","Japan","Netherlands","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI Group","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Cornell University","Guangxi University","Max Planck Institute for Chemical Ecology","North Carolina State University","Okinawa Institute of Science and Technology Graduate University","Smithsonian Institution","The University of Hong Kong","University of California at Davis","University of California at Santa Cruz","University of Cambridge","University of Fribourg","University of Lausanne","University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","University of Münster","University of Regensburg","Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam","Zhejiang University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"adaptive radiation and social evolution of the ants","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2025.05.030","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-827753","identifier":[{"id":"40527318","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105008570750","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-887a691e-b446-45f4-ba3e-42c5bb2ce469"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-EFECC385BBBFF1CCAD070004154BE8C3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2025.05.030","version":"Published Version"},{"access":