AU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Danish Center for Health Services Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ran","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Ran","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dennis","key":"watpau","last":"Wat","name":"Wat, Dennis","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Steven Ho Man","key":"lampau","last":"Lam","name":"Lam, Steven Ho Man","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 4 5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Tommaso","key":"buccipau","last":"Bucci","name":"Bucci, Tommaso","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher Tze-Wei","key":"tsangpau","last":"Tsang","name":"Tsang, Christopher Tze-Wei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8 9","corresponding":null,"first":"An-Ping","key":"caipau","last":"Cai","name":"Cai, An-Ping","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Yap-Hang","key":"chanpau","last":"Chan","name":"Chan, Yap-Hang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qing-Wen","key":"renpau","last":"Ren","name":"Ren, Qing-Wen","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jia-Yi","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Jia-Yi","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jing-Nan","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Jing-Nan","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wen-Li","key":"gupau","last":"Gu","name":"Gu, Wen-Li","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Ching-Yan","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Ching-Yan","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Yik-Ming","key":"hungpau","last":"Hung","name":"Hung, Yik-Ming","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Freddy","key":"frostpau","last":"Frost","name":"Frost, Freddy","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 4 5 10","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregory Y. H.","key":"lippau","last":"Lip","locid":"8fa30e84-7381-41b4-8037-afc032238a3d","name":"Lip, Gregory Y H","name_org":"Lip, Gregory Y. H.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kai-Hang","key":"yiupau","last":"Yiu","name":"Yiu, Kai-Hang","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39603670"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1183/13993003.01574-2024","issn":["09031936","13993003"],"issn_org":["09031936"],"issue":"3","journal":"European Respiratory Journal","paperid":"2401574","publisher":"European Respiratory Society","status":"p","title":"European Respiratory Journal","volume":"65"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-86000757429"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3dd9f4fd-7f3c-4f4a-9f76-33f0a44431dc"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Cardiovascular Benefits and Safety Profile of Macrolide Maintenance Therapy in Patients with Bronchiectasis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-770116","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Per- and polyfluoroalkyl substances (PFAS) with stable carbon-fluorine bonds are used in a wide range of industrial and commercial applications. Due to their extreme environmental persistence, PFAS have the potential to bioaccumulate, cause adverse effects, and present challenges regarding remediation. Recently, microbial and enzymatic reactions for sustainable degradation of PFAS have gained attention from researchers, although biological decomposition of PFAS remains challenging. Surprisingly, laccases, the multi-copper oxidases produced by various organisms, showed potential for PFAS degradation. Mediators play key roles in initiating laccase induced PFAS degradation and defluorination reactions. The laccase-catalyzed PFAS degradation reactions are relatively slower than normal biocatalytic reactions and the low activity of native laccases constrains their capacity to complete defluorination. With their low redox potential and narrow substrate scope, an innovative remediation strategy must be taken to accelerate this reaction. In this review we have summarized the status, challenges, and future perspectives of enzymatic PFAS degradation. The knowledge of laccase-based defluorination and the molecular basis of the reaction mechanisms overviewed in this study could inform future applications of laccases for sustainable PFAS remediation.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Mekureyaw, Mengistu Fentahun","Junker, A","Bai, Lu","Zhang, Yan","Wei, Zongsu","Guo, Zheng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-787121"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Guo, Zheng","Wei, Zongsu"],"keyword":["Biodegradation","Defluorination","Enzymes","Laccase","Mediators","Per and polyfluoroalkyl substances PFAS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"laccase based per and polyfluoroalkyl substances degradation status and future perspectives","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.watres.2024.122888","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Aarhus University Research Foundation Starting Grant (No. AUFF-E-2019-7-28), Novo Nordisk Fonden (No. NNF20OC0064799), and Independent Research Fund Denmark Sapere Aude Award (No. 1051-00058B)."],"id":"S01-000.00-787121","identifier":[{"id":"85211069557","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39637694","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-49cb3519-98be-4886-8f37-9121d52b9141"],"keyword":["Biodegradation","Defluorination","Enzymes","Laccase","Mediators","Per- and polyfluoroalkyl substances (PFAS)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1D0AD7CECF8F06953C2D4F211DAEC4AC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.watres.2024.122888","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/419923073/1-s2.0-S0043135424017883-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Biological and Chemical Engineering, Department of Biological and Chemical Engineering - Industrial Biotechnology - Gustav Wieds Vej 10D"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mengistu Fentahun","key":"mekureyawpau","last":"Mekureyaw","locid":"c88f3a9f-b718-4bd5-82ba-60efa8f32c2c","name":"Mekureyaw, Mengistu Fentahun","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A","key":"junkerpau","last":"Junker","locid":"3a65a648-be0f-4d19-9dc5-d15aa6e62858","name":"Junker, A","orcid":"0000-0002-5712-7075","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lu","key":"baipau","last":"Bai","locid":"98807f94-3f22-46b7-b302-901f47b0b0e4","name":"Bai, Lu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yan","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"251ea212-fcf4-4249-8672-42fcf09ea051","name":"Zhang, Yan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zongsu","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","locid":"e187efc6-abcf-468f-92b6-f27824e33e91","name":"Wei, Zongsu","orcid":"0000-0001-8747-2251","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zheng","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","locid":"67372258-2bc9-4585-98c9-1b93c60d0ca9","name":"Guo, Zheng","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39637694"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.watres.2024.122888","issn":["00431354","18792448"],"issn_org":["00431354"],"journal":"Water Research","paperid":"122888","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Water Research","volume":"271"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85211069557"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-49cb3519-98be-4886-8f37-9121d52b9141"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Laccase based per- and polyfluoroalkyl substances degradation : Status and future perspectives","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-787121","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Adult zebrafish robustly regenerate injured hearts through a complex orchestration of molecular and cellular activities. However, this remarkable process, which is largely non-existent in humans, remains incompletely understood. Here, we utilize integrated spatial transcriptomics (Stereo-seq) and single-cell RNA-sequencing (scRNA-seq) to generate a spatially-resolved molecular and cellular atlas of regenerating zebrafish heart across eight stages. We characterize the cascade of cardiomyocyte cell states responsible for producing regenerated myocardium and explore a potential role for tpm4a in cardiomyocyte re-differentiation. Moreover, we uncover the activation of ifrd1 and atp6ap2 genes as a unique feature of regenerative hearts. Lastly, we reconstruct a 4D “virtual regenerating heart” comprising 569,896 cells/spots derived from 36 scRNA-seq libraries and 224 Stereo-seq slices. Our comprehensive atlas serves as a valuable resource to the cardiovascular and regeneration scientific communities and their ongoing efforts to understand the molecular and cellular mechanisms underlying vertebrate heart regeneration.","author_count":36,"contributors":["Li, Lei","Lu, Meina","Guo, Lidong","Zhang, Xuejiao","Liu, Qun","Zhang, Meiling","Gao, Junying","Xu, Mengyang","Lu, Yijian","Zhang, Fang","Li, Yao","Zhang, Ruihua","Liu, Xiawei","Pan, Shanshan","Zhang, Xianghui","Li, Zhen","Chen, Yadong","Su, Xiaoshan","Zhang, Nannan","Guo, Wenjie","Yang, Tao","Chen, Jing","Qin, Yating","Zhang, Zhe","Cui, Wei","Yu, Lindong","Gu, Ying","Yang, Huanming","Xu, Xun","Wang, Jianxun","Burns, Caroline E.","Burns, C. Geoffrey","Han, Kai","Zhao, Long","Fan, Guangyi","Su, Ying"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-809097"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","Boston Children's Hospital","Harvard University","MG