{"abstract":"Operando measurement of expansion force has become an effective way of monitoring physical-chemical events in lithium-ion batteries, of which the conventional optical means is limited by material fragility, structural incompatibility and system complexity. The utilization of flexible sensors can potentially address these challenges; however, their functionality and stability are restricted within hours in corrosive environments. Here, an in-situ unified iontronic sensing mechanism, derived from the super-capacitive electrode/electrolyte interface, is developed for expansion-force measurement in highly corrosive electrolyte environments. Specifically, it leverages the structural and material similarities between batteries and iontronic sensors to create a unified assessing device, utilizing only existing materials to produce in-situ detection. Consequently, the intelligence-incorporated architecture exhibits exceptional stability for continuous measurements over one month, enabling 400 charging/discharging cycles in a battery lifespan. Therefore, the unified iontronic sensing device, which has long-term on-board monitoring of expansion forces, offers an accurate and effective solution for the aging evaluation and safety pre-warning of lithium-ion batteries.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Chang, Yu","Cheng, Yu","Jia, Rui","Wang, Ruojiang","Xu, Qing","Gong, Lanqing","Wei, Yike","Tang, Bin","Guo, Chenhui","Sun, Bin","He, Xingmin","Li, Xueyan","Gong, Lili","Ye, Hong","Wang, Xiaoyang","Dai, Yitao","Dong, Mingdong","Tang, Yongbing","Zhang, Fan","Tan, Peng","Pan, Tingrui"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-815281"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Chang, Yu","Pan, Tingrui","Tan, Peng","Tang, Yongbing","Zhang, Fan"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Great Bay University","University of Science and Technology of China"],"keyword":["Flexible electronics","Lithium ion battery"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unified iontronic sensing for operando monitoring of physical chemical events in lithium ion batteries","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/nsr/nwaf151","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-815281","identifier":[{"id":"40444227","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105007341760","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12121480","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-18104852-3422-48b4-bea5-32e37dab37e4"],"keyword":["battery safety","flexible electronics","implanted sensor","iontronic","lithium-ion battery","operando sensing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-657B068E6C59495DF49F0E2901AEB16D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/nsr/nwaf151","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"university of science and technology of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Science and Technology of China","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"great bay university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Great Bay University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Fysik, iNANO-h