.","key":"lipgregoryyhpau","last":"Lip","locid":"8fa30e84-7381-41b4-8037-afc032238a3d","name":"Lip, Gregory Y H","name_org":"Lip, Gregory Y. H.","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Dong","key":"zhaodongpau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Dong","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jianzeng","key":"dongjianzengpau","last":"Dong","name":"Dong, Jianzeng","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Changsheng","key":"machangshengpau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Changsheng","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38146256"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/cm9.0000000000002915","issn":["03666999"],"issue":"2","journal":"Chinese Medical Journal","pages":"172-180","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Chinese Medical Journal","volume":"137"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85182926983"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b6f90d3a-08f6-4026-88bf-f39a487f844a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Oral anti-coagulants use in Chinese hospitalized patients with atrial fibrillation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-716949","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: The association of haemoglobin A1c (HbA1c) variability with the risk of adverse outcomes in patients with atrial fibrillation (AF) prescribed anticoagulants remains unclear. This study aimed to evaluate the association of HbA1c variability with the risk of ischaemic stroke (IS)/systemic embolism (SE) and all-cause mortality among patients with non-valvular AF prescribed anticoagulants. METHODS AND RESULTS: Patients newly diagnosed with AF from 2013 to 2018 were included. Variability in HbA1c, indexed by the coefficient of variation (CV), was determined for those with at least three HbA1c measurements available from the time of study enrolment to the end of follow-up. To evaluate whether prevalent diabetes would modify the relationship between HbA1c variability and outcomes, participants were divided into diabetes and non-diabetes groups. The study included 8790 patients (mean age 72.7% and 48.5% female). Over a median follow-up of 5.5 years (interquartile range 5.2, 5.8), the incident rate was 3.74 per 100 person-years for IS/SE and 4.89 for all-cause mortality in the diabetes group. The corresponding incident rates in the non-diabetes group were 2.41 and 2.42 per 100 person-years. In the diabetes group, after adjusting for covariates including mean HbA1c, greater HbA1c variability was significantly associated with increased risk of IS/SE [hazard ratio (HR) = 1.65, 95% confidence interval (CI): 1.27-2.13) and all-cause mortality (HR = 1.24, 95% CI: 1.05-1.47) compared with the lowest CV tertile. A similar pattern was evident in the non-diabetes group (IS/SE: HR = 1.58, 95% CI: 1.23-2.02; all-cause mortality: HR = 1.35, 95% CI: 1.10-1.64). CONCLUSION: Greater HbA1c variability was independently associated with increased risk of IS/SE and all-cause mortality among patients with AF, regardless of diabetic status.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Huang, Jia-Yi","Cai, An-Ping","Tsang, Christopher Tze Wei","Wu, Mei-Zhen","Gu, Wen-Li","Guo, Ran","Zhang, Jing-Nan","Zhu, Ching-Yan","Hung, Yik-Ming","Lip, Gregory Y H","Yiu, Kai-Hang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-756620"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Yiu, Kai-Hang"],"country":["China","Hong Kong","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Guangdong Provincial People's Hospital","Liverpool Centre for Cardiovascular Science","Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","Queen Mary Hospital","Southern Medical University","The University of Hong Kong","The University of Hong Kong-Shenzhen Hospital","University of Liverpool"],"keyword":["Adverse events","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Anticoagulants therapeutic use","Atrial Fibrillation drug therapy","Atrial fibrillation","Biomarkers blood","Blood Glucose metabolism","Cause of Death trends","Diabetes Mellitus blood","Female","Glycated Hemoglobin metabolism","Humans","Incidence","Ischemic Stroke mortality","Male","Middle Aged","Retrospective Studies","Risk Assessment","Risk Factors","Time Factors","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the association of haemoglobin a000000000001c variability with adverse outcomes in patients with atrial fibrillation prescribed anticoagulants","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85213389890&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The current study was performed in Queen Mary Hospital, Hong Kong. This study was supported by the Sanming Project of Medicine in Shenzhen, China (No. SZSM201911020) and supported by the HKU-SZH Fund for Shenzhen Key Medical Discipline (No. SZXK2020081)."],"id":"S01-000.00-756620","identifier":[{"id":"39140113","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85213389890","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-3dc9594d-b72a-4078-b494-881c7b5f017e"],"keyword":["Adverse events","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Anticoagulants/therapeutic use","Atrial Fibrillation/drug therapy","Atrial fibrillation","Biomarkers/blood","Blood Glucose/metabolism","Cause of Death/trends","Diabetes Mellitus/blood","Female","Glycated Hemoglobin/metabolism","Haemoglobin A1c variability","Humans","Incidence","Ischemic Stroke/mortality","Male","Middle Aged","Retrospective Studies","Risk Assessment","Risk Factors","Time Factors","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9EC0EAED450C8B9071741E8FDD6165C5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"the university of hong kong shenzhen hospital","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"The University of Hong Kong-Shenzhen Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"hk","key":"queen mary hospital","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"Queen Mary Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"southern medical university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southern Medical University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"guangdong provincial people s hospital","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Guangdong Provincial People's Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"hk","key":"the university of hong kong","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"The University of Hong Kong","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"gb","key":"liverpool centre for cardiovascular science","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Liverpool Centre for Cardiovascular Science","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"gb","key":"university of liverpool","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Liverpool","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"gb","key":"liverpool heart and chest hospital nhs foundation trust","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jia-Yi","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Jia-Yi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"An-Ping","key":"caipau","last":"Cai","name":"Cai, An-Ping","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher Tze Wei","key":"tsangpau","last":"Tsang","name":"Tsang, Christopher Tze Wei","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mei-Zhen","key":"wupau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Mei-Zhen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wen-Li","key":"gupau","last":"Gu","name":"Gu, Wen-Li","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ran","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Ran","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jing-Nan","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Jing-Nan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ching-Yan","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Ching-Yan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yik-Ming","key":"hungpau","last":"Hung","name":"Hung, Yik-Ming","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 7 8 9","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregory Y. H.","key":"lippau","last":"Lip","locid":"8fa30e84-7381-41b4-8037-afc032238a3d","name":"Lip, Gregory Y H","name_org":"Lip, Gregory Y. H.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kai-Hang","key":"yiupau","last":"Yiu","name":"Yiu, Kai-Hang","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39140113"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/eurjpc/zwae249","issn":["20474873","20474881"],"issn_org":["20474873"],"issue":"18","journal":"European Journal of Preventive Cardiology","pages":"2073-2083","paperid":"zwae249","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Preventive Cardiology","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85213389890"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3dc9594d-b72a-4078-b494-881c7b5f017e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The association of haemoglobin A1c variability with adverse outcomes in patients with atrial fibrillation prescribed anticoagulants","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-756620","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Intestinal stem cells (ISCs) initiate intestinal epithelial regeneration and tumorigenesis, and they experience rapid refilling upon various injuries for epithelial repair as well as tumor reoccurrence. It is crucial to reveal the mechanism underlying such plasticity for intestinal health. Recent studies have found that metabolic pathways control stem cell fate in homeostasis, but the role of metabolism in the regeneration of ISCs after damage has not been clarified. Here, we find that in a human colorectal cancer dataset, miR-29a and b (miR-29a/b) are metabolic regulators highly associated with intestinal tumorigenesis and worse prognostic value of radiotherapy. We also show that these two microRNAs are required for intestinal stemness maintenance in mice, and their expression is induced in regenerated ISCs after irradiation injury, resulting in skewed ISC fate from differentiation towards self-renewal. This upregulation of miR-29a/b expression in ISCs leads to suppression of fatty acid oxidation (FAO) and depression of oxidative phosphorylation, which in turn controls the balance between self-renewal and differentiation of ISCs. Deletion of miR-29a/b prevents these effects and thus impairs ISC-mediated epithelial recovery. Finally, we filter the potential targets of miR-29a/b and identify Hnf4g, a transcription factor, that drives this metabolic reprogramming through regulating FAO-related enzymes. Our work discovers an important metabolic mechanism of ISC-mediated regeneration and potentially pave the way for more targeted and effective therapeutic strategies for intestinal repair as well as tumor treatment.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Lin, Yingying","Lu, Yao","Wang, Yuqi","Lv, Cong","Chen, Juan","Luo, Yongting","Quan, Heng","Yu, Weiru","Chen, Lining","Huang, Ziyu","Hao, Yanling","Wang, Qingyu","Luo, Qingfeng","Yan, Jingyu","Li, Yixuan","Zhang, Wei","Du, Min","He, Jian","Ren, Fazheng","Guo, Huiyuan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-772674"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Guo, Huiyuan"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Dalian Institute of Chemical Physics","CAS - Institute of Biophysics","Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences","Food Lab Zhongyuan","National Center of Technology Innovation for Dairy","Washington State University Pullman","Washington University St. Louis"],"keyword":["Fatty acid oxidation","Intestinal stem cells","Mitochondrial oxidative phosphorylation","Regeneration"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the regeneration of intestinal stem cells is driven by mir 000000000029 induced metabolic reprogramming","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eng.2024.08.008","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-772674","identifier":[{"id":"85206628542","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-6d6cd82b-22e0-4b9f-aefa-c8272077f6b2"],"keyword":["Fatty acid oxidation","Hnf4g","Intestinal stem cells","MiR-29a/b","Mitochondrial oxidative phosphorylation","Regeneration"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-80B254CC91E6962585CB0207F3ECC51E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eng.2024.08.008","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"national center of technology innovation for dairy","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"National Center of Technology Innovation for Dairy","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"cas institute of biophysics","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Institute of Biophysics","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"food lab zhongyuan","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Food Lab Zhongyuan","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Food Science, Department of Food Science - Differentiated & Biofunctional Foods"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of medical sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"cn","key":"cas dalian institute of chemical physics","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Dalian Institute of Chemical Physics","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"us","key":"washington university st louis","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Washington University St. Louis","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"us","key":"washington state university pullman","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Washington State University Pullman","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yingying","key":"linyingyingpau","last":"Lin","name":"Lin, Yingying","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yao","key":"luyaopau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Yao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuqi","key":"wangyuqipau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Yuqi","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cong","key":"lvcongpau","last":"Lv","name":"Lv, Cong","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan","key":"chenjuanpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Juan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yongting","key":"luoyongtingpau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Yongting","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Heng","key":"quanhengpau","last":"Quan","name":"Quan, Heng","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Weiru","key":"yuweirupau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Weiru","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lining","key":"chenliningpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Lining","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ziyu","key":"huangziyupau","last":"Huang","locid":"4a8d5a33-11fc-49e8-b605-9e63b49f3cd7","name":"Huang, Ziyu","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yanling","key":"haoyanlingpau","last":"Hao","name":"Hao, Yanling","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Qingyu","key":"wangqingyupau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Qingyu","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Qingfeng","key":"luoqingfengpau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Qingfeng","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Jingyu","key":"yanjingyupau","last":"Yan","name":"Yan, Jingyu","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yixuan","key":"liyixuanpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yixuan","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"zhangweipau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Wei","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Min","key":"duminpau","last":"Du","name":"Du, Min","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jian","key":"hejianpau","last":"He","name":"He, Jian","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Fazheng","key":"renfazhengpau","last":"Ren","name":"Ren, Fazheng","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Huiyuan","key":"guohuiyuanpau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Huiyuan","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.eng.2024.08.008","issn":["10091742","20958099"],"issn_org":["20958099"],"journal":"Engineering","pages":"39-58","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Engineering","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206628542"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6d6cd82b-22e0-4b9f-aefa-c8272077f6b2"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The Regeneration of Intestinal Stem Cells Is Driven by miR-29-Induced Metabolic Reprogramming","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-772674","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: With the implementation of the 11th edition of the International Classification of Diseases (ICD-11) and the publication of the metabolic dysfunction-associated fatty liver disease (MAFLD) nomenclature in 2020, it is important to establish consensus for the coding of MAFLD in ICD-11. This will inform subsequent revisions of ICD-11. Methods: Using the Qualtrics XM and WJX platforms, questionnaires were sent online to MAFLD-ICD-11 coding collaborators, authors of papers, and relevant association members. Results: A total of 890 international experts in various fields from 61 countries responded to the survey. We also achieved full coverage of provincial-level administrative regions in China. 77.1% of respondents agreed that MAFLD should be represented in ICD-11 by updating NAFLD, with no significant regional differences (77.3% in Asia and 76.6% in non-Asia, p = 0.819). Over 80% of respondents agreed or somewhat agreed with the need to assign specific codes for progressive stages of MAFLD (i.e. steatohepatitis) (92.2%), MAFLD combined with comorbidities (84.1%), or MAFLD subtypes (i.e., lean, overweight/obese, and diabetic) (86.1%). Conclusions: This global survey by a collaborative panel of clinical, coding, health management and policy experts, indicates agreement that MAFLD should be coded in ICD-11. The data serves as a foundation for corresponding adjustments in the ICD-11 revision.","author_count":95,"contributors":["Zhang, Huai","Targher, Giovanni","Byrne, Christopher D","Kim, Seung Up","Wong, Vincent Wai-Sun","Valenti, Luca","Glickman, Myer","Ponce, Jaime","Mantzoros, Christos S","Crespo, Javier","Gronbaek, Henning","Yang, Wah","Eslam, Mohammed","Wong, Robert J","Machado, Mariana Verdelho","Yu, Ming-Lung","Ghanem, Omar M","Okanoue, Takeshi","Liu, Jun-Feng","Lee, Yong-Ho","Xu, Xiao-Yuan","Pan, Qiuwei","Sui, Meili","Lonardo, Amedeo","Yilmaz, Yusuf","Zhu, Li-Yong","Moreno, Christophe","Miele, Luca","Lupsor-Platon, Monica","Zhao, Lei","LaMa