{"abstract":"The problem of common-mode voltage (CMV) in current source converter (CSC) has been concerned with the development and application of CSC, such as in the transformerless motor drive system. Using a common-mode (CM) choke is a popular solution to suppressing CMV. The high-frequency harmonics of the CMV can be eliminated by the CM filter. However, the low-order harmonics cannot be eliminated effectively, especially at low modulation index, which may cause CM resonance and increase the size of the choke. In this article, a novel virtual space vector modulation method is proposed, which constructs virtual space vectors by the original vectors. The average value of the CMV produced by each virtual vector is zero. The proposed method can reduce the amplitude and third-order harmonic component of the CMV. In addition, the number of switching transitions in a switching sequence of the proposed method is the same as the conventional five-segment space vector modulation. The suppression effects of different methods on the low-order harmonics of CMV are compared through simulation and experiments, and the effectiveness of the proposed methods is verified.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Wei, Yupeng","Diao, Naizhe","Guo, Xiaoqiang","Hua, Changchun","Blaabjerg, Frede"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-717108"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Yanshan University"],"keyword":["Common mode voltage CMV","Current source converter CSC","Space vector modulation SVM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a novel common mode voltage suppression strategy for current source converter","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85151554595&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported in part by the National Key Research and Development Program of China under Grant 2022YFE0102500, in part by the National Natural Science Foundation of China under Grant 52077190 and Grant 52277202, in part by the Central for Local Science and Technology Development Program under Grant 226Z4504G, in part by the Hebei Province Natural Science Foundation under Grant F2020203013, and in part by the Science and Technology Project of Hebei Education De- partment under Grant QN2023151."],"id":"S01-000.00-717108","identifier":[{"id":"85151554595","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-fa9f2b1b-d92b-466a-aec2-bb1ab676a07a"],"keyword":["Common-mode voltage (CMV)","current source converter (CSC)","space vector modulation (SVM)","third-order component","virtual space vector"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A68A2EA4287708D628DB10BDAA549889"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"yanshan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Yanshan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Applied Power Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, E-Mobility and Drives","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, EMI/EMC in Power Electronics","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Photovoltaic Systems","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Control, Reliability and System Optimization","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Wind Power Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yupeng","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Yupeng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Naizhe","key":"diaopau","last":"Diao","name":"Diao, Naizhe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoqiang","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Xiaoqiang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Changchun","key":"huapau","last":"Hua","name":"Hua, Changchun","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frede","key":"blaabjergpau","last":"Blaabjerg","locid":"22b09e36-1f7b-4d33-90bf-918730e1d09a","name":"Blaabjerg, Frede","orcid":"0000-0001-8311-7412","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tie.2023.3257367","issn":["02780046","15579948"],"issn_org":["02780046"],"issue":"2","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Industrial Electronics","pages":"1104-1112","publisher":"IEEE Industrial Electronics Society","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Industrial Electronics","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Industrial Electronics","volume":"71"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85151554595"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-fa9f2b1b-d92b-466a-aec2-bb1ab676a07a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A Novel Common-Mode Voltage Suppression Strategy for Current Source Converter","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-717108","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"We construct non-linear machine learning (ML) prediction models for systolic and diastolic blood pressure (SBP, DBP) using demographic and clinical variables and polygenic risk scores (PRSs). We developed a two-model ensemble, consisting of a baseline model, where prediction is based on demographic and clinical variables only, and a genetic model, where we also include PRSs. We evaluate the use of a linear versus a non-linear model at both the baseline and the genetic model levels and assess the improvement in performance when incorporating multiple PRSs. We report the ensemble model’s performance as percentage variance explained (PVE) on a held-out test dataset. A non-linear baseline model improved the PVEs from 28.1 to 30.1% (SBP) and 14.3% to 17.4% (DBP) compared with a linear baseline model. Including seven PRSs in the genetic model computed based on the largest available GWAS of SBP/DBP improved the genetic model PVE from 4.8 to 5.1% (SBP) and 4.7 to 5% (DBP) compared to using a single PRS. Adding additional 14 PRSs computed based on two independent GWASs further increased the genetic model PVE to 6.3% (SBP) and 5.7% (DBP). PVE differed across self-reported race/ethnicity groups, with primarily all non-White groups benefitting from the inclusion of additional PRSs. In summary, non-linear ML models improves BP prediction in models incorporating diverse populations.","author_count":37,"contributors":["Hrytsenko, Yana","Shea, Benjamin","Elgart, Michael","Kurniansyah, Nuzulul","Lyons, Genevieve","Morrison, Alanna C.","Carson, April P.","Haring, Bernhard","Mitchell, Braxton D.","Psaty, Bruce M.","Jaeger, Byron C.","Gu, C. Charles","Kooperberg, Charles","Levy, Daniel","Lloyd-Jones, Donald","Choi, Eunhee","Brody, Jennifer A.","Smith, Jennifer A.","Rotter, Jerome I.","Moll, Matthew","Fornage, Myriam","Simon, Noah","Castaldi, Peter","Casanova, Ramon","Chung, Ren Hua","Kaplan, Robert","Loos, Ruth J.F.","Kardia, Sharon L.R.","Rich, Stephen S.","Redline, Susan","Kelly, Tanika","O’Connor, Timothy","Zhao, Wei","Kim, Wonji","Guo, Xiuqing","Ida Chen, Yii Der","Sofer, Tamar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747809"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Taiwan","United States"],"glorg":["Albert Einstein College of Medicine","All Global Affiliations","Beth Israel Deaconess Medical Center","Columbia University","Department of Veterans Affairs","Framingham Heart Study, National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute (NHLBI)","Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center","Harvard T.H. Chan School of Public Health","Harvard University","Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","National Health Research Institutes Taiwan","Northwestern University","Saarland University","Tulane University","University of California at Los Angeles","University of Maryland, Baltimore","University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","University of Mississippi","University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston","University of Virginia","University of Washington","Wake Forest University","Washington University St. Louis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"machine learning models for predicting blood pressure phenotypes by combining multiple polygenic risk scores","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-024-62945-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747809","identifier":[{"id":"85194998457","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38816422","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11139858","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-3663caab-3722-46a2-bb06-006db806bd91"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CE5012599