{"abstract":"Biochar’s underlying biochemical and physiological mechanisms in reducing irrigation and salinity stress are elusive. This paper investigates the effects of two types of biochar (wood biochar and poultry biochar) on the growth and physiology of tomato seedlings exposed to the combined effects of drought and salinity stress. Two types of biochar, wood biochar (WB) and poultry biochar (PB), were added to the soil separately, with three salinity gradients of 0, 100, and 200 mmol/L and two water supply conditions of full irrigation (FI) and deficit irrigation (DI). Results showed that biochar addition effectively improved the root water potential and osmotic potential of tomato plant under drought and salinity stress. Biochar application also mitigated leaf relative water content by 9.86% and 24.37% under drought and salinity stress, respectively. Furthermore, biochar application decreased abscisic acid concentrations in xylem sap under drought and salinity stress. Biochar altered the soil structure and increased field water holding capacity, indirectly increasing the soil water supply. While water use efficiency did not increase significantly after biochar application, a synergistic increase in seedling growth and water consumption occurred. In conclusion, biochar addition shows promise for promoting seedling growth to help mitigate the adverse impacts of drought and salinity stress on plant growth and physiology.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Zhang, Wenqian","Wei, Jiahua","Guo, Lili","Fang, Heng","Liu, Xiaojuan","Liang, Kehao","Niu, Wenquan","Liu, Fulai","Siddique, Kadambot H.M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-670584"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Anhui Agricultural University","Huazhong Agricultural University","Northwest A&F University","Northwest University","Sichuan Agricultural University","Tsinghua University","University of Western Australia"],"keyword":["ABA","Biochar","Photosynthesis","Water use efficiency WUE"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of two biochar types on mitigating drought and salt stress in tomato seedlings","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/agronomy13041039","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-670584","identifier":[{"id":"000979541500001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85154056678","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8f9818cd-0d1b-4360-ae05-4a2fb8ff4bff"],"keyword":["ABA","biochar","photosynthesis","water relationship","water use efficiency (WUE)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2596F888295723B20A133C30C27F4045"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/agronomy13041039","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/346535979/agronomy_13_01039.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"northwest a f university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northwest A&F University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"tsinghua university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tsinghua University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"huazhong agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Huazhong Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"anhui agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Anhui Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"cn","key":"sichuan agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sichuan Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"cn","key":"northwest university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northwest University","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"au","key":"university of western australia","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Western Australia","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Wenqian","key":"zhangwenqianpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Wenqian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jiahua","key":"weijiahuapau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Jiahua","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Lili","key":"guolilipau","last":"Guo","locid":"14e25841-05c0-41d4-baf4-1bc0cdc362f1","name":"Guo, Lili","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 3","first":"Heng","key":"fanghengpau","last":"Fang","name":"Fang, Heng","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 6","first":"Xiaojuan","key":"liuxiaojuanpau","last":"Liu","locid":"07bdefa7-8463-4a5a-9f33-fe41da5e8ee0","name":"Liu, Xiaojuan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Kehao","key":"liangkehaopau","last":"Liang","locid":"53b1a13e-2d53-433a-a644-bf6bd7b0460b","name":"Liang, Kehao","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","first":"Wenquan","key":"niuwenquanpau","last":"Niu","name":"Niu, Wenquan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Fulai","key":"liufulaipau","last":"Liu","locid":"dc299ce8-5a4c-46f4-9af0-4d935f7cf190","name":"Liu, Fulai","orcid":"0000-0002-5006-8965","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Kadambot H.M.","key":"siddiquekadambothmpau","last":"Siddique","name":"Siddique, Kadambot H.M.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/agronomy13041039","issn":["20734395"],"issue":"4","journal":"Agronomy","paperid":"1039","status":"p","title":"Agronomy","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85154056678"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8f9818cd-0d1b-4360-ae05-4a2fb8ff4bff"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effects of Two Biochar Types on Mitigating Drought and Salt Stress in Tomato Seedlings","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-670584","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Most variations in the human genome refer to single-nucleotide variation (SNV), small fragment insertions and deletions, and genomic copy number variation (CNV). Many human diseases including genetic disorders are associated with variations in the genome. These disorders are often difficult to be diagnosed because of their complex clinical conditions, therefore, an effective detection method is needed to facilitate clinical diagnosis and prevent birth defects. With the development of high-throughput sequencing technology, the method of targeted sequence capture chip has been extensively used owing to its high throughput, high accuracy, fast speed, and low cost. In this study, we designed a chip that potentially captured the coding region of 3043 genes associated with 4013 monogenic diseases, with an addition of 148 chromosomal abnormalities that can be identified by targeting specific regions. To assess the efficiency, a strategy of combining the BGISEQ500 sequencing platform with the designed chip was utilized to screen variants in 63 patients. Eventually, 67 disease-associated variants were found, 31 of which were novel. The results of the evaluation test also show that this combined strategy complies with the requirements of clinical testing and has proper clinical application value. Genetic testing: One-step targeted sequencing helps diagnose genetic disordersA new DNA screening method potentially offers a one-step solution to the challenge of diagnosing genetic diseases. A team from China led by Xiaoming Wei from BGI Genomics in Shenzhen and Yang Wan from the Fuyang People's Hospital has designed a DNA chip that captures the coding regions of 4,013 disease-causing genes plus another 148 common chromosomal abnormalities. The targeted next-generation sequencing strategy can detect a variety of genomic alterations including single-letter mutations as well as chromosomal abnormalities including insertions, deletions and duplications of larger pieces of DNA. The researchers ran the test on blood samples from 63 patients with genetic disorders. In 52 of these individuals, they found a total of 67 different disease-related variants, including 31 novel variants, demonstrating the clinical utility of the approach.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Liu, Yanqiu","Mao, Liangwei","Huang, Hui","Li, Wei","Man, Jianfen","Zhang, Wenqian","Wang, Lina","Li, Long","Sun, Yan","Zhai, Teng","Guo, Xueqin","Du, Lique","Huang, Jin","Li, Hao","Wan, Yang","Wei, Xiaoming"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-677668"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","Fuyang People’s Hospital","Hubei University","Jiangxi Maternal and Child Health Hospital"],"keyword":["American college","Disease","Exome","Framework","Medical Genetics","UPDATE"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"clinical diagnosis of genetic disorders at both single nucleotide and chromosomal levels based on bgiseq 000000000500 platform","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41439-023-00238-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-677668","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10203365","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000991662600001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85160042357","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37217505","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1c8475b2-5a48-4937-9e88-09a698efd6e2"],"keyword":["AMERICAN-COLLEGE","DISEASE","EXOME","FRAMEWORK","MEDICAL GENETICS","UPDATE"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-2F125D3C687BC0BB0A231984E4DA436C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/347885165/s41439_023_00238_9.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41439-023-00238-9","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"jiangxi maternal and child health hospital","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jiangxi Maternal and Child Health Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"hubei university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hubei University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"bgi","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Computational and RNA Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"fuyang people s hospital","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Fuyang People’s Hospital","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Yanqiu","key":"liuyanqiupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Yanqiu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Liangwei","key":"maoliangweipau","last":"Mao","name":"Mao, Liangwei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Hui","key":"huanghuipau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Hui","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Wei","key":"liweipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Wei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jianfen","key":"manjianfenpau","last":"Man","name":"Man, Jianfen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Wenqian","key":"zhangwenqianpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"e8c2655e-e683-4eb0-b325-6e8f56fc3544","name":"Zhang, Wenqian","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Lina","key":"wanglinapau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Lina","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Long","key":"li