":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Gregg C.","key":"fonarowgreggcpau","last":"Fonarow","name":"Fonarow, Gregg C.","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Sidney C.","key":"smithsidneycpau","last":"Smith","name":"Smith, Sidney C.","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 7 8","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregory Y. H.","key":"lipgregoryyhpau","last":"Lip","locid":"8fa30e84-7381-41b4-8037-afc032238a3d","name":"Lip, Gregory Y H","name_org":"Lip, Gregory Y. H.","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Dong","key":"zhaodongpau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Dong","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jian-Zeng","key":"dongjianzengpau","last":"Dong","name":"Dong, Jian-Zeng","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Chang-Sheng","key":"machangshengpau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Chang-Sheng","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37712716"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/europace/euad272","issn":["10995129","10996044"],"issn_org":["10995129"],"issue":"10","journal":"Europace","paperid":"euad272","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Europace","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85173567117"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-da00d5d0-8921-430b-9c25-db58fcb49d5b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Asymptomatic Atrial Fibrillation among Hospitalized Patients : clinical correlates and in-hospital outcomes in Improving Care for Cardiovascular Disease in China-Atrial Fibrillation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-693071","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"With the rapid increase in the installed capacity of wind power, day-ahead wind power interval prediction is becoming more and more important. To solve such a challenging problem and provide intervals of higher quality, this paper proposes a prediction method based on conformal asymmetric multi-quantile generative transformer. Herein, the multi-quantile generative transformer is a deep learning model that generates multi-quantile forecast results for next day through one forward propagation process. Then, two quantiles, whose width is the smallest while satisfying the nominal confidence constraint, are selected from the predicted sequence as the upper bound and lower bound of the asymmetric interval. Furthermore, we introduce the conformal quantile regression to calibrate the bounds of the prediction interval to ensure that its coverage rate is as close as nominal confidence. The experiments show that the proposed method surpasses the benchmarks by providing narrower prediction intervals with more accurate empirical coverage probability. Under nominal confidence 90%, it gives prediction intervals with average empirical coverage probability of 90.50% and normalized average width of 0.44 on four wind farms. Compared with symmetric prediction intervals given by common benchmark quantile long short term memory network, the average width is reduced by 19.6%.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Wang, Wei","Feng, Bin","Huang, Gang","Guo, Chuangxin","Liao, Wenlong","Chen, Zhe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-756872"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Feng, Bin"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Zhejiang Lab","Zhejiang University"],"keyword":["Interval prediction","Wind power"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"conformal asymmetric multi quantile generative transformer for day ahead wind power interval prediction","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85146073941&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-756872","identifier":[{"id":"85146073941","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-7444858d-4292-4bca-9420-0f83f2a7873a"],"keyword":["Asymmetric interval","Conformal quantile","Generative transformer","Interval prediction","Wind power"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8528BE886319E905442EFCA089E878C4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang lab","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang Lab","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Electric Power Systems and Microgrids","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Intelligent Energy Systems and Flexible Markets"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Wei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bin","key":"fengpau","last":"Feng","name":"Feng, Bin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gang","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Gang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chuangxin","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Chuangxin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenlong","key":"liaopau","last":"Liao","locid":"7cf3bc06-b490-4dfa-a4ef-70f1a9fae3a2","name":"Liao, Wenlong","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zhe","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","locid":"d823b80a-ad7f-4339-b75a-8dee8403f02a","name":"Chen, Zhe","orcid":"0000-0002-2919-4481","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.apenergy.2022.120634","issn":["03062619","18729118"],"issn_org":["03062619"],"journal":"Applied Energy","paperid":"120634","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Applied Energy","volume":"333"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146073941"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7444858d-4292-4bca-9420-0f83f2a7873a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Conformal asymmetric multi-quantile generative transformer for day-ahead wind power interval prediction","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-756872","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Suicidal behavior is heritable and is a major cause of death worldwide. Two large-scale genome-wide association studies (GWASs) recently discovered and crossvalidated genome-wide significant (GWS) loci for suicide attempt (SA). The present study leveraged the genetic cohorts from both studies to conduct the largest GWAS metaanalysis of SA to date. Multi-ancestry and admixture-specific meta-analyses were conducted within groups of significant African, East Asian, and European ancestry admixtures. Methods: This study comprised 22 cohorts, including 43,871 SA cases and 915,025 ancestry-matched controls. Analytical methods across multi-ancestry and individual ancestry admixtures included inverse variance-weighted fixed-effects meta-analyses, followed by gene, gene-set, tissue-set, and drug-target enrichment, as well as summary-data-based Mendelian randomization with brain expression quantitative trait loci data, phenome-wide genetic correlation, and genetic causal proportion analyses. Results: Multi-ancestry and European ancestry admixture GWAS meta-analyses identified 12 risk loci at p values <5×10-8. These loci were mostly intergenic and implicated DRD2, SLC6A9, FURIN, NLGN1, SOX5, PDE4B, and CACNG2. The multi-ancestry SNP-based heritability estimate of SA was 5.7% on the liability scale (SE=0.003, p=5.7×10-80). Significant brain tissue gene expression and drug set enrichment were observed. There was shared genetic variation of SA with attention deficit hyperactivity disorder, smoking, and risk tolerance after conditioning SA on both major depressive disorder and posttraumatic stress disorder. Genetic causal proportion analyses implicated shared genetic risk for specific health factors. Conclusions: This multi-ancestry analysis of suicide attempt identified several loci contributing to risk and establishes significant shared genetic covariation with clinical phenotypes. These findings provide insight into genetic factors associated with suicide