{"abstract":"Polarity inversion from the bioanode to the biocathode enables a rapid formation of efficient biofilms for microbial electrochemical reduction. Though this approach has been widely adopted for various applications, the mechanism behind the enhanced extracellular electron transfer (EET) during the polarity inversion process remains unclear. Therefore, in this study, the succession pattern and electron transfer mechanism of the inverted denitrifying biocathode were investigated by continuously monitoring the electrochemical properties, denitrification dynamics, and biofilm characteristics. The results indicated that the highest current density of the biocathode after inversion from bioanode was twice that of the steady current density, and the dominant flora of the electrode biofilm shifted from Geobacter sp. to denitrifying bacteria (e.g., Shinella and Comamonas). The reversal polarity induced a decreasing content of cytochrome C, while iron-containing compounds were found to be responsible for an enhanced EET within the denitrification process. This study provides a deep understanding of the EET mechanism behind the electrode polarity inversion and is of great significance for the future development of biocathode applications.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Feng, Huajun","Guo, Wei","Ying, Xianbin","Ma, Xiangjuan","Jin, Anan","Hong, Zhicheng","Ding, Yangcheng","Zhao, Nannan","Zhang, Yifeng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-359262"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Zhang, Yifeng","Zhao, Nannan"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Zhejiang Gongshang University"],"keyword":["Biocathode","Denitrification","Microbial community","Polarity inversion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unveiling the mechanism of enhanced extracellular electron transfer by polarity inversion of bioelectrodes","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/302752011/acs_2_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-359262","identifier":[{"id":"85145598415","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-b6fe5999-4bae-4518-aac7-5d0449be32e2"],"keyword":["Biocathode","Denitrification","Electron transfer mechanism","Microbial community","Polarity inversion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5CED62DEA18B1A14AB4C20089C88FF69"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/302752011/acs_2_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang gongshang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang Gongshang University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental and Resource Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental and Resource Engineering, Water Technology & Processes"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Huajun","key":"fengpau","last":"Feng","name":"Feng, Huajun","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Wei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xianbin","key":"yingpau","last":"Ying","name":"Ying, Xianbin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiangjuan","key":"mapau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Xiangjuan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anan","key":"jinpau","last":"Jin","name":"Jin, Anan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhicheng","key":"hongpau","last":"Hong","name":"Hong, Zhicheng","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yangcheng","key":"dingpau","last":"Ding","name":"Ding, Yangcheng","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nannan","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Nannan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yifeng","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"ce49a7e7-7f82-427b-babf-27d0549e1f8f","name":"Zhang, Yifeng","orcid":"0000-0002-2832-2277","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acsestwater.2c00463","issn":["26900637"],"issue":"1","journal":"ACS ES and T Water","pages":"156-165","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"ACS ES and T Water","title_org":"ACS EST Water","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85145598415"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-b6fe5999-4bae-4518-aac7-5d0449be32e2"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Unveiling the Mechanism of Enhanced Extracellular Electron Transfer by Polarity Inversion of Bioelectrodes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-359262","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This study aimed to prepare single-component LNPs with sugar alcohol fatty acid monoesters for temperature-controlled release. In total, 20 kinds of lipids with a series of sugar alcohol head groups (ethylene glycol, glycerol, erythritol, xylitol and sorbitol) and fatty acyl tails (12:0, 14:0, 16:0 and 18:0) were synthesised via lipase-catalysed esterification. Their physicochemical properties and upper/lower critical solution temperature (LCST/USCT) were analysed. Two groups of mixed lipids, 78 % ethylene glycol lauric acid monoester + 22 % sorbitol stearic acid monoester (LNP-1) and 90 % ethylene glycol lauric acid monoester + 10 % xylitol myristic acid monoester (LNP-2), had LCST/USCT of approximately 37 °C, which formed empty LNPs using the emulsification−diffusion method. These two mixed lipids were prepared for LNPs loaded with curcumin, showing high encapsulation (>90 %), mean particle sizes of approximately 250 nm and low polydispersity index (≤0.2). These lipids have the potential for tailor-made LNPs achieving thermo-responsivity in delivering bioactive agents and drugs.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Ye, Shengyuan","Cheng, Yang","Guo, Zheng","Wang, Xingguo","Wei, Wei"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-675340"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Wei, Wei"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Jiangnan University"],"keyword":["Curcumin","Lipid nanoparticle","Release"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a lipid toolbox of sugar alcohol fatty acid monoesters for single component lipid nanoparticles with temperature controlled release","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.colsurfb.2023.113426","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-675340","identifier":[{"id":"85163863954","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37399694","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-90456b52-3b9f-4a61-aace-3cb844e2aae2"],"keyword":["Critical dissolution temperature","Curcumin","Lipid nanoparticle","Release","Sugar alcohol fatty acid ester"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-24FCB830A5D401E314CC590F1A74EB04"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.colsurfb.2023.113426","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"jiangnan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jiangnan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Biological and Chemical Engineering, Department of Biological and Chemical Engineering - Industrial Biotechnology - Gustav Wieds Vej 10D"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shengyuan","key":"yepau","last":"Ye","name":"Ye, Shengyuan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yang","key":"chengpau","last":"Cheng","name":"Cheng, Yang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zheng","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","locid":"67372258-2bc9-4585-98c9-1b93c60d0ca9","name":"Guo, Zheng","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xingguo","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Xingguo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Wei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37399694"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.colsurfb.2023.113426","issn":["09277765","18734367"],"issn_org":["09277765"],"journal":"Colloids and Surfaces B: Biointerfaces","paperid":"113426","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Colloids and Surfaces B: Biointerfaces","volume":"228"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85163863954"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-90456b52-3b9f-4a61-aace-3cb844e2aae2"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A Lipid Toolbox of Sugar Alcohol Fatty Acid Monoesters for Single-component Lipid Nanoparticles with Temperature-controlled Release","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-675340","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: Blood eosinophil count and eosinophil cationic protein (ECP) concentration are risk factors of cardiovascular diseases. This study tested whether and how eosinophils and ECP contribute to vascular calcification and atherogenesis. METHODS AND RESULTS: Immunostaining revealed eosinophil accumulation in human and mouse atherosclerotic lesions. Eosinophil deficiency in ΔdblGATA mice slowed atherogenesis with increased lesion smooth muscle cell (SMC) content and reduced calcification. This protection in ΔdblGATA mice was muted when mice received donor eosinophils from wild-type (WT), Il4-/-, and Il13-/- mice or mouse eosinophil-associated-ribonuclease-1 (mEar1), a murine homologue of ECP. Eosinophils or mEar1 but not interleukin (IL) 4 or IL13 increased the calcification of SMC from WT mice but not those from Runt-related transcription factor-2 (Runx2) knockout mice. Immunoblot analyses showed that eosinophils and mEar1 activated Smad-1/5/8 but did not affect Smad-2/3 activation or expression of bone morphogenetic protein receptors (BMPR-1A/1B/2) or transforming growth factor (TGF)-β receptors (TGFBR1/2) in SMC from WT and Runx2 knockout mice. Immunoprecipitation showed that mEar1 formed immune complexes with BMPR-1A/1B but not TGFBR1/2. Immunofluorescence double-staining, ligand binding, and Scatchard plot analysis demonstrated that mEar1 bound to BMPR-1A and BMPR-1B with similar affinity. Likewise, human ECP and eosinophil-derived neurotoxin (EDN) also bound to BMPR-1A/1B on human vascular SMC and promoted SMC osteogenic differentiation. In a cohort of 5864 men from the Danish Cardiovascular Screening trial and its subpopulation of 394 participants, blood eosinophil counts and ECP levels correlated with the calcification scores of different arterial segments from coronary arteries to iliac arteries. CONCLUSION: Eosinophils release cationic proteins that can promote SMC calcification and atherogenesis using the BMPR-1A/1B-Smad-1/5/8-Runx2 signalling pathway.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Meng, Zhaojie","Zhang, Shuya","Li, Wei","Wang, Yunzhe","Wang, Minjie","Liu, Xin","Liu, Cong Lin","Liao, Sha","Liu, Tianxiao","Yang, Chongzhe","Lindholt, Jes Sanddal","Rasmussen, Lars Melholt","Obel, Lasse M.","Stubbe, Jane","Diederichsen, Axel Cosmus Pyndt","Sun, Yong","Chen, Yabing","Yu, Paul B.","Libby, Peter","Shi, Guo Ping","Guo, Junli"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-685232"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Guo, Junli"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Birmingham VA Medical Center","Brigham and Women's Hospital","First Affiliated Hospital of Zhengzhou University","Guangzhou Medical University","Hainan Medical University","Jilin Agricultural University"],"keyword":["Calcification","Eosinophil","Eosinophil cationic protein","Smooth muscle cell"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cationic proteins from eosinophils bind bone morphogenetic protein receptors promoting vascular calcification and atherogenesis","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/eurheartj/ehad262","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-685232","identifier":[{"id":"85166392867","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10393071","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37279475","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-87a66f93-9247-424b-ae9f-05613e381535"],"keyword":["Bone morphogenetic protein receptors","Calcification","Eosinophil","Eosinophil cationic protein","Smooth muscle cell"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0E9F493F6E54E230DAECA5F9367AEDD7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/237885333/ehad262.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/eurheartj/ehad262","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"brigham and women s hospital","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Brigham and Women's Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"hainan medical university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hainan Medical University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"jilin agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jilin Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"first affiliated hospital of zhengzhou university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"First Affiliated Hospital of Zhengzhou University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"guangzhou medical university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Guangzhou Medical University","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiac, thoracic, and Vascular surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"us","key":"birmingham va medical center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Birmingham VA Medical Center","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhaojie","key":"mengzhaojiepau","last":"Meng","name":"Meng, Zhaojie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuya","key":"zhangshuyapau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Shuya","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"liweipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Wei","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Yunzhe","key":"wangyunzhepau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Yunzhe","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Minjie","key":"wangminjiepau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Minjie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xin","key":"liuxinpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Xin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Cong Lin","key":"liuconglinpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Cong Lin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sha","key":"liaoshapau","last":"Liao","name":"Liao, Sha","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tianxiao","key":"liutianxiaopau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Tianxiao","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Chongzhe","key":"yangchongzhepau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Chongzhe","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Jes S.","key":"lindholtjessanddalpau","last":"Lindholt","locid":"27d83f24-51cd-4d27-9e32-7501319bdf2b","name":"Lindholt, Jes Sanddal","name_org":"Lindholt, Jes S.","orcid":"0000-0001-9536-4488","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars M.","key":"rasmussenlarsmelholtpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"bf5d4e3b-cb51-4e61-a6d1-e22445213324","name":"Rasmussen, Lars Melholt","name_org":"Rasmussen, Lars M.","orcid":"0000-0001-5795-4794","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse M.","key":"obellassempau","last":"Obel","locid":"17bb0772-8f32-409a-b977-05438dd78b3a","name":"Obel, Lasse M.","orcid":"0000-0003-0037-8962","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jane","key":"stubbejanepau","last":"Stubbe","locid":"f6c78cb4-b790-4690-b62e-