dus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-685232","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Low-pass genome sequencing (LP GS) has shown distinct advantages over traditional methods for the detection of mosaicism. However, no study has systematically evaluated the accuracy of LP GS in the detection of mosaic aneuploidies and copy number variants (CNVs) in prenatal diagnosis. Moreover, the influence of sequencing depth on mosaicism detection of LP GS has not been fully evaluated. To evaluate the accuracy of LP GS in the detection of mosaic aneuploidies and mosaic CNVs, 27 samples with known aneuploidies and CNVs and 1 negative female sample were used to generate 6 simulated samples and 21 virtual samples, each sample contained 9 different mosaic levels. Mosaic levels were simulated by pooling reads or DNA from each positive sample and the negative sample according to a series of percentages (ranging from 3 to 40%). Then, the influence of sequencing depth on LP GS in the detection of mosaic aneuploidies and CNVs was evaluated by downsampling. To evaluate the accuracy of LP GS in the detection of mosaic aneuploidies and CNVs, a comparative analysis of mosaic levels was performed using 6 simulated samples and 21 virtual samples with 35 M million (M) uniquely aligned high-quality reads (UAHRs). For mosaic levels > 30%, the average difference (detected mosaic levels vs. theoretical mosaic levels) of 6 mosaic CNVs in simulated samples was 4.0%, and the average difference (detected mosaic levels vs. mosaic levels of Y chromosome) of 6 mosaic aneuploidies and 15 mosaic CNVs in virtual samples was 2.7%. Furthermore, LP GS had a higher detection rate and accuracy for the detection of mosaic aneuploidies and CNVs of larger sizes, especially mosaic aneuploidies. For depth evaluation, the results of LP GS in downsampling samples were compared with those of LP GS using 35 M UAHRs. The detection sensitivity of LP GS for 6 mosaic aneuploidies and 15 mosaic CNVs in virtual samples increased with UAHR. For mosaic levels > 30%, the total detection sensitivity reached a plateau at 30 M UAHRs. With 30 M UAHRs, the total detection sensitivity was 99.2% for virtual samples. We demonstrated the accuracy of LP GS in mosaicism detection using simulated data and virtual samples, respectively. Thirty M UAHRs (single-end 35 bp) were optimal for LP GS in the detection of mosaic aneuploidies and most mosaic CNVs larger than 1.48 Mb (Megabases) with mosaic levels > 30%. These results could provide a reference for laboratories that perform clinical LP GS in the detection of mosaic aneuploidies and CNVs.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Liu, Yanqiu","Hao, Shengju","Guo, Xueqin","Fan, Linlin","Qiao, Zhihong","Wang, Yaoshen","Wang, Xiaoli","Man, Jianfen","Wang, Lina","Wei, Xiaoming","Peng, Huanhuan","Peng, Zhiyu","Sun, Yan","Song, Lijie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-701148"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Song, Lijie","Sun, Yan"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI Group","Gansu Provincial Maternity and Child-care Hospital","Jiangxi Maternal and Child Health Hospital","MGI Tech"],"keyword":["Low pass genome sequencing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"accuracy and depth evaluation of clinical low pass genome sequencing in the detection of mosaic aneuploidies and cnvs","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12920-023-01703-8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-701148","identifier":[{"id":"37978521","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10656965","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85177042315","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-d91d5920-0a96-42bc-8ea7-2a022e08ecfb"],"keyword":["Low pass genome sequencing","Mosaic CNVs","Mosaic aneuploidies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D952629FF43F8CE6BA10B1CBDFAA3CF1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12920-023-01703-8","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/340668636/s12920-023-01703-8.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"jiangxi maternal and child health hospital","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jiangxi Maternal and Child Health Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"gansu provincial maternity and child care hospital","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Gansu Provincial Maternity and Child-care Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"bgi group","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI Group","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"mgi tech","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"MGI Tech","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Microbial and Chemical Ecology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Microbial and Chemical Ecology, Bacterial Interactions and Evolution"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yanqiu","key":"liuyanqiupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Yanqiu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Shengju","key":"haoshengjupau","last":"Hao","name":"Hao, Shengju","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Xueqin","key":"guoxueqinpau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Xueqin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Linlin","key":"fanlinlinpau","last":"Fan","name":"Fan, Linlin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhihong","key":"qiaozhihongpau","last":"Qiao","name":"Qiao, Zhihong","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yaoshen","key":"wangyaoshenpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Yaoshen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoli","key":"wangxiaolipau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Xiaoli","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jianfen","key":"manjianfenpau","last":"Man","name":"Man, Jianfen","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lina","key":"wanglinapau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Lina","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoming","key":"weixiaomingpau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Xiaoming","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Huanhuan","key":"penghuanhuanpau","last":"Peng","name":"Peng, Huanhuan","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhiyu","key":"pengzhiyupau","last":"Peng","name":"Peng, Zhiyu","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yan","key":"sunyanpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Yan","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Lijie","key":"songlijiepau","last":"Song","locid":"f7e5c93a-492f-45b2-992d-e1c2d5c6423b","name":"Song, Lijie","orcid":"0000-0002-0168-3937","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37978521"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12920-023-01703-8","issn":["17558794"],"journal":"BMC Medical Genomics","paperid":"294","publisher":"BioMed Central Ltd.","status":"p","title":"BMC Medical Genomics","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85177042315"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d91d5920-0a96-42bc-8ea7-2a022e08ecfb"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Accuracy and depth evaluation of clinical low pass genome sequencing in the detection of mosaic aneuploidies and CNVs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-701148","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Extreme precipitation events caused by climate change leads to large variation of nitrogen input to aquatic ecosystems. Our previous study demonstrated the significant effect of different ammonium pulse patterns (differing in magnitude and frequency) on submersed macrophyte growth based on six plant morphological traits. However, how connectivity among plant traits responds to nitrogen pulse changes, which in turn affects plant performance, has not yet been fully elucidated. The response of three common submersed macrophytes (Myriophyllum spicatum, Vallisneria natans and Potamogeton maackianus) to three ammonium pulse patterns was tested using plant trait network (PTN) analysis based on 18 measured physiological and morphological traits. We found that ammonium pulses enhanced trait connectivity in PTN, which may enable plants to assimilate ammonium and/or mitigate ammonium toxicity. Large input pulses with low frequency had stronger effects on PTNs compared to low input pulses with high frequency. Due to the cumulative and time-lagged effect of the plant response to the ammonium pulse, there was a profound and prolonged effect on plant performance after the release of the pulse. The highly connected traits in PTN were those related to biomass allocation (e.g., plant biomass, stem ratio, leaf ratio and ramet number) rather than physiological traits, while phenotype-related traits (e.g., plant height, root length and AB ratio) and energy storage-related traits (e.g., stem starch) were least connected. V. natans showed clear functional divergence among traits, making it more flexible to cope with unfavorable habitats (i.e., high input pulses with low frequencies). M. spicatum with high RGR revealed strong correlations among traits and thus supported nitrogen accumulation from favourable environments (i.e., low input pulses with high frequencies). Our study highlights the responses of PTN for submerged macrophytes to ammonium pulses depends on their intrinsic metabolic rates, the magnitude, frequency and duration of the pulses, and our results contribute to the understanding of the impact of resource pulses on the population dynamics of submersed macrophytes within the context of global climate change.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Yuan, Guixiang","Tan, Xiaoyao","Guo, Peiqin","Xing, Ke","Chen, Zhenglong","Li, Dongbo","Yu, Sizhe","Peng, Hui","Li, Wei","Fu, Hui","Jeppesen, Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-145349"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Wei","Yuan, Guixiang"],"country":["China","Turkey"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hunan Agricultural University","Middle East Technical University","Nanchang Institute of Technology","Sino-Danish Centre for Education and Research"],"keyword":["Plant trait network","Submerged macrophyte"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"linking trait network to growth performance of submerged macrophytes in response to ammonium pulse","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85142673064","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-145349","identifier":[{"id":"85142673064","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36446174","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-1bf19e71-e4f2-4f50-be1d-f3f0f7f8d255"],"keyword":["Ammonium pulse","Plant trait network","Pulse size","Submerged macrophyte"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F3F6854F482C3283E0555836CCD7E706"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"hunan agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hunan Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"nanchang institute of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanchang Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Freshwater Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"tr","key":"middle east technical university","loc":["Turkey","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Middle East Technical University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"cn","key":"sino danish centre for education and research","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sino-Danish Centre for Education and Research","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Guixiang","key":"yuanguixiangpau","last":"Yuan","name":"Yuan, Guixiang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoyao","key":"tanxiaoyaopau","last":"Tan","name":"Tan, Xiaoyao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peiqin","key":"guopeiqinpau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Peiqin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ke","key":"xingkepau","last":"Xing","name":"Xing, Ke","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhenglong","key":"chenzhenglongpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Zhenglong","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dongbo","key":"lidongbopau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Dongbo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sizhe","key":"yusizhepau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Sizhe","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hui","key":"penghuipau","last":"Peng","name":"Peng, Hui","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"liweipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Wei","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hui","key":"fuhuipau","last":"Fu","name":"Fu, Hui","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5 6","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"jeppesenerikpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"22bb5d6e-a9ae-4f70-81da-df1c57e71163","name":"Jeppesen, Erik","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36446174"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.watres.2022.119403","issn":["00431354","18792448"],"issn_org":["00431354"],"journal":"Water Research","paperid":"119403","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Water Research","volume":"229"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85142673064"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1bf19e71-e4f2-4f50-be1d-f3f0f7f8d255"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Linking trait network to growth performance of submerged macrophytes in response to ammonium pulse","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-145349","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Soil microorganisms dominate the biogeochemical cycles of elements in glacier forelands, which continue to expand due to the climate warming. We analyzed the soil microbial functional characteristics among three types of glacier forelands on the Tibetan Plateau: Yulong Glacier (Y), a temperate glacier; Tianshan Urumqi Glacier No. 1 (T), a sub-continental glacier; and Laohugou Glacier No. 12 (L), a continental glacier. Here, soil microbial functional genes were quantified using quantitative microbial element cycling technology (QMEC). We found that, in the three glacier forelands, the abundances of soil microbial functional genes related to hemicellulose degradation and reductive acetyl-CoA pathway were highest compared with other carbon-related functional genes. The main nitrogen cycling genes were involved in ammonification. The functional genes of the phosphorus cycle and sulfur cycle were related to organic phosphate mineralization and sulfur oxidation. Furthermore, the soils of the temperate glacier foreland with better hydrothermal conditions had the most complex microbial functional gene structure and the highest functional potentials, followed by those of the soils of continental glacier foreland with the driest environment. These significant differences in soil microbial functional genes among the three types of glacier forelands verified the impacts of geographic difference on microbial functional characteristics, as well as providing a basis for the study of soil microbial functions and biogeochemical cycles in glacier forelands.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Zhang, Jie Jie","Priemé, Anders","Chen, Xian Ke","Zhou, Han Chang","Zhang, Qin Wei","Zhuang, Xu Liang","Qin, Xiang","Zhuang, Guo Qiang","Ma, An Zhou"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-533579"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Northwest Institute of Eco-Environment and Resources","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Sino-Danish Center for education and research","State Key Laboratory of Environmental Chemistry and Ecotoxicology, Research Center for Eco-Environmental Sciences, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Microbial functional gene","Tibetan Plateau"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"基于 qmec 分析的青藏高原不同类型冰川前缘地土壤微生物功能潜力","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-533579","identifier":[{"id":"85146421582","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36635839","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-eaa651bc-5829-442a-aea3-ca1dc645a42c"],"keyword":["Tibetan Plateau","glacier foreland soil","glacier types","microbial functional gene","quantitative microbial element cycling (QMEC)"],"lang":"Chinese","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AD3B4B491B93BBEDC232A50A16680216"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"state key laboratory of environmental chemistry and ecotoxicology research center for eco environmental sciences chinese academy of sciences beijing","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"State Key Laboratory of Environmental Chemistry and Ecotoxicology, Research Center for Eco-Environmental Sciences, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"sino danish center for education and research","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sino-Danish Center for education and research","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"cn","key":"cas northwest institute of eco environment and resources","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Northwest Institute of Eco-Environment and Resources","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jie Jie","key":"zhangjiejiepau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Jie Jie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"prieméanderspau","last":"Priemé","locid":"412c33ea-a5f0-4348-aea8-1d126e9f3c2f","name":"Priemé, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-9925-067X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 4","first":"Xian Ke","key":"chenxiankepau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Xian Ke","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Han Chang","key":"zhouhanchangpau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Han Chang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Qin Wei","key":"zhangqinweipau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Qin Wei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 5","first":"Xu Liang","key":"zhuangxuliangpau","last":"Zhuang","name":"Zhuang, Xu Liang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Xiang","key":"qinxiangpau","last":"Qin","name":"Qin, Xiang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Guo Qiang","key":"zhuangguoqiangpau","last":"Zhuang","name":"Zhuang, Guo Qiang","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"An Zhou","key":"maanzhoupau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, An Zhou","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36635839"],"pub":{"doi":"10.13227/j.hjkx.202203184","issn":["02503301"],"issue":"1","journal":"Huanjing Kexue","pages":"512-519","status":"p","title":"Huanjing Kexue","title_org":"Huanjing Kexue/Environmental Science","volume":"44"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146421582"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-eaa651bc-5829-442a-aea3-ca1dc645a42c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"基于 QMEC 分析的青藏高原不同类型冰川前缘地土壤微生物功能潜力","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-533579","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background The medicinal material quality of Citrus reticulata ‘Chachi’ differs depending on the bioactive components influenced by the planting area. Environmental factors, such as soil nutrients, the plant-associated microbiome and climatic conditions, play important roles in the accumulation of bioactive components in citrus. However, how these environmental factors mediate the production of bioactive components of medicinal plants remains understudied. Results Here, a multi-omics approach was used to clarify the role of environmental factors such as soil nutrients and the root-associated microbiome on the accumulation of monoterpenes in the peel of C. reticulata ‘Chachi’ procured from core (geo-authentic product region) and non-core (non-geo-authentic product region) geographical regions. The soil environment (high salinity, Mg, Mn and K) enhanced the monoterpene content by promoting the expression of salt stress-responsive genes and terpene backbone synthase in the host plants from the core region. The microbial effects on the monoterpene accumulation of citrus from the core region were further verified by synthetic community (SynCom) experiments. Rhizosphere microorganisms activated terpene synthesis and promoted monoterpene accumulation through interactions with the host immune system. Endophyte microorganisms derived from soil with the potential for terpene synthesis might enhance monoterpene accumulation in citrus by providing precursors of monoterpenes. Conclusions Overall, this study demonstrated that both soil properties and the soil microbiome impacted monoterpene production in citrus peel, thus providing an essential basis for increasing fruit quality via reasonable fertilization and precision microbiota management.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Su, Jianmu","Wang, Yayu","Bai, Mei","Peng, Tianhua","Li, Huisi","Xu, Hui Juan","Guo, Guifang","Bai, Haiyi","Rong, Ning","Sahu, Sunil Kumar","He, Hanjun","Liang, Xiangxiu","Jin, Canzhi","Liu, Wei","Strube, Mikael Lenz","Gram, Lone","Li, Yongtao","Wang, Ertao","Liu, Huan","Wu, Hong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-669216"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Liu, Huan","Wu, Hong"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI Group","Chinese Academy of Sciences","South China Agricultural University"],"keyword":["Monoterpenes","Soil conditions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"soil conditions and the plant microbiome boost the accumulation of monoterpenes in the fruit of i citrus reticulata i chachi","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40168-023-01504-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-669216","identifier":[{"id":"85151000854","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36973820","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10044787","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-3748cad1-19d2-4435-b67c-30f991c0dcfa"],"keyword":["Citri Reticulatae Pericarpium","Citrus reticulata ‘Chachi'","Monoterpenes","Plant micropbiome","Soil conditions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-68A8683DA304DCBCC67CF56A5A56B540"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/318113347/s40168_023_01504_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40168-023-01504-2","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"south china agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"South China Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark