{"abstract":"The optimal allocation of deterioration control in risk-based inspection (RBI) planning is based on the pre-posterior analysis using Bayesian decision theory and expected utility theory. This paper applies the RBI planning in the area of offshore wind turbine foundation structure, aiming to minimize the life-cycle cost which takes the direct cost and the indirect consequence into account. The direct cost refers to the direct loss and the indirect consequence refers to the power loss due to the downtime of wind turbine. A monopile offshore wind turbine structure is analyzed in OpenFAST simulation package to demonstrate how to utilize RBI planning in the field of support structure of offshore wind turbine, in which the environmental condition is taken from the statistical data in North Sea. The case study show that the RBI planning can effectively reduce the expected life-cycle cost of offshore wind turbine.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Zhang, Wei Heng","Lu, Dagang","Qin, Jianjun","Liu, Min","Faber, Michael Havbro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-726225"],"event":{"end":"2022-07-27","place":"Guilin, cn","start":"2022-07-24","title":"International Conference on Green Building, Civil Engineering and Smart City, GBCESC 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Lu, Dagang"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harbin Institute of Technology","Shanghai Jiao Tong University"],"keyword":["Life Cycle Cost","Offshore wind turbine","Risk based inspection"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk based inspection planning for support structure of offshore wind turbine","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85138812414&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Acknowledgement. China’s National Key R&D Plan is funding this project (Grant No. 2021YFB2600500). The China Scholarship Council (CSC) (Grant No. 201906120281) supports the first author’s research at Aalborg University."],"id":"S01-000.00-726225","identifier":[{"id":"85138812414","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-bfd60ee1-837f-47c5-91b8-b5572ade4759"],"keyword":["Life-cycle cost","Offshore wind turbine","Risk-based inspection"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EB34F891F59736025E1DC583D6905B99"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"harbin institute of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Harbin Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"shanghai jiao tong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai Jiao Tong University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Weiheng","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"983baec6-6769-4e0e-93a6-9d1dfa5dd6cc","name":"Zhang, Wei Heng","name_org":"Zhang, Weiheng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dagang","key":"lupau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Dagang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jianjun","key":"qinpau","last":"Qin","name":"Qin, Jianjun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Min","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","locid":"714a754d-0015-42ff-a4c8-07d78a0ed4b6","name":"Liu, Min","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael Havbro","key":"faberpau","last":"Faber","locid":"304dde84-c558-4302-a230-e375d61f0c1e","name":"Faber, Michael Havbro","orcid":"0000-0003-3761-0737","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wei","key":"guopedh","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Wei","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kai","key":"qianpedh","last":"Qian","name":"Qian, Kai","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-981-19-5217-3_59","eisbn":["9789811952173"],"isbn":["9789811952166","9789811952180"],"issn":["23662557"],"pages":"591-598","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Civil Engineering","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2022 International Conference on Green Building, Civil Engineering and Smart City"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85138812414"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-bfd60ee1-837f-47c5-91b8-b5572ade4759"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Risk-Based Inspection Planning for Support Structure of Offshore Wind Turbine","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-726225","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The in-person workshop \"Drug Dissolution in Oral Drug Absorption\" was held on May 23-24, 2023, in Baltimore, MD, USA. The workshop was organized into lectures and breakout sessions. Three common topics that were re-visited by various lecturers were amorphous solid dispersions (ASDs), dissolution/permeation interplay, and in vitro methods to predict in vivo biopharmaceutics performance and risk. Topics that repeatedly surfaced across breakout sessions were the following: (1) meaning and assessment of \"dissolved drug,\" particularly of poorly water soluble drug in colloidal environments (e.g., fed conditions, ASDs); (2) potential limitations of a test that employs sink conditions for a poorly water soluble drug; (3) non-compendial methods (e.g., two-stage or multi-stage method, dissolution/permeation methods); (4) non-compendial conditions (e.g., apex vessels, non-sink conditions); and (5) potential benefit of having both a quality control method for batch release and a biopredictive/biorelevant method for biowaiver or bridging scenarios. An identified obstacle to non-compendial methods is the uncertainty of global regulatory acceptance of such methods.","author_count":46,"contributors":["Raines, Kimberly","Agarwal, Payal","Augustijns, Patrick","Alayoubi, Alaadin","Attia, Lucas","Bauer-Brandl, Annette","Brandl, Martin","Chatterjee, Parnali","Chen, Hansong","Yu, Yuly Chiang","Coutant, Carrie","Coutinho, Ana Luisa","Curran, David","Dressman, Jennifer","Ericksen, Bryan","Falade, Leah","Gao, Yi","Gao, Zongming","Ghosh, Debasis","Ghosh, Tapash","Govada, Anitha","Gray, Elizabeth","Guo, Ruiqiong","Hammell, Dana","Hermans, Andre","Jaini, Rohit","Li, Hanlin","Mandula, Haritha","Men, Shuaiqian","Milsmann, Johanna","Moldthan, Huong","Moody, Rebecca","Moseson, Dana E","Müllertz, Anette","Patel, Roshni","Paudel, Kalpana","Reppas, Christos","Savkur, Rajesh","Schaefer, Kerstin","Serajuddin, Abu","Taylor, Lynne S","Valapil, Rutu","Wei, Kevin","Weitschies, Werner","Yamashita, Shinji","Polli, James E"],"cuid":["S02-088.46-735470"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Polli, James E"],"country":["Belgium","Canada","Germany","Greece","Japan","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["AbbVie","All Global Affiliations","Boehringer Ingelheim","Boehringer Ingelheim Pharma GmbH &amp; Co. KG","Eli Lilly USA","Eli Lilly and Company, Insulins Development Team, Bracknell, UK","Fraunhofer Institute for Translational Medicine and Pharmacology (ITMP)","Fraunhofer Institute of Translational Pharmacology and Medicine","Ghent University","GlaxoSmithKline","KU Leuven","Massachusetts Institute of Technology","Massachusetts Institute of Technology Haystack Observatory","Merck","Merck Canada Inc.","National and Kapodistrian University of Athens","Pfizer","Pfizer Inc.","Purdue University","Ritsumeikan University","St. John's University","Takeda Pharmaceutical Company Limited","Takeda Pharmaceuticals International Company","United States Food and Drug Administration","University of Greifswald","University of Leuven","University of Maryland","University of Maryland, Baltimore","Ursinus College","Vertex Pharmaceuticals","Vertex Pharmaceuticals, Inc."],"keyword":["Absorption","Amorphous","Biopharmaceutics","Dissolution","Drug Liberation","Food","Humans","Intestinal Absorption","Permeability","Solubility","Water"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"drug dissolution in oral drug absorption workshop report","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://do