{"abstract":"Monitoring P flux at the Earth’s surface-atmosphere interface has many challenges. Therefore, the development of a technology with high selectivity and high sensitivity to in situ trace PH3 in aquatic or sedimentary environments has become a priority. Herein, an amperometric PH3 microsensor meeting the above conditions is developed. The sensor is equipped with a Au-coated Pt working electrode (WE) and a Pt guard electrode (GE) positioned in an outer glass casing. The WE and GE are polarized at a fixed value of +150 mV with respect to a pseudo-reference electrode. The outer casing is filled with an acid electrolyte solution, and the tip is sealed using a thin silicone membrane. Mixed gases from the environment diffuse through the first layer of the silicone membrane, and the major H2S disruptor is eliminated by a ZnCl2-propylene carbonate trap positioned in the front of the microsensor. Later, the gases diffuse into an electrolytic solution through the second layer of the silicone membrane, and PH3 is selectively oxidized into H3PO4 on the Au-coated Pt WE. This electrochemical oxidation thereby creates a current that is proportional to the concentration of PH3 (>2 nmol·L-1). With the aid of the H2S trap casing and selective catalysis, the effects of other gases on the microsensor can be ignored in terms of environmental monitoring. An example from the sedimentary profile shows that high PH3 accumulations are found 13 mm below the sediment surface.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kang, Fuxing","Yang, Wei","Guo, Mengwen","Pedersen, Lars Borregaard","Nielsen, Lars Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-154034"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Kang, Fuxing"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nanjing Agricultural University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"highly selective microsensor for monitoring trace phosphine in the environment","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85146597509","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-154034","identifier":[{"id":"85146597509","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36656060","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-2b305f15-a208-4ba2-94a8-1ed2ab417551"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5061099B96DD0016F450D07DC91E4BA3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Center for Electromicrobiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"nanjing agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing Agricultural University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Fuxing","key":"kangpau","last":"Kang","locid":"670c1dcb-cfd4-45b4-bc4b-74929684a38d","name":"Kang, Fuxing","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Wei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mengwen","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Mengwen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Borregaard","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"685203c6-f052-4c13-8bf8-428938013116","name":"Pedersen, Lars Borregaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Peter","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"7b1f70e1-663b-4a12-b10c-a12dfc320c81","name":"Nielsen, Lars Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-7269-4860","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36656060"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.analchem.2c04652","issn":["00032700","15204782"],"issn_org":["00032700"],"issue":"4","journal":"Analytical Chemistry","pages":"2460-2468","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Analytical Chemistry","volume":"95"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146597509"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2b305f15-a208-4ba2-94a8-1ed2ab417551"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Highly Selective Microsensor for Monitoring Trace Phosphine in the Environment","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-154034","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Studies on the associations between maternal complications during pregnancy and childhood asthma are exclusively conducted in Western countries. The findings are mixed and may not be translated to other populations. We aimed to investigate the associations among the Chinese population and to determine whether the associations were mediated through pre-term birth, caesarean delivery, low birthweight and not breastfeeding in the first 6 months. METHODS: We conducted a retrospective cohort study of 166 772 children in Guangzhou, China. Information on maternal gestational hypertension, gestational diabetes and gestational anaemia during pregnancy was extracted from medical records. Ever-diagnosis of asthma in children aged 6-12 years was obtained by questionnaire. Logistic regression models and mediation analyses were used to estimate the adjusted odds ratios (aORs) and 95% confidence intervals for childhood asthma. RESULTS: Gestational hypertension, gestational diabetes and gestational anaemia during pregnancy were associated with an increased risk of ever-diagnosed childhood asthma: aOR 1.48 (95% CI 1.37-1.60), 1.71 (95% CI 1.65-1.78) and 1.34 (95% CI 1.26-1.45), respectively. A stronger association was observed for two or three gestational complications (aOR 2.02 (95% CI 1.93-2.16)) than one gestational complication (aOR 1.64 (95% CI 1.52-1.77)). The aOR for the three gestational complications was 1.35 (95% CI 1.26-1.45), 1.63 (95% CI 1.58-1.70) and 1.32 (95% CI 1.24-1.43), respectively, after controlling for the mediators, including pre-term birth, caesarean delivery, low birthweight and not breastfeeding in the first 6 months. CONCLUSIONS: Gestational hypertension, gestational diabetes and gestational anaemia were associated with childhood asthma, and the associations were partially explained by the mediation effects.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Ma, Ying","Wu, Yu","Zhang, Yi","Jiao, Ting","Guo, Shuangshuang","Zhang, Dongying","Yang, Jiewen","Deng, Nali","Liang, Zhijiang","Wang, Harry H X","Bao, Wei","Chen, Ruoling","Tang, Jie","Liu, Xiaoqin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-232990"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["China","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Guangzhou Medical College","Guangzhou University","Shenzhen Center for Disease Control and Prevention","Sun Yat-Sen University","University of Science and Technology of China","University of Wolverhampton"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"associations between maternal complications during pregnancy and childhood asthma a retrospective cohort study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1183/23120541.00548-2022","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study was embedded within the framework of the Physical Health Monitoring Project of Primary and High School Students in Guangzhou (PHMPPHSS), launched by the Education Bureau of Guangzhou in 2017. The design, organisation and implementation of PHMPPHSS have been described previously [16]. Parents whose children planned to participate in the annual physical examination were contacted through the internet to get parental consent for their children to participate in the PHMPPHSS. A pre-developed health management software was shared with the parents after they provided informed consent. The parents were then surveyed by a structured parental questionnaire and a child’s questionnaire using the software. Support statement: This study was supported by National Natural Science Foundation of China (82073571 and 81773457 to J. Tang). The study sponsors had no role in the design and conduct of the study; collection, management, analysis and interpretation of the data; preparation, review or approval of the manuscript; or decision to submit the manuscript for publication. Funding information for this article has been deposited with the Crossref Funder Registry."],"id":"S01-000.00-232990","identifier":[{"id":"37057092","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10086685","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85156257742","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b5b743da-1feb-4a36-a845-27e118dd99f3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1FAFEE35A32EB4AC884C73931B163A25"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1183/23120541.00548-2022","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"guangzhou university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Guangzhou University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"shenzhen center for disease control and prevention","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shenzhen Center for Disease Control and Prevention","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"guangzhou medical college","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Guangzhou Medical College","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"sun yat sen university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sun Yat-Sen University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"cn","key":"university of science and technology of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Science and Technology of China","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"gb","key":"university of wolverhampton","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Wolverhampton","used":1},{"affno":"8","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - National Centre for Register-based Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ying","key":"mayingpau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Ying","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yu","key":"wuyupau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Yu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Yi","key":"zhangyipau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yi","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ting","key":"jiaotingpau","last":"Jiao","name":"Jiao, Ting","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuangshuang","key":"guoshuangshuangpau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Shuangshuang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Dongying","key":"zhangdongyingpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Dongying","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jiewen","key":"yangjiewenpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Jiewen","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Nali","key":"dengnalipau","last":"Deng","name":"Deng, Nali","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhijiang","key":"liangzhijiangpau","last":"Liang","name":"Liang, Zhijiang","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Harry H X","key":"wangharryhxpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Harry H X","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"baoweipau","last":"Bao","name":"Bao, Wei","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Ruoling","key":"chenruolingpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Ruoling","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jie","key":"tangjiepau","last":"Tang","name":"Tang, Jie","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xiaoqin","key":"liuxiaoqinpau","last":"Liu","locid":"9e8aa4c4-0d47-4838-88e7-124337341316","name":"Liu, Xiaoqin","orcid":"0000-0003-4519-1536","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37057092"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1183/23120541.00548-2022","issn":["23120541"],"issue":"2","journal":"ERJ Open Research","paperid":"00548-2022","publisher":"European Respiratory Society","status":"p","title":"ERJ Open Research","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85156257742"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b5b743da-1feb-4a36-a845-27e118dd99f3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Associations between maternal complications during pregnancy and childhood asthma : a retrospective cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-232990","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Molecular doping is an effective approach to tune the charge density and optimize electrical performance of conjugated polymers. However, the introduction of dopants, on the other hand, may disturb the polymer microstructure and disrupt the charge transport path, often leading to a decrease of charge carrier mobility and deterioration of electrical conductivity of the doped films. Here we show that dopant-induced disorder can be overcome by rational engineering of polymer-dopant interactions, resulting in remarkable enhancement of electrical conductivity. Benchmark poly(3-hexylthiophene) (P3HT) and its analogous random polymers of 3-hexylthiophene and thiophene P[(3HT)1-x-stat-(T)x] were synthesized and doped by 2,3,5,6-tetrafluoro-7,7,8,8-tetracyanoquinodimethane (F4TCNQ). Remarkably, random P[(3HT)1-x-stat-(T)x] was doped to a far superior electrical conductivity, that in the case of x ≥ 0.24, the conductivity of P[(3HT)1-x-stat-(T)x] is over 100 times higher than that of the doped P3HT, despite both P3HT and P[(3HT)1-x-stat-(T)x] exhibit comparable charge carrier mobility in their pristine state and in spite of their practically identical redox properties. This result can be traced back to the formation of π-stacked polymer-dopant-polymer co-crystals exhibiting extremely short packing distances of 3.13–3.15 Å. The mechanism behind these performances is based on a new role played by the dopant molecules that we name “bridging-gluing”. The results are coherently verified by the combination of optical absorption spectroscopy, X-ray diffraction, density functional theory calculations, and molecular dynamics simulations.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Kim, Jongho","Guo, Jing","Sini, Gjergji","Sørensen, Michael Korning","Andreasen, Jens Wenzel","Woon, Kai Lin","Coropceanu, Veaceslav","Paleti, Sri Harish Kumar","Wei, Huan","Peralta, Sébastien","Mallouki, Mohamed","Müller, Christian","Hu, Yuanyuan","Bui, Thanh Tuan","Wang, Suhao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-375163"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Hu, Yuanyuan","Sini, Gjergji","Wang, Suhao"],"country":["China","France","Malaysia","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CY Cergy Paris Université","Chalmers University of Technology","Hunan University","University of Arizona","University of Malaya"],"keyword":["Charge transport","Conducting polymers","DFT calculations","Doping"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"remarkable conductivity enhancement in p doped polythiophenes via rational engineering of polymer dopant interactions","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mtadv.2023.100360","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-375163","identifier":[{"id":"85150025370","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ebe97290-c35a-4394-b174-95bf102e85f2"],"keyword":["Aggregations","Charge-transport","Conducting polymers","DFT calculations","Doping"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-39C034CE38698C9A2C03AC949B2A8D7E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/315222138/1_s2.0_S2590049823000206_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mtadv.2023.100360","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fr","key":"cy cergy paris université","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"CY Cergy Paris Université","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"hunan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hunan University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Energy Conversion and Storage","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Energy Conversion and Storage, Imaging and Structural Analysis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"my","key":"university of malaya","loc":["Malaysia","Asia, South"],"name":"University of Malaya","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"university of arizona","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Arizona","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"se","key":"chalmers university of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Chalmers University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jongho","key":"kimpau","last":"Kim","name":"Kim, Jongho","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jing","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Jing","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gjergji","key":"sinipau","last":"Sini","name":"Sini, Gjergji","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Korning","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"de7ab019-58bd-44c1-9d94-a7c5a98279fe","name":"Sørensen, Michael Korning","orcid":"0000-0002-7031-2072","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Wenzel","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"c838d5f7-f708-47d2-a9f4-c4c12e5c7c2d","name":"Andreasen, Jens Wenzel","orcid":"0000-0002-3145-0229","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Kai Lin","key":"woonpau","last":"Woon"