,"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85159222787"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f6203458-e10e-411b-94e5-cabaa47899d6"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Validation and depth evaluation of low-pass genome sequencing in prenatal diagnosis using 387 amniotic fluid samples","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695193","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Robust U-Pb dating of accessory minerals (e.g., apatite, titanite, wolframite, and cassiterite) by LA-ICP-MS is often impeded by variable contents of common Pb in matrix-matched reference material (RM). Therefore, common Pb needs to be corrected in these RMs analyses that are used as standards to calibrate isotope fractionation during data reduction. In this study, a novel stand-alone computer program (called Isoclock) focused on the deduction of common Pb from RM, and the corrected RM were used for isotope fractionation. A new common Pb correction method was introduced into the program that allows the deduction of common Pb not only in 206Pb and 207Pb, but also in 208Pb, so that both U/Pb and Th/Pb age calculations can be performed. The software contains several processing steps for the raw files of different mass spectrometers. The processing interface contains data import and view, background correction and filtering of outliers, calculation of common Pb for RMs, fractionation calibration, and age calculation. Isoclock is written using the free and open-source Python language and can either run the code directly or by using a graphical interface. Finally, we discuss the main advantages of this software and its geological application using six examples of apatite, cassiterite, titanite, monazite and wolframite U-Pb dating.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Liu, Guo Qi","Zhao, Kui Dong","Ulrich, Thomas","Chen, Wei","Zhang, Di","Li, Qian","Zhao, He Dong","Zhang, Rong Qing","Xia, Fei"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-700101"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Qian","Liu, Guo Qi","Xia, Fei"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","China University of Geosciences, Wuhan","East China University Of Technology","Nanjing University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"isoclock a free and novel routine for common pb correction in u th pb data reduction of la icp ms analysis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85170675181","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-700101","identifier":[{"id":"85170675181","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-cb11b5ed-a6f3-4e7d-a6c0-7c4bfba6db10"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BC93EDB73BBB2B54D5B0B7C50807FC5D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"east china university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"East China University Of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"china university of geosciences wuhan","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China University of Geosciences, Wuhan","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Geoscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"nanjing university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guo Qi","key":"liuguoqipau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Guo Qi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kui Dong","key":"zhaokuidongpau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Kui Dong","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"ulrichthomaspau","last":"Ulrich","locid":"2f17303e-f53d-44ba-8f79-19298ed879fe","name":"Ulrich, Thomas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"chenweipau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Wei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Di","key":"zhangdipau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Di","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Qian","key":"liqianpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Qian","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"He Dong","key":"zhaohedongpau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, He Dong","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Rong Qing","key":"zhangrongqingpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Rong Qing","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fei","key":"xiafeipau","last":"Xia","name":"Xia, Fei","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/d3ja00217a","issn":["02679477","13645544"],"issn_org":["02679477"],"issue":"10","journal":"Journal of Analytical Atomic Spectrometry","pages":"2007-2018","publisher":"Royal Society of Chemistry","status":"p","title":"Journal of Analytical Atomic Spectrometry","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85170675181"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-cb11b5ed-a6f3-4e7d-a6c0-7c4bfba6db10"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Isoclock : a free and novel routine for common Pb correction in U-Th-Pb data reduction of LA-ICP-MS analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-700101","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The structural engineering of hydrated ammonium vanadate as a cathode for aqueous Zn-ion batteries has attracted significant research interest because of its ability to suppress vanadium dissolution and accelerate the electrochemical dynamics. Herein, a feasible fabrication strategy for oxygen-deficient (NH4)2V10O25·xH2O/GO (NVOH@GO) composites was proposed, and the charge storage mechanism was discussed. The results of characterization analysis showed that the introduction of graphene oxide (GO) not only enlarged the layer spacing and improved electrical conductivity, providing spacious channels for Zn2+ (de)intercalation and accelerating the ion diffusion dynamics, but also induced more oxygen vacancies, inhibited the dissolution of vanadium, and reduced self-discharging, offering additional and stable active sites for ion storage. The optimized NVOH@GO electrode delivered extraordinarily stable capacities of 334 mAh·g−1 after 2000 cycles at 5 A·g−1 and 238 mAh·g−1 after 10,000 cycles at 20 A·g−1. Furthermore, ex-situ X-ray diffraction (XRD), X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy (XPS), and Raman results systematically revealed the electrochemical mechanism, including a phase transition reaction and subsequent Zn2+/H2O co-(de)intercalation process. This study provides an effective strategy for expanding the interlayer spacing, inducing defect engineering, and enhancing the structural stability of vanadium-based cathodes for Zn-ion batteries and other multivalent aqueous ion batteries.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Liu, Gui-Long","Zhang, Ting","Li, Xiao-Jie","Cao, Ru-Ping","Shen, Ji-Ke","Guo, Dong-Lei","Wu, Nai-Teng","Yuan, Wei-Wei","Cao, Ang","Liu, Xian-Ming"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-700944"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Guo, Dong-Lei","Liu, Xian-Ming"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Luoyang Normal University"],"keyword":["Oxygen defects","Phase transition"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"oxygen deficient ammonium vanadate go composites with suppressed vanadium dissolution for ultra stable high rate aqueous zinc ion batteries","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85171151353","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-700944","identifier":[{"id":"001065277900001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85171151353","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-7d91b21b-3d2a-4954-bf9f-5a99c28c6226"],"keyword":["Aqueous Zn-ion batteries","Dissolution restraint","Oxygen defects","Phase transition","Vanadium-based cathode"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-64EE1C23FDA84B7348ABABD7023B7E03"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"luoyang normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Luoyang Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Catalysis Theory Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gui-Long","key":"liuguilongpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Gui-Long","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ting","key":"zhangtingpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Ting","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao-Jie","key":"lixiaojiepau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao-Jie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ru-Ping","key":"caorupingpau","last":"Cao","name":"Cao, Ru-Ping","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ji-Ke","key":"shenjikepau","last":"Shen","name":"Shen, Ji-Ke","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dong-Lei","key":"guodongleipau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Dong-Lei","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nai-Teng","key":"wunaitengpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Nai-Teng","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei-Wei","key":"yuanweiweipau","last":"Yuan","name":"Yuan, Wei-Wei","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ang","key":"caoangpau","last":"Cao","locid":"bcb0a893-26f0-4e9c-84d6-ec895a5d3a7b","name":"Cao, Ang","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xian-Ming","key":"liuxianmingpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Xian-Ming","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s12598-023-02364-3","issn":["10010521"],"journal":"Rare Metals","pages":"3729-3740","publisher":"Springer International Publishing","status":"p","title":"Rare Metals","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85171151353"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7d91b21b-3d2a-4954-bf9f-5a99c28c6226"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Oxygen-deficient ammonium vanadate/GO composites with suppressed vanadium dissolution for ultra-stable high-rate aqueous zinc-ion batteries","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-700944","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Global eutrophication and climate warming exacerbate production of cyanotoxins such as microcystins (MCs), presenting risks to human and animal health. Africa is a continent suffering from severe environmental crises, including MC intoxication, but with very limited understanding of the occurrence and extent of MCs. By analysing 90 publications from 1989 to 2019, we found that in various water bodies where MCs have been detected so far, the concentrations were 1.4–2803 times higher than the WHO provisional guideline for human lifetime exposure via drinking water (1 µg/L) in 12 of 15 African countries where data were available. MCs were relatively high in the Republic of South Africa (averaged 2803 μg/L) and Southern Africa as a whole (702 μg/L) when compared to other regions. Values were higher in reservoirs (958 μg/L) and lakes (159 μg/L) than in other water types, and much higher in temperate (1381 μg/L) than in arid (161 μg/L) and tropical (4 μg/L) zones. Highly significant positive relationships were found between MCs and planktonic chlorophyll a. Further assessment revealed high ecological risk for 14 of the 56 water bodies, with half used as human drinking water sources. Recognizing the extremely high MCs and exposure risk in Africa, we recommend routine monitoring and risk assessment of MCs be prioritized to ensure safe water use and sustainability in this region.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Zhao, Xu","Liu, Ying","Guo, Yu Ming","Xu, Chi","Chen, Liang","Codd, Geoffrey A.","Chen, Jun","Wang, Ying","Wang, Pu Ze","Yang, Li Wei","Zhou, Long","Li, Yan","Xiao, Shi Man","Wang, Hai Jun","Paerl, Hans W.","Jeppesen, Erik","Xie, Ping"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-146277"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Wang, Hai Jun"],"country":["Australia","China","Turkey","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Institute of Hydrobiology","Middle East Technical University","Monash University","Nanjing University","Sino-Danish Centre for Education and Research","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","University of Dundee","University of North Carolina","University of Stirling","Yunnan University"],"keyword":["Africa","Climatic zones","Exposure risk","Inland waters","Microcystins"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"meta analysis reveals cyanotoxins risk across african inland waters","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jhazmat.2023.131160","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-146277","identifier":[{"id":"85149758724","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36907061","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-1d99c5f8-8e35-4f3c-8548-6986f1da6c1f"],"keyword":["Africa","Climatic zones","Exposure risk","Inland waters","Microcystins","Water types"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-99C06F0117E83C0D9D03444BB31A9F6E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/407019598/1-s2.0-S0304389423004429-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jhazmat.2023.131160","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"yunnan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Yunnan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"monash university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Monash University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"nanjing university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanj