ournal of Hazardous Materials","paperid":"131160","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Hazardous Materials","volume":"451"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85149758724"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1d99c5f8-8e35-4f3c-8548-6986f1da6c1f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Meta-analysis reveals cyanotoxins risk across African inland waters","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-146277","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Three-phase current source rectifier is concerned due to its flexible output voltage regulation, high reliability, and fast dynamic response. Excessive voltage stress on the switch will increase the cost of the rectifier and reduce the reliability of the system. Therefore, it is essential to optimize the voltage stress on the switch. In this letter, the voltage stress of the switch caused by each current vector in space vector modulation (SVM) is analyzed. Then, the vectors with low-voltage stress are selected for combination to reduce the voltage stress of the switch without changing the topology. In addition, the vectors are reoptimized considering the effects of displacement angle. The reoptimized SVM can reduce the voltage stress by up to 13% under the leading or lagging power factor operation. Furthermore, the dc-link current ripple and modulation index range of different modulation methods are compared, and the effectiveness of the proposed modulation schemes are verified by experiments.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Wei, Yupeng","Guo, Xiaoqiang","Lu, Zhigang","Hua, Changchun","Blaabjerg, Frede"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-673726"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Yanshan University"],"keyword":["Current source rectifier CSR","Space vector modulation SVM","Voltage stress"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of space vector selection and input displacement angle on switch voltage stress of current source rectifier","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85148427738&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-673726","identifier":[{"id":"85148427738","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-69b08c2b-71f6-42ee-8c9d-10dc17b6ca37"],"keyword":["Current source rectifier (CSR)","space vector modulation (SVM)","the displacement angle","voltage stress"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-47DACB5D1CCC1E483F03065E4FD67345"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"yanshan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Yanshan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Applied Power Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, E-Mobility and Drives","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, EMI/EMC in Power Electronics","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Electric Power Systems and Microgrids","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Photovoltaic Systems","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Control, Reliability and System Optimization","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Wind Power Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yupeng","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Yupeng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoqiang","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Xiaoqiang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhigang","key":"lupau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Zhigang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Changchun","key":"huapau","last":"Hua","name":"Hua, Changchun","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frede","key":"blaabjergpau","last":"Blaabjerg","locid":"22b09e36-1f7b-4d33-90bf-918730e1d09a","name":"Blaabjerg, Frede","orcid":"0000-0001-8311-7412","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tpel.2023.3241578","issn":["08858993","19410107"],"issn_org":["08858993"],"issue":"5","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Power Electronics","pages":"5675-5679","paperid":"10035517","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Power Electronics","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Power Electronics","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85148427738"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-69b08c2b-71f6-42ee-8c9d-10dc17b6ca37"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Impact of Space Vector Selection and Input Displacement Angle on Switch Voltage Stress of Current Source Rectifier","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-673726","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"There is a significant interest in identifying blood-borne factors that mediate tissue crosstalk and function as molecular effectors of physical activity. Although past studies have focused on an individual molecule or cell type, the organism-wide secretome response to physical activity has not been evaluated. Here, we use a cell-type-specific proteomic approach to generate a 21-cell-type, 10-tissue map of exercise training-regulated secretomes in mice. Our dataset identifies >200 exercise training-regulated cell-type-secreted protein pairs, the majority of which have not been previously reported. Pdgfra-cre-labeled secretomes were the most responsive to exercise training. Finally, we show anti-obesity, anti-diabetic, and exercise performance-enhancing activities for proteoforms of intracellular carboxylesterases whose secretion from the liver is induced by exercise training.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Wei, Wei","Riley, Nicholas M.","Lyu, Xuchao","Shen, Xiaotao","Guo, Jing","Raun, Steffen Henning","Zhao, Meng","Moya-Garzon, Maria Dolores","Basu, Himanish","Sheng-Hwa Tung, Alan","Li, Veronica L.","Huang, Wentao","Wiggenhorn, Amanda L.","Svensson, Katrin J.","Snyder, Michael P.","Bertozzi, Carolyn R.","Long, Jonathan Z."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-677603"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard University","Massachusetts Institute of Technology","Stanford University","Whitehead Institute for Biomedical Research"],"keyword":["Energy Metabolism","Exercise","Exercise performance","Hepatokine","Obesity","Secretome","Tissue crosstalk","cell type"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"organism wide cell type specific secretome mapping of exercise training in mice","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/399348786/Organism_wide.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-677603","identifier":[{"id":"85163155389","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37141889","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10524249","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-146eef57-25a0-4b74-916f-ccfeea1e681e"],"keyword":["CES2","cell type","energy metabolism","exercise","exercise performance","hepatokine","obesity","secretome","tissue crosstalk"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C9F168359ED47C10A015630339487CAD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/399348786/Organism_wide.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Molecular Metabolism in Cancer and Ageing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"whitehead institute for biomedical research","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Whitehead Institute for Biomedical Research","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"massachusetts institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology"