{"abstract":"The problems of energy shortage, severe pollution, and global warming are becoming increasingly severe. Renewable energy systems with hydrogen have been widely used. In recent years, much literature has described the energy management of renewable energy systems with hydrogen in a comprehensive way. However, most of them are proposed and discussed from an academic point of view. There are likewise several different approaches and ideas in the patents that address the energy management of hydrogen renewable energy systems. Moreover, most patents are oriented toward industrial applications and still need to be reviewed and analyzed. To fill this gap, this paper reviews relevant US patents to find potential and industrial hydrogen applications and energy management strategies in renewable energy systems. The work presented in this paper will provide solutions and guidance in solving energy management problems in renewable energy systems.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Zhang, Shiqi","Wei, Yupeng","Guo, Xiaoqiang","Li, Zheng","Song, Xiaofei","Blaabjerg, Frede"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-673623"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Guo, Xiaoqiang"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Yanshan University"],"keyword":["Electrolyser","Energy management","Fuel cell","Hydrogen","Renewable energy systems","US Patents"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"overview of us patents for energy management of renewable energy systems with hydrogen","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85145691267&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-673623","identifier":[{"id":"85145691267","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-4e26e80b-adb4-4dea-85ca-5b14c5036b81"],"keyword":["Electrolyser","Energy management","Fuel cell","Hydrogen","Renewable energy systems","US patents"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BEEC5803BC43EB194D439E5C6AB15FDC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"yanshan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Yanshan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Applied Power Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, E-Mobility and Drives","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, EMI/EMC in Power Electronics","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Electric Power Systems and Microgrids","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Photovoltaic Systems","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Control, Reliability and System Optimization","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Wind Power Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shiqi","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Shiqi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yupeng","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Yupeng","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoqiang","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Xiaoqiang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zheng","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Zheng","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaofei","key":"songpau","last":"Song","name":"Song, Xiaofei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frede","key":"blaabjergpau","last":"Blaabjerg","locid":"22b09e36-1f7b-4d33-90bf-918730e1d09a","name":"Blaabjerg, Frede","orcid":"0000-0001-8311-7412","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijhydene.2022.12.091","issn":["03603199","18793487"],"issn_org":["03603199"],"issue":"26","journal":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","pages":"9574-9591","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Hydrogen Energy","volume":"48"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85145691267"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4e26e80b-adb4-4dea-85ca-5b14c5036b81"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Overview of US patents for energy management of renewable energy systems with hydrogen","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-673623","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Energy homeostasis is essential for the adaptation of animals to their environment and some wild animals keep low metabolism adaptive to their low-nutrient dietary supply. Giant panda is such a typical low-metabolic mammal exhibiting species specialization of extremely low daily energy expenditure. It has low levels of basal metabolic rate, thyroid hormone, and physical activities, whereas the cellular bases of its low metabolic adaptation remain rarely explored. RESULTS: In this study, we generate a single-nucleus transcriptome atlas of 21 organs/tissues from a female giant panda. We focused on the central metabolic organ (liver) and dissected cellular metabolic status by cross-species comparison. Adaptive expression mode (i.e., AMPK related) was prominently displayed in the hepatocyte of giant panda. In the highest energy-consuming organ, the heart, we found a possibly optimized utilization of fatty acid. Detailed cell subtype annotation of endothelial cells showed the uterine-specific deficiency of blood vascular subclasses, indicating a potential adaptation for a low reproductive energy expenditure. CONCLUSIONS: Our findings shed light on the possible cellular basis and transcriptomic regulatory clues for the low metabolism in giant pandas and helped to understand physiological adaptation response to nutrient stress.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Yang, Shangchen","Lan, Tianming","Wei, Rongping","Lin, Lin","Du, Hanyu","Huang, Yunting","Zhang, Guiquan","Huang, Shan","Shi, Minhui","Wang, Chengdong","Li, Rengui","Han, Lei","Tang, Dan","Li, Haimeng","Zhang, Hemin","Cui, Jie","Lu, Haorong","Huang, Jinrong","Luo, Yonglun","Li, Desheng","Wan, Qiu-Hong","Liu, Huan","Fang, Sheng-Guo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-699393"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Fang, Sheng-Guo","Li, Desheng","Liu, Huan","Wan, Qiu-Hong"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI-Shenzhen","China Agricultural University","China National GeneBank","Northeast Forestry University","Qingdao-Europe Advanced Institute for Life Sciences","Zhejiang Gongshang University"],"keyword":["Adaptation","Animals","Animals Wild","Endothelial Cells","Energy homeostasis","Exercise","Female","Giant panda","Transcriptome","Ursidae genetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"single nucleus transcriptome inventory of giant panda reveals cellular basis for fitness optimization under low metabolism","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12915-023-01691-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-699393","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10588165","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37858133","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85174548121","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-310fc015-a7e2-41af-9c75-551e4490c4b3"],"keyword":["Adaptation","Animals","Animals, Wild","Endothelial Cells","Energy homeostasis","Exercise","Female","Giant panda","Low metabolism","Single-nucleus transcriptome atlas","Transcriptome","Ursidae/genetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4514E336F24B07FA22BE589510F97D85"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12915-023-01691-2","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang gongshang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang Gongshang University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"china agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT",