Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7f52c43b-bd79-4b7f-9d80-afa7714cfd2e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The Seventeenth Data Release of the Sloan Digital Sky Surveys : Complete Release of MaNGA, MaStar, and APOGEE-2 Data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-202175","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Ruminants digest plant biomass more efficiently than monogastric animals due to their symbiotic relationship with a complex microbiota residing in the rumen environment. What remains unclear is the relationship between the rumen microbial taxonomic and functional composition and feed efficiency (FE), especially in crossbred dairy cattle (Holstein x Gyr) raised under tropical conditions. In this study, we selected twenty-two F1 Holstein x Gyr heifers and grouped them according to their residual feed intake (RFI) ranking, high efficiency (HE) (n = 11) and low efficiency (LE) (n = 11), to investigate the effect of FE on the rumen microbial taxa and their functions. Rumen fluids were collected using a stomach tube apparatus and analyzed using amplicon sequencing targeting the 16S (bacteria and archaea) and 18S (protozoa) rRNA genes. Alpha-diversity and beta-diversity analysis revealed no significant difference in the rumen microbiota between the HE and LE animals. Multivariate analysis (sPLS-DA) showed a clear separation of two clusters in bacterial taxonomic profiles related to each FE group, but in archaeal and protozoal profiles, the clusters overlapped. The sPLS-DA also revealed a clear separation in functional profiles for bacteria, archaea, and protozoa between the HE and LE animals. Microbial taxa were differently related to HE (e.g., Howardella and Shuttleworthia) and LE animals (e.g., Eremoplastron and Methanobrevibacter), and predicted functions were significatively different for each FE group (e.g., K03395—signaling and cellular process was strongly related to HE animals, and K13643—genetic information processing was related to LE animals). This study demonstrates that differences in the rumen microbiome relative to FE ranking are not directly observed from diversity indices (Faith’s Phylogenetic Diversity, Pielou’s Evenness, Shannon’s diversity, weighted UniFrac distance, Jaccard index, and Bray–Curtis dissimilarity), but from targeted identification of specific taxa and microbial functions characterizing each FE group. These results shed light on the role of rumen microbial taxonomic and functional profiles in crossbred Holstein × Gyr dairy cattle raised in tropical conditions, creating the possibility of using the microbial signature of the HE group as a biological tool for the development of biomarkers that improve FE in ruminants.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Fregulia, Priscila","Campos, Mariana Magalhães","Dias, Roberto Júnio Pedroso","Liu, Junhong","Guo, Wei","Pereira, Luiz Gustavo Ribeiro","Machado, Marco Antônio","Faza, Daniele Ribeiro de Lima Reis","Guan, Le Luo","Garnsworthy, Phil C.","Alves Neves, Andre Luis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-443634"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Brazil","Canada","China","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Brazilian Agricultural Research Corporation","Guizhou University","Universidade Federal de Juiz de Fora","University of Alberta","University of Nottingham"],"keyword":["RFI","Rumen microbiome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"taxonomic and predicted functional signatures reveal linkages between the rumen microbiota and feed efficiency in dairy cattle raised in tropical areas","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2022.1025173","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-443634","identifier":[{"id":"85143905669","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36523842","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9745175","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-5411db7e-a268-4174-bfca-546df99bb1aa"],"keyword":["RFI","SSU rRNA","functional microbial composition","rumen microbiome","taxonomic microbial composition"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-02DEF71DB7C43A21B20CAC2DF66F7FD8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/330935377/fmicb_13_1025173.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2022.1025173","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"br","key":"universidade federal de juiz de fora","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"Universidade Federal de Juiz de Fora","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"br","key":"brazilian agricultural research corporation","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"Brazilian Agricultural Research Corporation","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"university of alberta","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Alberta","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"guizhou university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Guizhou University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"university of nottingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Nottingham","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Production, Nutrition and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Priscila","key":"freguliapau","last":"Fregulia","name":"Fregulia, Priscila","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mariana Magalhães","key":"campospau","last":"Campos","name":"Campos, Mariana Magalhães","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Roberto Júnio Pedroso","key":"diaspau","last":"Dias","name":"Dias, Roberto Júnio Pedroso","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Junhong","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Junhong","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Wei","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Wei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Luiz Gustavo Ribeiro","key":"pereirapau","last":"Pereira","name":"Pereira, Luiz Gustavo Ribeiro","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marco Antônio","key":"machadopau","last":"Machado","name":"Machado, Marco Antônio","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Daniele Ribeiro de Lima Reis","key":"fazapau","last":"Faza","name":"Faza, Daniele Ribeiro de Lima Reis","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Le Luo","key":"guanpau","last":"Guan","name":"Guan, Le Luo","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Phil C.","key":"garnsworthypau","last":"Garnsworthy","name":"Garnsworthy, Phil C.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"André Luis Alves","key":"nevespau","last":"Neves","locid":"381f5fae-b9b0-439f-b5e2-85888508aabe","name":"Alves Neves, Andre Luis","name_org":"Neves, André Luis Alves","orcid":"0000-0002-2617-6210","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36523842"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fmicb.2022.1025173","issn":["1664302X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Microbiology","paperid":"1025173","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Microbiology","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85143905669"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5411db7e-a268-4174-bfca-546df99bb1aa"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Taxonomic and predicted functional signatures reveal linkages between the rumen microbiota and feed efficiency in dairy cattle raised in tropical areas","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-443634","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Mammalian cortical interneurons (CINs) could be classified into more than two dozen cell types that possess diverse electrophysiological and molecular characteristics, and participate in various essential biological processes in the human neural system. However, the mechanism to generate diversity in CINs remains controversial. This study aims to predict CIN diversity in mouse embryo by using single-cell transcriptomics and the machine learning methods. Data of 2,669 single-cell transcriptome sequencing results are employed. The 2,669 cells are classified into three categories, caudal ganglionic eminence (CGE) cells, dorsal medial ganglionic eminence (dMGE) cells, and ventral medial ganglionic eminence (vMGE) cells, corresponding to the three regions in the mouse subpallium where the cells are collected. Such transcriptomic profiles were first analyzed by the minimum redundancy and maximum relevance method. A feature list was obtained, which was further fed into the incremental feature selection, incorporating two classification algorithms (random forest and repeated incremental pruning to produce error reduction), to extract key genes and construct powerful classifiers and classification rules. The optimal classifier could achieve an MCC of 0.725, and category-specified prediction accuracies of 0.958, 0.760, and 0.737 for the CGE, dMGE, and vMGE cells, respectively. The related genes and rules may provide helpful information for deepening the understanding of CIN diversity.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Li, Zhandong","Wang, Deling","Guo, Wei","Zhang, ShiQi","Chen, Lei","Zhang, Yu-Hang","Lu, Lin","Pan, XiaoYong","Huang, Tao","Cai, Yu-Dong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-456663"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","NewYork-Presbyterian Brooklyn Methodist Hospital","Shanghai Jiao Tong University","Shanghai Maritime University","Sun Yat-Sen University","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Embryo","Expression","Generation","Kinase","Machine learning","PAX3","Pathway","Receptor"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Jilin Engineering Normal University"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identification of cortical interneuron cell markers in mouse embryos based on machine learning analysis of single cell transcriptomics","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fnins.2022.841145","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-456663","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9337837","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85135153936","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000834253300001","type":"wos"},{"id":"35911980","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-69db0cb9-9b30-4aba-a019-86e97b1c2a93"],"keyword":["EXPRESSION","GENERATION","KINASE","LHX8","PATHWAY","PAX3","RECEPTOR","cortical interneuron diversity","embryo","ganglionic eminences","machine learning","rule learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F60B2FC4CE5704D9EA4AF2FA53AD0DF6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/315708524/fnins_16_841145.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fnins.2022.841145","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Jilin Engineering Normal Unive