{"abstract":"Octenyl succinate anhydride (OSA) modified high amylose maize starch (HAMS) showed limited emulsion stability due to the OSA groups were located on the surface of starch granules. However, amylose is enriched in the internal region of HAMS and provides the reaction site for OSA groups. In this study, five types of starches with different amylose content were prepared using optimized reaction conditions. Our data showed that amylose content (AC) was the most important parameter controlling the degree of substitution (DS), in comparison with temperature, pH, starch concentration and time. DS reached a maximum (2.1%) at AC of 58%. Importantly, OSA groups were mainly located in the internal regions of HAMS under the optimized reaction conditions. This was supported by (1) the decrease of the crystallinity, (2) the weaker fluorescence intensity of the starch fluorophore probe 8-amino-1,3,6-pyrenetrisulfonic acid (APTS) in the internal regions of HAMS, and (3) unchanged signals from Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy which characterized the granular surface structure ordering. This new OSA reaction pattern permits HAMS to be used in stabilizing Pickering emulsions This is the first report that OSA groups located in the internal regions of HAMS granules.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Li, Jinyuan","Wang, Qian","Blennow, Andreas","Herburger, Klaus","Zhu, Chuanhao","Nurzikhan, Seitkali","Wei, Jiangpeng","Zhong, Yuyue","Guo, Dongwei"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-477560"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Central","Asia, East"],"country":["China","Kazakhstan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Kazakh National Agricultural Research University","Ltd.","Northwest University"],"keyword":["Emulsion","High amylose starch","Orthogonal test","Surface modification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the location of octenyl succinate anhydride groups in high amylose maize starch granules and its effect on stability of pickering emulsion stability","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.lwt.2022.113892","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-477560","identifier":[{"id":"85138090862","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000867685300003","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-8caba2a2-b695-4ece-9a67-e909696a6da8"],"keyword":["Emulsion","High amylose starch","Matrix modification","Orthogonal test","Surface modification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BB611668D8770019237FD84F726C2339"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/323194304/1_s2.0_S0023643822008271_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.lwt.2022.113892","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"northwest university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northwest University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Plant Glycobiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"kz","key":"kazakh national agricultural research university","loc":["Kazakhstan","Asia, Central"],"name":"Kazakh National Agricultural Research University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"ltd","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Ltd.","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jinyuan","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Jinyuan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Qian","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Qian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Andreas","key":"blennowpau","last":"Blennow","locid":"3c313f25-a5e5-4c67-88dd-dcf21d2a4120","name":"Blennow, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0001-6476-9546","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Klaus","key":"herburgerpau","last":"Herburger","locid":"57274f7a-cdb9-413c-9791-2088342d6a14","name":"Herburger, Klaus","orcid":"0000-0001-8014-0844","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chuanhao","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Chuanhao","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Seitkali","key":"nurzikhanpau","last":"Nurzikhan","name":"Nurzikhan, Seitkali","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Jiangpeng","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Jiangpeng","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yuyue","key":"zhongpau","last":"Zhong","locid":"1ddc08ab-54ae-457e-9133-e19bf9ffcaf2","name":"Zhong, Yuyue","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dongwei","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Dongwei","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.lwt.2022.113892","issn":["00236438","10961127"],"issn_org":["00236438"],"journal":"LWT","paperid":"113892","status":"p","title":"LWT","volume":"169"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85138090862"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8caba2a2-b695-4ece-9a67-e909696a6da8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The location of octenyl succinate anhydride groups in high-amylose maize starch granules and its effect on stability of pickering emulsion stability","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-477560","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The fall armyworm (FAW), Spodoptera frugiperda, is a destructive pest native to America and has recently become an invasive insect pest in China. Because of its rapid spread and great risks in China, understanding of FAW genetic background and pesticide resistance is urgent and essential to develop effective management strategies. Here, we assembled a chromosome-level genome of a male FAW (SFynMstLFR) and compared re-sequencing results of the populations from America, Africa, and China. Strain identification of 163 individuals collected from America, Africa and China showed that both C and R strains were found in the American populations, while only C strain was found in the Chinese and African populations. Moreover, population genomics analysis showed that populations from Africa and China have close relationship with significantly genetic differentiation from American populations. Taken together, FAWs invaded into China were most likely originated from Africa. Comparative genomics analysis displayed that the cytochrome p450 gene family is extremely expanded to 425 members in FAW, of which 283 genes are specific to FAW. Treatments of Chinese populations with twenty-three pesticides showed the variant patterns of transcriptome profiles, and several detoxification genes such as AOX, UGT and GST specially responded to the pesticides. These findings will be useful in developing effective strategies for management of FAW in China and other invaded areas.","author_count":44,"contributors":["Gui, Furong","Lan, Tianming","Zhao, Yue","Guo, Wei","Dong, Yang","Fang, Dongming","Liu, Huan","Li, Haimeng","Wang, Hongli","Hao, Ruoshi","Cheng, Xiaofang","Li, Yahong","Yang, Pengcheng","Sahu, Sunil Kumar","Chen, Yaping","Cheng, Le","He, Shuqi","Liu, Ping","Fan, Guangyi","Lu, Haorong","Hu, Guohai","Dong, Wei","Chen, Bin","Jiang, Yuan","Zhang, Yongwei","Xu, Hanhong","Lin, Fei","Slippers, Bernard","Postma, Alisa","Jackson, Matthew","Abate, Birhan Addisie","Tesfaye, Kassahun","Demie, Aschalew Lemma","Bayeleygne, Meseret Destaw","Degefu, Dawit Tesfaye","Chen, Feng","Kuria, Paul K.","Kinyua, Zachary M.","Liu, Tong-Xian","Yang, Huanming","Huang, Fangneng","Liu, Xin","Sheng, Jun","Kang, Le"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-505783"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","Ethiopia","Kenya","South Africa","United States"],"glorg":["Addis Ababa University","All Global Affiliations","BGI","China National GeneBank","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Ethiopian Biotechnology Institute","Ethiopian Institute of Agricultural Research","Guangdong Provincial Key Laboratory of Genome Read and Write","Kenya Agricultural and Livestock Research Organization","Louisiana State University","Qingdao Agricultural University","South China Agricultural University","State Key Laboratory of Agricultural Genomics","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","University of Pretoria","Yunnan Agriculture University","Yunnan Plant Protection and Quarantine Station"],"keyword":["Chromosome level genome","Cytochrome P450","DNA","Expression","Format","LEPIDOPTERA NOCTUIDAE","Pesticides","Plants","Population differentiation","SUPERFAMILY","Spodoptera frugiperda"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genomic and transcriptomic analysis unveils population evolution and development of pesticide resistance in fall armyworm i spodoptera frugiperda i","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s13238-020-00795-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-505783","identifier":[{"id":"000582768400001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85094598945","type":"scopus"},{"id":"