{"abstract":"Transformerless inverters are used in small and medium power photovoltaic grid-connected systems due to small-size, low-cost and high-efficiency. Transformerless inverters have problems of leakage current and low-voltage gain in applications due to the lack of electrical isolation and boost characteristics of transformers. According to these problems, this paper introduces a gain unit circuit in the front-stage based on the two-stage topology of Boost converter combined with the H-bridge inverter to improve the boost capability. The rear-stage adopts double Buck inverter, which has the ability to prevent the short circuit of the bridge arms and improves the reliability of the system. At the same time, it is ensured that there is no high-frequency component in the parasitic capacitance voltage, and the leakage current is suppressed. In this paper, the operational modes, circuit gain and devices stress of the proposed inverter are analyzed, and the simulation verified the feasibility of the scheme.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Wei, Yupeng","Guo, Xiaoqiang","Zhang, Zhe","Wang, Lichong","Guerrero, Josep M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-667311"],"event":{"end":"2022-12-12","place":"Beijing, cn","start":"2022-12-09","title":"4th International Conference on Smart Power and Internet Energy Systems, SPIES 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Wei, Yupeng"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Shenke Electronic Co.","Yanshan University"],"keyword":["Grid connected inverter","High voltage gain","Leakage current","two stage converter"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a high voltage gain transformerless grid connected inverter","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85153400298&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported in part by National Natural Science Foundation of China under Grant 52077190, Central for Local Science and Technology Development Program under Grant 226Z4504G, and Hebei Province Natural Science Foundation under Grant F2020203013."],"id":"S01-000.00-667311","identifier":[{"id":"85153400298","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-6d176e77-8e99-4001-b741-3c1dfe1e76e1"],"keyword":["grid-connected inverter","high-voltage gain","leakage current","nonisolated inverter","two-stage converter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E023B0429D6E3F9BD447872C0D749284"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"yanshan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Yanshan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"shenke electronic co","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shenke Electronic Co.","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Center for Research on Microgrids​","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Electric Power Systems and Microgrids"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yupeng","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Yupeng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoqiang","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Xiaoqiang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhe","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Zhe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lichong","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Lichong","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Josep M.","key":"guerreropau","last":"Guerrero","locid":"07d2eed6-2177-4f61-b812-a08c55b2e8af","name":"Guerrero, Josep M.","orcid":"0000-0001-5236-4592","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/spies55999.2022.10082633","eisbn":["9781665489577"],"isbn":["9781665489560","9781665489584"],"pages":"533-536","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"2022 4th International Conference on Smart Power and Internet Energy Systems, SPIES 2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85153400298"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6d176e77-8e99-4001-b741-3c1dfe1e76e1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A High-Voltage Gain Transformerless Grid-Connected Inverter","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-667311","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Online distillation attracts attention from the community as it simplifies the traditional two-stage knowledge distillation process into a single stage. Online distillation collaboratively trains a group of peer models, which are treated as students, and all students gain extra knowledge from each other. However, memory consumption and diversity among students are two key challenges to the scalability and quality of online distillation. To address the two challenges, this paper presents a framework called Weighted Mutual Learning with Diversity-Driven Model Compression (WML) for online distillation. First, at the base of a hierarchical structure where students share different parts, we leverage the structured network pruning to generate diversified students with different models sizes, thus also helping reduce the memory requirements. Second, rather than taking the average of students, this paper, for the first time, leverages a bi-level formulation to estimate the relative importance of students with a close-form, to further boost the effectiveness of the distillation from each other. Extensive experiments show the generalization of the proposed framework, which outperforms existing online distillation methods on a variety of deep neural networks. More interesting, as a byproduct, WML produces a series of students with different model sizes in a single run, which also achieves competitive results compared with existing channel pruning methods.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Zhang, Miao","Wang, Li","Campos, David","Huang, Wei","Guo, Chenjuan","Yang, Bin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-681794"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Shandong First Medical University & Shandong Academy of Medical Sciences","University of New South Wales"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"weighted mutual learning with diversity driven model compression","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2022/file/4b25c000967af9036fb9b207b198a626-Paper-Conference.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-681794","ids":["aau-53fbac2e-ceb7-45aa-a8cb-94df7cb577d5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3F2768519BFA4F924923B07D2CBB4EDE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2022/file/4b25c000967af9036fb9b207b198a626-Paper-Conference.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Database and Web Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"shandong first medical university shandong academy of medical sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong First Medical University & Shandong Academy of Medical Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"university of new south wales","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of New South Wales","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Miao","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"f747736e-31bb-483f-9836-73b54bcf3544","name":"Zhang, Miao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Li","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Li","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"David","key":"campospau","last":"Campos","locid":"ec36d6b8-05a1-4eec-9603-56b60bd53cf6","name":"Campos, David","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Wei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Chenjuan","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","locid":"036ea733-d9ad-489e-95ff-0fa24c03e803","name":"Guo, Chenjuan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bin","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","locid":"b7f7782f-010a-4656-b02d-55ef4a3d2072","name":"Yang, Bin","orcid":"0000-0002-1658-1079","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-53fbac2e-ceb7-45aa-a8cb-94df7cb577d5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Weighted Mutual Learning with Diversity-Driven Model Compression.","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-681794","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Suicide is a leading cause of death worldwide, and nonfatal suicide attempts, which occur far more frequently, are a major source of disability and social and economic burden. Both have substantial genetic etiology, which is partially shared and partially distinct from that of related psychiatric disorders. METHODS: We conducted a genome-wide association study (GWAS) of 29,782 suicide attempt (SA) cases and 519,961 controls in the International Suicide Genetics Consortium (ISGC). The GWAS of SA was conditioned on psychiatric disorders using GWAS summary statistics via multitrait-based conditional and joint analysis, to remove genetic effects on SA mediated by psychiatric disorders. We investigated the shared and divergent genetic architectures of SA, psychiatric disorders, and other known risk factors. RESULTS: Two loci reached genome-wide significance for SA: the major histocompatibility complex and an intergenic locus on chromosome 7, the latter of which remained associated with SA after conditioning on psychiatric disorders and replicated in an independent cohort from the Million Veteran Program. This locus has been implicated in risk-taking behavior, smoking, and insomnia. SA showed strong genetic correlation with psychiatric disorders, particularly major depression, and also with smoking, pain, risk-taking behavior, sleep disturbances, lower educational attainment, reproductive traits, lower socioeconomic status, and poorer general health. After conditioning on psychiatric disorders, the genetic correlations between SA and psychiatric disorders decreased, whereas those with nonpsychiatric traits remained largely unchanged. CONCLUSIONS: Our results identify a risk locus that contributes more strongly to SA than other phenotypes and suggest a shared underlying biology between SA and known risk factors that is not mediated by psychiatric disorders.","author_count":59,"contributors":["Mullins, Niamh","Kang, Joo Eun","Campos, Adrian I.","Col