:"pau"},{"affno":"7 16 17","first":"Yves","key":"vandepeeryvespau","last":"Van de Peer","name":"Van de Peer, Yves","rank":40,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Catherine","key":"kidnercatherinepau","last":"Kidner","name":"Kidner, Catherine","rank":41,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Shouzhou","key":"zhangshouzhoupau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Shouzhou","rank":42,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 13","first":"Huan","key":"liuhuanpau","last":"Liu","locid":"1798b485-54ff-41e1-bc73-9525213709c6","name":"Liu, Huan","rank":43,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34997964"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/nph.17949","issn":["0028646X","14698137"],"issn_org":["0028646X"],"issue":"1","journal":"New Phytologist","pages":"295-310","status":"p","title":"New Phytologist","volume":"234"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85124533435"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6b2d9f52-d4b0-4a8a-a3c9-df19a06a0982"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Genomes shed light on the evolution of <i>Begonia</i>, a mega-diverse genus","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-457425","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Spatially resolved transcriptomic technologies are promising tools to study complex biological processes such as mammalian embryogenesis. However, the imbalance between resolution, gene capture, and field of view of current methodologies precludes their systematic application to analyze relatively large and three-dimensional mid- and late-gestation embryos. Here, we combined DNA nanoball (DNB)-patterned arrays and in situ RNA capture to create spatial enhanced resolution omics-sequencing (Stereo-seq). We applied Stereo-seq to generate the mouse organogenesis spatiotemporal transcriptomic atlas (MOSTA), which maps with single-cell resolution and high sensitivity the kinetics and directionality of transcriptional variation during mouse organogenesis. We used this information to gain insight into the molecular basis of spatial cell heterogeneity and cell fate specification in developing tissues such as the dorsal midbrain. Our panoramic atlas will facilitate in-depth investigation of longstanding questions concerning normal and abnormal mammalian development.","author_count":69,"contributors":["Chen, Ao","Liao, Sha","Cheng, Mengnan","Ma, Kailong","Wu, Liang","Lai, Yiwei","Qiu, Xiaojie","Yang, Jin","Xu, Jiangshan","Hao, Shijie","Wang, Xin","Lu, Huifang","Chen, Xi","Liu, Xing","Huang, Xin","Li, Zhao","Hong, Yan","Jiang, Yujia","Peng, Jian","Liu, Shuai","Shen, Mengzhe","Liu, Chuanyu","Li, Quanshui","Yuan, Yue","Wei, Xiaoyu","Zheng, Huiwen","Feng, Weimin","Wang, Zhifeng","Liu, Yang","Wang, Zhaohui","Yang, Yunzhi","Xiang, Haitao","Han, Lei","Qin, Baoming","Guo, Pengcheng","Lai, Guangyao","Muñoz-Cánoves, Pura","Maxwell, Patrick H","Thiery, Jean Paul","Wu, Qing-Feng","Zhao, Fuxiang","Chen, Bichao","Li, Mei","Dai, Xi","Wang, Shuai","Kuang, Haoyan","Hui, Junhou","Wang, Liqun","Fei, Ji-Feng","Wang, Ou","Wei, Xiaofeng","Lu, Haorong","Wang, Bo","Liu, Shiping","Gu, Ying","Ni, Ming","Zhang, Wenwei","Mu, Feng","Yin, Ye","Yang, Huanming","Lisby, Michael","Cornall, Richard J","Mulder, Jan","Uhlén, Mathias","Esteban, Miguel A.","Li, Yuxiang","Liu, Longqi","Xu, Xun","Wang, Jian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-525497"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["China","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","China National GeneBank","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Guangdong Provincial Key Laboratory of Genome Read and Write","Guangzhou University of Chinese Medicine","Howard Hughes Medical Institute","Instituto de Salud Carlos III","James D. Watson Institute of Genome Sciences","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","Karolinska Institutet","Pompeu Fabra University","University of Cambridge","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","University of Oxford","Whitehead Institute for Biomedical Research","Zhengzhou University"],"keyword":["Animals","DNA genetics","Embryo Mammalian","Female","Gene Expression Profiling methods","Mammals genetics","Mice","Organogenesis genetics","Pregnancy","Sequence Analysis RNA methods","Single Cell Analysis methods","Transcriptome genetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Guangdong Academy of Medical Sciences"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"spatiotemporal transcriptomic atlas of mouse organogenesis using dna nanoball patterned arrays","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2022.04.003","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-525497","identifier":[{"id":"85129914359","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35512705","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-dd123904-163c-4267-bf46-c612c3bc3492"],"keyword":["Animals","DNA/genetics","Embryo,