{"abstract":"Sweet potato was planted at three soil and air temperatures (21, 25 and 28 °C) with the same humidity and light time/intensity. Root tuber starches were isolated, and their multi-scale structures were investigated to reveal the effects of growth temperature on starch properties. Growth temperature did not change the morphology and amylose content of starch, but markedly increased the size of starch from volume-weighted mean diameter 12.2 μm to 17.0 μm. Starch grown at high growth temperature exhibited less A branch-chains and lower branching degree of amylopectin and more B2 and B3+ branch-chains of amylopectin than at low growth temperature. With increasing growth temperature, starch changed from CC-type to CA-type, its relative crystallinity and lamellar peak intensity increased, and the thickness of crystalline and amorphous lamellae did not significantly change. Starch grown at high growth temperature exhibited significantly higher gelatinization temperature than at low growth temperature, but had similar gelatinization enthalpy.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Guo, Ke","Lin, Lingshang","Li, Enpeng","Zhong, Yuyue","Petersen, Bent Larsen","Blennow, Andreas","Bian, Xiaofeng","Wei, Cunxu"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-414690"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Jiangsu Academy of Agricultural Sciences","Yangzhou University"],"keyword":["Biosynthesis","Multi scale structure","Starch","Sweet potato"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of growth temperature on multi scale structure of root tuber starch in sweet potato","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-414690","identifier":[{"id":"85139026391","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000868946400001","type":"wos"},{"id":"36241302","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-239661f4-bd46-4e95-85df-e6c3ba4b7b95"],"keyword":["Biosynthesis","Growth temperature","Multi-scale structure","Starch","Sweet potato"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-543EBFD03A1594D9F536EE78BC52CD55"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Plant Glycobiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"yangzhou university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Yangzhou University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"jiangsu academy of agricultural sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jiangsu Academy of Agricultural Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Ke","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","locid":"e36bb2b8-9380-4f59-b922-9fa0a9ec106d","name":"Guo, Ke","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lingshang","key":"linpau","last":"Lin","name":"Lin, Lingshang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Enpeng","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Enpeng","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yuyue","key":"zhongpau","last":"Zhong","locid":"1ddc08ab-54ae-457e-9133-e19bf9ffcaf2","name":"Zhong, Yuyue","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bent Larsen","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"0d3fa717-88a9-444e-8096-3163ca10ec75","name":"Petersen, Bent Larsen","orcid":"0000-0002-2004-9077","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"blennowpau","last":"Blennow","locid":"3c313f25-a5e5-4c67-88dd-dcf21d2a4120","name":"Blennow, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0001-6476-9546","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Xiaofeng","key":"bianpau","last":"Bian","name":"Bian, Xiaofeng","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Cunxu","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Cunxu","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36241302"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.carbpol.2022.120136","issn":["01448617","18791344"],"issn_org":["01448617"],"journal":"Carbohydrate Polymers","paperid":"120136","status":"p","title":"Carbohydrate Polymers","volume":"298"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85139026391"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-239661f4-bd46-4e95-85df-e6c3ba4b7b95"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effects of growth temperature on multi-scale structure of root tuber starch in sweet potato","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-414690","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Ant colonies are higher-level organisms consisting of specialized reproductive and non-reproductive individuals that differentiate early in development, similar to germ–soma segregation in bilateral Metazoa. Analogous to diverging cell lines, developmental differentiation of individual ants has often been considered in epigenetic terms but the sets of genes that determine caste phenotypes throughout larval and pupal development remain unknown. Here, we reconstruct the individual developmental trajectories of two ant species, Monomorium pharaonis and Acromyrmex echinatior, after obtaining >1,400 whole-genome transcriptomes. Using a new backward prediction algorithm, we show that caste phenotypes can be accurately predicted by genome-wide transcriptome profiling. We find that caste differentiation is increasingly canalized from early development onwards, particularly in germline individuals (gynes/queens) and that the juvenile hormone signalling pathway plays a key role in this process by regulating body mass divergence between castes. We quantified gene-specific canalization levels and found that canalized genes with gyne/queen-biased expression were enriched for ovary and wing functions while canalized genes with worker-biased expression were enriched in brain and behavioural functions. Suppression in gyne larvae of Freja, a highly canalized gyne-biased ovary gene, disturbed pupal development by inducing non-adaptive intermediate phenotypes between gynes and workers. Our results are consistent with natural selection actively maintaining canalized caste phenotypes while securing robustness in the life cycle ontogeny of ant colonies.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Qiu, Bitao","Dai, Xueqin","Li, Panyi","Larsen, Rasmus Stenbak","Li, Ruyan","Price, Alivia Lee","Ding, Guo","Texada, Michael J.","Zhang, Xiafang","Zuo, Dashuang","Gao, Qionghua","Jiang, Wei","Wen, Tinggang","Pontieri, Luigi","Guo, Chunxue","Rewitz, Kim","Li, Qiye","Liu, Weiwei","Boomsma, Jacobus Jan","Zhang, Guojie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-531179"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Guangxi University","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","Zhejiang University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"canalized gene expression during development mediates caste differentiation in ants","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41559-022-01884-y","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-531179","identifier":[{"id":"36192540","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9630140","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85139265641","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e6a4f71a-aa30-489d-8e30-98d860e02ded"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-49A85EB53FC8E3C607BEEDE2E0DA292E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/326741214/s41559_022_01884_y.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41559-022-01884-y","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Ecology and Evolution"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country"