","name":"Zhang, Xiafang","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Dashuang","key":"zuodashuangpau","last":"Zuo","name":"Zuo, Dashuang","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","first":"Qionghua","key":"gaoqionghuapau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Qionghua","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Wei","key":"jiangweipau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Wei","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Tinggang","key":"wentinggangpau","last":"Wen","name":"Wen, Tinggang","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Luigi","key":"pontieriluigipau","last":"Pontieri","locid":"a1aab1ab-ca4c-459e-b8f6-9e57e45732f6","name":"Pontieri, Luigi","orcid":"0000-0002-1506-3827","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Chunxue","key":"guochunxuepau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Chunxue","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kim","key":"rewitzkimpau","last":"Rewitz","locid":"a6869192-bd30-4f96-8d90-25365a0bab3f","name":"Rewitz, Kim","orcid":"0000-0002-4409-9941","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","first":"Qiye","key":"liqiyepau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Qiye","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Weiwei","key":"liuweiweipau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Weiwei","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jacobus J.","key":"boomsmajacobusjanpau","last":"Boomsma","locid":"bf2786c8-6e04-4853-ba15-ced76aceb8aa","name":"Boomsma, Jacobus Jan","name_org":"Boomsma, Jacobus J.","orcid":"0000-0002-3598-1609","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 6","first":"Guojie","key":"zhangguojiepau","last":"Zhang","locid":"f5381bdc-b377-47a3-bdc0-4deccfda761c","name":"Zhang, Guojie","orcid":"0000-0001-6860-1521","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36192540"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41559-022-01884-y","issn":["2397334X"],"issue":"11","journal":"Nature Ecology & Evolution","pages":"1753-1765","status":"p","title":"Nature Ecology & Evolution","title_org":"Nature Ecology and Evolution","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85139265641"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e6a4f71a-aa30-489d-8e30-98d860e02ded"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Canalized gene expression during development mediates caste differentiation in ants","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-531179","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Soil fauna takes an active part in accelerating turnover of nutrients in terrestrial ecosystems. Anaerobic ammonium oxidation (anammox) has been widely characterized, however, whether anammox is active in earthworm gut and the effect of earthworm on anammox in soil remain unknown. In this study, the activity, abundance and community of anammox bacteria in earthworm guts and soils from microcosms were determined using a N-15-tracing technique, quantitative PCR, and anammox bacterial 16S rRNA gene amplicon sequencing. Results showed that anammox rates in guts ranged between 5.81 and 14.19 nmol N g(-1) dw gut content h(-1), which were significantly (P <0.01) higher than that in their surrounding soils during 30 day incubation. On the contrary, abundances of hzsB genes encoding subunit B hydrazine synthase in guts were significantly (P <0.05) lower than those in their surrounding soils. Anammox rates, denitrification N-2 production rates and hzsB genes in soils with earthworms were significantly (P <0.05) lower than those in control soils. Anammox bacterial compositions differed significantly (P <0.05) between gut and soil, and earthworm altered anammox bacterial communities in soils. Brocadia, Kuenenia and abundant unclassified anammox bacteria were detected in collected soils and gut contents, in which Brocadia was only detected in guts. These results suggested that microbes in earthworm gut increase, but present of earthworm reduces anammox and denitrification associated N loss by altering the anammox bacterial community compositions in soils. (C) 2020 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Li, Hu","Yang, Xiao-Ru","Wang, Juan","Zhou, Guo-Wei","Zhang, Yu-Sen","Lassen, Simon Bo","Zhu, Yong-Guan","Su, Jian-Qiang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-425849"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Agricultural soil","Anammox","Denitrification","Denitrifying bacteria","Gut microbiota","Microbial biomass","Nitrification","Nitrogen cycle","Nitrogen loss","Organic matter","Soil fauna","Temperature"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"earthworm gut an overlooked niche for anaerobic ammonium oxidation in agricultural soil","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-425849","identifier":[{"id":"000588243900067","type":"wos"},{"id":"32889284","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85090052492","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3687e7f7-127d-4691-8cfe-5693dc9c4b2b"],"keyword":["Agricultural soil","Anammox","DENITRIFICATION","DENITRIFYING BACTERIA","Gut microbiota","IN-SITU DETECTION","MICROBIAL BIOMASS","NITRIFICATION","NITROGEN LOSS","Nitrogen cycle","ORGANIC-MATTER","OXIDIZING BACTERIA","Soil fauna","TEMPERATURE"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0DC6A3E5318CA66F841D054F977E5CC2"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Microbial Ecology and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Hu","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Hu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiao-Ru","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Xiao-Ru","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Juan","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Juan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Guo-Wei","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Guo-Wei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yu-Sen","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yu-Sen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Simon Bo","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"7550f1f0-7813-4a66-8524-1287b55f402a","name":"Lassen, Simon Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-9781-1939","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yong-Guan","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Yong-Guan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jian-Qiang","key":"supau","last":"Su","name":"Su, Jian-Qiang","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32889284"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scitotenv.2020.141874","issn":["00489697","18791026"],"issn_org":["00489697"],"journal":"Science of the Total Environment","paperid":"141874","status":"p","title":"Science of the Total Environment","volume":"752"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090052492"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3687e7f7-127d-4691-8cfe-5693dc9c4b2b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Earthworm gut : An overlooked niche for anaerobic ammonium oxidation in agricultural soil","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-425849","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Although important factors governing the meiosis have been reported in the embryonic ovary, meiosis in postnatal testis remains poorly understood. Herein, we first report that SRY-box 30 (Sox30) is an age-related and essential regulator of meiosis in the postnatal testis. Sox30-null mice exhibited uniquely impaired testis, presenting the abnormal arrest of germ-cell differentiation and irregular Leydig cell proliferation. In aged Sox30-null mice, the observed testicular impairments were more severe. Furthermore, the germ-cell arrest occurred at the stage of meiotic zygotene spermatocytes, which is strongly associated with critical regulators of meiosis (such as Cyp26b1, Stra8 and Rec8) and sex differentiation (such as Rspo1, Foxl2, Sox9, Wnt4 and Ctnnb1). Mechanistically, Sox30 can activate Stra8 and Rec8, and inhibit Cyp26b1 and Ctnnb1 by direct binding to their promoters. A different Sox30 domain required for regulating the activity of these gene promoters, providing a “fail-safe” mechanism for Sox30 to facilitate germ-cell differentiation. Indeed, retinoic acid levels were reduced owing to increased degradation following the elevation of Cyp26b1 in Sox30-null testes. Re-expression of Sox30 in Sox30-null mice successfully restored germ-cell meiosis, differentiation and Leydig cell proliferation. Moreover, the restoration of actual fertility appeared to improve over time. Consistently, Rec8 and Stra8 were reactivated, and Cyp26b1 and Ctnnb1 were reinhibited in the restored testes. In summary, Sox30 is necessary, sufficient and age-associated for germ-cell meiosis and differentiation in testes by direct regulating critical regulators. This study advances our understanding of the regulation of germ-cell meiosis and differentiation in the postnatal testis.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Han, Fei","Yin, Li","Jiang, Xiao","Zhang, Xi","Zhang, Ning","Yang, Jun tang","Ouyang, Wei ming","Hao, Xiang lin","Liu, Wen bin","Huang, Yong sheng","Chen, Hong qiang","Gao, Fei","Li, Zhong tai","Guo, Qiao nan","Cao, Jia","Liu, Jin yi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-515734"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identification of sry box 000000000030 as an age related essential gatekeeper for male germ cell meiosis and differentiation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/acel.13343","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-515734","identifier":[{"id":"33721419","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8135013","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85102465488","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ccc165ef-73ed-4ba4-a935-2b1a25fa3293"],"keyword":["SRY-box 30","induced recovery","meiosis arrest","postnatal testis","retinoic acid signalling","zygotene spermatocyte"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-53AFC63639A4BC3FCEEDB5A50272C8F6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/273598138/acel.13343.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/acel.13343","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Comparative Pediatrics and Nutrition"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Fei","key":"hanfeipau","last":"Han","name":"Han, Fei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Li","key":"yinlipau","last":"Yin","name":"Yin, Li","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiao","key":"jiangxiaopau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Xiao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xi","key":"zhangxipau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Xi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ning","key":"zhangningpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Ning","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jun tang","key":"yangjuntangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Jun tang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wei ming","key":"ouyangweimingpau","last":"Ouyang","name":"Ouyang, Wei ming","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiang lin","key":"haoxianglinpau","last":"Hao","name":"Hao, Xiang lin","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wen bin","key":"liuwenbinpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Wen bin","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yong sheng","key":"huangyongshengpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Yong sheng","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hong qiang","key":"chenhongqiangpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Hong qiang","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Fei","key":"gaofeipau","last":"Gao","locid":"70b6cfb5-ec35-418f-8f24-520bb5696a8d","name":"Gao, Fei","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Zhong tai","key":"lizhongtaipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Zhong tai","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Qiao nan","key":"guoqiaonanpau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Qiao nan","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jia","key":"caojiapau","last":"Cao","name":"Cao, Jia","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jin yi","key":"liujinyipau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Jin yi","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33721419"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/acel.13343","issn":["14749718","14749726"],"issn_org":["14749718"],"issue":"5","journal":"Aging Cell","paperid":"e13343","status":"p","title":"Aging Cell","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85102465488"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ccc165ef-73ed-4ba4-a935-2b1a25fa3293"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Identification of SRY-box 30 as an age-related essential gatekeeper for male germ-cell meiosis and differentiation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-515734","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Cotton fibre is the most important source for natural textiles. The secondary cell walls (SCWs) of mature cotton fibres contain the highest proportion of cellulose content (> 90%) in any plant. The onset and progression of SCW cellulose synthesis need to be tightly controlled to balance fibre elongation and cell wall deposition. However, regulatory mechanisms that control cellulose synthesis during cotton fibre growth remain elusive. Here, we conducted genetic and functional analyses demonstrating that the R2R3-MYB GhMYB7 controls cotton fibre cellulose synthesis. Overexpression of GhMYB7 in cotton sped up SCW cellulose biosynthesis in fibre cells, and led to shorter fibres with thicker walls. By contrast, RNA interference (RNAi) silencing of GhMYB7 delayed fibre SCW cellulose synthesis and resulted in elongated fibres with thinner walls. Furthermore, we demonstrated that GhMYB7 regulated cotton fibre SCW cellulose synthases by directly binding to three distinct cis-elements in the respective GhCesA4, GhCesA7 and GhCesA8 promoters. We found that this regulatory mechanism of cellulose synthesis was 'hi-jacked' also by other GhMYBs. Together, our findings uncover a hitherto-unknown mechanism that cotton fibre employs to regulate SCW cellulose synthesis. Our results also provide a strategy for genetic improvement of SCW thickness of cotton fibre.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Huang, Junfeng","Chen, Feng","Guo, Yanjun","Gan, Xinli","Yang, Mingming","Zeng, Wei","Persson, Staffan","Li, Juan","Xu, Wenliang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-538300"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Shanghai Jiao Tong University"],"keyword":["Arabidopsis","Biosynthesis","Cell elongation","Identification","MYB","NAC","Proteins","Sequence","Transcription factor","XYLEM","cellulose synthesis","secondary cell wall"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ghmyb000000000007 promotes secondary wall cellulose deposition in cotton fibres by regulating i ghcesa i gene expression through three distinct i cis i elements","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/332598423/nph.17612.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-538300","identifier":[{"id":"85111753766","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34245570","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000680929800001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-f2b7db42-ddc9-4f98-ab17-564338ea0ade"],"keyword":["ARABIDOPSIS","BIOSYNTHESIS","CELL ELONGATION","IDENTIFICATION","MYB","NAC","PROTEINS","SEQUENCE","TRANSCRIPTION FACTOR","XYLEM","cellulose synthesis","cis-elements","cotton fibre","secondary cell wall"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-166FD266DC5948084C9EF57858909C8E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/332598423/nph.17612.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Plant Glycobiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"shanghai jiao tong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai Jiao Tong University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Junfeng","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Junfeng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Feng","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Feng","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yanjun","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Yanjun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xinli","key":"ganpau","last":"Gan","name":"Gan, Xinli","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mingming","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Mingming","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wei","key":"zengpau","last":"Zeng","name":"Zeng, Wei","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Staffan","key":"perssonpau","last":"Persson","locid":"ce45e4c4-89a7-4e38-8123-ae7c628c239f","name":"Persson, Staffan","orcid":"0000-0002-6377-5132","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Juan","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Juan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wenliang","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Wenliang","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34245570"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/nph.17612","issn":["0028646X","14698137"],"issn_org":["0028646X"],"issue":"4","journal":"New Phytologist","pages":"1718-1737","status":"p","title":"New Phytologist","volume":"232"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111753766"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f2b7db42-ddc9-4f98-ab17-564338ea0ade"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"GhMYB7 promotes secondary wall cellulose deposition in cotton fibres by regulating<i> GhCesA</i> gene expression through three distinct <i>cis</i>-elements","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-538300","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: The origin of sex differences in prevalence and presentation of neuropsychiatric and behavioral traits is largely unknown. Given established genetic contributions and correlations, we tested for a sex-differentiated genetic architecture within and between traits. Methods: Using European ancestry genome-wide association summary statistics for 20 neuropsychiatric and behavioral traits, we tested for sex differences in single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP)-based heritability and genetic correlation (rg < 1). For each trait, we computed per-SNP z scores from sex-stratified regression coefficients and identified genes with sex-differentiated effects using a gene-based approach. We calculated correlation coefficients between z scores to test for shared sex-differentiated effects. Finally, we tested for sex differences in across-trait genetic correlations. Results: We observed no consistent sex differences in SNP-based heritability. Between-sex, within-trait genetic correlations were high, although <1 for educational attainment and risk-taking behavior. We identified 4 genes with significant sex-differentiated effects across 3 traits. Several trait pairs shared sex-differentiated effects. The top genes with sex-differentiated effects were enriched for multiple gene sets, including neuron- and synapse-related sets. Most between-trait genetic correlation estimates were not significantly different between sexes, with exceptions (educational attainment and risk-taking behavior). Conclusions: Sex differences in the common autosomal genetic architecture of neuropsychiatric and behavioral phenotypes are small and polygenic and unlikely to fully account for observed sex-differentiated attributes. Larger sample sizes are needed to identify sex-differentiated effects for most traits. For well-powered studies, we identified genes with sex-differentiated effects that were enriched for neuron-related and other biological functions. This work motivates further investigation of genetic and environmental influences on sex differences.","author_count":32,"contributors":["Martin, Joanna","Khramtsova, Ekaterina A.","Goleva, Slavina B.","Blokland, Gabriëlla A.M.","Traglia, Michela","Walters, Raymond K.","Hübel, Christopher","Coleman, Jonathan R.I.","Breen, Gerome","Børglum, Anders D","Demontis, Ditte","Grove, Jakob","Werge, Thomas","Bralten, Janita","Bulik, Cynthia M.","Lee, Phil H.","Mathews, Carol A.","Peterson, Roseann E.","Winham, Stacey J.","Wray, Naomi","Edenberg, Howard J.","Guo, Wei","Yao, Yin","Neale, Benjamin M.","Faraone, Stephen V.","Petryshen, Tracey L.","Weiss, Lauren A.","Duncan, Laramie E.","Goldstein, Jill M.","Smoller, Jordan W.","Stranger, Barbara E.","Davis, Lea K."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-014415"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["Sex Differences Cross-Disorder Analysis Group of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium"],"corresponding_author":["Martin, Joanna"],"country":["Australia","China","Netherlands","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Broad Institute","Cardiff University","Department of Environment Science and Engineering, Fudan University","Fudan University","Harvard University","Indiana University Bloomington","Johnson & Johnson","Karolinska Institutet","King's College London","Maastricht University","Mayo Clinic Rochester, MN","National Institutes of Health","National Institutes of Health (NIH)","Northwestern University","Purdue University","Radboud University Nijmegen","SUNY Upstate Medical University","South London and Maudsley NHS Foundation Trust","Stanford University","The University of Chicago","University of California San Francisco","University of California at San Francisco","University of Chicago","University of Florida","University of North Carolina","Unive