key":"petryshenpau","last":"Petryshen","name":"Petryshen, Tracey L.","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8 9","corresponding":null,"first":"Lauren A.","key":"weisspau","last":"Weiss","name":"Weiss, Lauren A.","rank":27,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"30","corresponding":null,"first":"Laramie E.","key":"duncanpau","last":"Duncan","name":"Duncan, Laramie E.","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Jill M.","key":"goldsteinpau","last":"Goldstein","name":"Goldstein, Jill M.","rank":29,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Jordan W.","key":"smollerpau","last":"Smoller","name":"Smoller, Jordan W.","rank":30,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 31 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara E.","key":"strangerpau","last":"Stranger","name":"Stranger, Barbara E.","rank":31,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 32","corresponding":null,"first":"Lea K.","key":"davispau","last":"Davis","name":"Davis, Lea K.","rank":32,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33648717"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.biopsych.2020.12.024","issn":["00063223","18732402"],"issn_org":["00063223"],"issue":"12","journal":"Biological Psychiatry","pages":"1127-1137","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Biological Psychiatry","volume":"89"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85102837416"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Lundbeck Pharma","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-193a6abe-1284-4ab5-b8d6-5ba0f5418062","ku-0a323edd-188c-4c4e-a8c0-3d7e3770d31c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Examining Sex-Differentiated Genetic Effects Across Neuropsychiatric and Behavioral Traits","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-014415","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Heat stress is a major cause of welfare issues and economic losses to the worldwide dairy cattle industry. Genetic selection for heat tolerance has a great potential to positively affect the dairy industry, as the gains are permanent and cumulative over generations. Rectal temperature (RT) is hypothesized to be a good indicator trait of heat tolerance. Therefore, this study investigated the genetic architecture of RT by estimating genetic parameters, performing genome-wide association studies, and biologically validating potential candidate genes identified to be related to RT in Holstein cattle. A total of 33,013 RT records from 7,598 cows were used in this study. In addition, 1,114 cows were genotyped using the Illumina 150K Bovine BeadChip (Illumina, San Diego, CA). Rectal temperature measurements taken in the morning (AMRT) and in the afternoon (PMRT) are moderately heritable traits, with estimates of 0.09 ± 0.02 and 0.04 ± 0.01, respectively. These 2 traits are also highly genetically correlated (r = 0.90 ± 0.08). A total of 10 SNPs (located on BTA3, BTA4, BTA8, BTA13, BTA14, and BTA29) were found to be significantly associated with AMRT and PMRT. Subsequently, gene expression analyses were performed to validate the key functional genes identified (SPAG17, FAM107B, TSNARE1, RALYL, and PHRF1). This was done through in vitro exposure of peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMC) to different temperatures (37°C, 39°C, and 42°C). The relative mRNA expression of 2 genes, FAM107B and PHRF1, significantly changed between the control and heat stressed PBMC. In summary, RT is heritable, and enough genetic variability exists to enable genetic improvement of heat tolerance in Holstein cattle. Important genomic regions were identified and biologically validated; FAM107B and PHRF1 are the main candidate genes identified to influence heat stress response in dairy cattle.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Luo, Hanpeng","Li, Xiang","Hu, Lirong","Xu, Wei","Chu, Qin","Liu, Aoxing","Guo, Gang","Liu, Lin","Brito, Luiz F.","Wang, Yachun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-152191"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Wang, Yachun"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beijing Academy of Agriculture and Forestry Sciences","Beijing Dairy Cattle Center","China Agricultural University","Purdue University"],"keyword":["Chinese Holstein cattle","Gene expression","Genome Wide Association Study","Heat stress","animal resilience"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genomic analyses and biological validation of candidate genes for rectal temperature as an indicator of heat stress in holstein cattle","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3168/jds.2020-18725","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-152191","identifier":[{"id":"33589260","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85101048051","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-27d7656e-9b88-4fad-a3f7-94fcab900479"],"keyword":["Chinese Holstein cattle","animal resilience","gene expression","genome-wide association study","heat stress"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8862F0962F4CACC2E47CEF5824DFC41A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3168/jds.2020-18725","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"china agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"beijing academy of agriculture and forestry sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Beijing Academy of Agriculture and Forestry Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Center for Quantitative Genetics and Genomics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"beijing dairy cattle center","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Beijing Dairy Cattle Center","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"purdue university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Purdue University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanpeng","key":"luohanpengpau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Hanpeng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiang","key":"lixiangpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lirong","key":"hulirongpau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Lirong","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"xuweipau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Wei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Qin","key":"chuqinpau","last":"Chu","name":"Chu, Qin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Aoxing","key":"liuaoxingpau","last":"Liu","locid":"f611c6f3-d0db-4412-9153-45109c50d714","name":"Liu, Aoxing","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Gang","key":"guogangpau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Gang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Lin","key":"liulinpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Lin","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Luiz F.","key":"britoluizfpau","last":"Brito","name":"Brito, Luiz F.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yachun","key":"wangyachunpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Yachun","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33589260"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3168/jds.2020-18725","issn":["00220302","15253198"],"issn_org":["00220302"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Dairy Science","pages":"4441-4451","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Dairy Science","volume":"104"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85101048051"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-27d7656e-9b88-4fad-a3f7-94fcab900479"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Genomic analyses and biological validation of candidate genes for rectal temperature as an indicator of heat stress in Holstein cattle","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-152191","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: The overall objective of the present study is to extend our understanding of the clinical phenotype and underlying mechanism of a newly discovered cardiac arrhythmia syndrome through a multicenter study. Gain-of-function mutations in the cardiac Ca 2+release channel (RyR2 [ryanodine receptor 2]) cause catecholaminergic polymorphic ventricular tachycardia, whereas loss-of-function RyR2 mutations are linked to a new cardiac arrhythmia disorder termed Ca 2+-release deficiency syndrome (CRDS). Catecholaminergic polymorphic ventricular tachycardia is an inherited arrhythmia disorder characterized by stress-induced bidirectional and polymorphic ventricular tachyarrhythmias and is routinely diagnosed by using exercise stress testing. Conversely, RyR2-CRDS is characterized by ventricular arrhythmias and sudden cardiac death but a negative exercise stress testing for catecholaminergic polymorphic ventricular tachycardia. There are currently no clinical diagnostic tests for CRDS and affected patients may manifest with sudden cardiac death as their first symptom. In the absence of effective clinical diagnostic tools, in vitro functional characterization of associated RyR2 mutations provides an alternative means to identify potential cases of CRDS. Methods: We searched for patients presenting with phenotypes compatible with CRDS that have RyR2 mutations and performed in vitro functional characterization. Results: We found that 3 novel (G570D, R4147K, and A4203V) and 2 previously reported (M4109R and A4204V) RyR2 mutations associated with CRDS phenotypes markedly reduced caffeine-induced Ca 2+release and store overload-induced Ca 2+release. We also characterized 2 additional loss-of-function RyR2 mutations previously reported (Q3925E and L4769S) that are located in the central and channel pore-forming domains critical for Ca 2+activation and channel gating. Q3925E was identified through postmortem genetic testing in an individual who died suddenly, while L4769S is a variant of uncertain significance reported in ClinVar, suggesting that RyR2 CRDS may be under detected. Conclusions: These findings provide further support for the existence of an emerging RyR2 loss-of-function associated arrhythmia syndrome (CRDS) and shed new insights into the disease mechanism.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Li, Yanhui","Wei, Jinhong","Guo, Wenting","Sun, Bo","Estillore, John Paul","Wang, Ruiwu","Yoruk, Ayhan","Roston, Thomas M","Sanatani, Shubhayan","Wilde, Arthur A M","Gollob, Michael H","Roberts, Jason D","Tseng, Zian H","Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","Chen, S R Wayne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-212088"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","China","Netherlands","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Huazhong University of Science and Technology","Kunming University of Science and Technology","McMaster University","Samuel Lunenfeld Research Institute, Mount Sinai Hospital, Toronto","University of Amsterdam","University of Calgary","University of California","University of California at Berkeley"],"keyword":["Caffeine","Death","Mutation","Phenotype"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"human ryr000000000002 ryanodine receptor 000000000002 loss of function mutations clinical phenotypes and in vitro characterization","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85116197322","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-212088","identifier":[{"id":"000697545200003","type":"wos"},{"id":"85116197322","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34546788","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-91206cd8-c84f-4c93-934f-049f924610f2"],"keyword":["caffeine","death","mutation","phenotype","ryanodine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CBF2C6D0FB575A493743AE5A8C4EDDA9"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ca","key":"university of calgary","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Calgary","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"huazhong university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Huazhong University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"kunming university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Kunming University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of california","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"university of california at berkeley","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Berkeley","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"nl","key":"university of amsterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Amsterdam","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"ca","key":"samuel lunenfeld research institute mount sinai hospital toronto","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Samuel Lunenfeld Research Institute, Mount Sinai Hospital, Toronto","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"ca","key":"mcmaster university","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"McMaster University","used":1},{"affno":"9","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yanhui","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yanhui","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jinhong","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Jinhong","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenting","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Wenting","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bo","key":"sunpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Bo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"John Paul","key":"estillorepau","last":"Estillore","name":"Estillore, John Paul","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ruiwu","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Ruiwu","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Ayhan","key":"yorukpau","last":"Yoruk","name":"Yoruk, Ayhan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas M","key":"rostonpau","last":"Roston","name":"Roston, Thomas M","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Shubhayan","key":"sanatanipau","last":"Sanatani","name":"Sanatani, Shubhayan","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Arthur A M","key":"wildepau","last":"Wilde","name":"Wilde, Arthur A M","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael H","key":"gollobpau","last":"Gollob","name":"Gollob, Michael H","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Jason D","key":"robertspau","last":"Roberts","name":"Roberts, Jason D","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Zian H","key":"tsengpau","last":"Tseng","name":"Tseng, Zian H","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik K","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5fb8d709-1b6d-4959-8f16-a4b5d78b436d","name":"Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","name_org":"Jensen, Henrik K","orcid":"0000-0003-1802-4302","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"S R Wayne","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, S R Wayne","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34546788"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/circep.121.010013","issn":["19413084","19413149"],"issn_org":["19413149"],"issue":"9","journal":"Circulation: Arrhythmia and Electrophysiology","pages":"874-885","paperid":"010013","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Circulation: Arrhythmia and Electrophysiology","title_org":"Circulation. Arrhythmia and Electrophysiology","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85116197322"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-91206cd8-c84f-4c93-934f-049f924610f2"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Human RyR2 (Ryanodine Receptor 2) Loss-of-Function Mutations : Clinical Phenotypes and In Vitro Characterization","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-212088","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The Large Hadron-Electron Collider (LHeC) is designed to move the field of deep inelastic scattering (DIS) to the energy and intensity frontier of particle physics. Exploiting energy-recovery technology, it collides a novel, intense electron beam with a proton or ion beam from the High-Luminosity Large Hadron Collider (HL-LHC). The accelerator and interaction region are designed for concurrent electron-proton and proton-proton operations. This report represents an update to the LHeC's conceptual design report (CDR), published in 2012. It comprises new results on the parton structure of the proton and heavier nuclei, QCD dynamics, and electroweak and top-quark physics. It is shown how the LHeC will open a new chapter of nuclear particle physics by extending the accessible kinematic range of lepton-nucleus scattering by several orders of magnitude. Due to its enhanced luminosity and large energy and the cleanliness of the final hadronic states, the LHeC has a strong Higgs physics programme and its own discovery potential for new physics. Building on the 2012 CDR, this report contains a detailed updated design for the energy-recovery electron linac (ERL), including a new lattice, magnet and superconducting radio-frequency technology, and further components. Challenges of energy recovery are described, and the lower-energy, high-current, three-turn ERL facility, PERLE at Orsay, is presented, which uses the LHeC characteristics serving as a development facility for the design and operation of the LHeC. An updated detector design is presented corresponding to the acceptance, resolution, and calibration goals that arise from the Higgs and parton-density-function physics programmes. This paper also presents novel results for the Future Circular Collider in electron-hadron (FCC-eh) mode, which utilises the same ERL technology to further extend the reach of DIS to even higher centre-of-mass energies.","author_count":335,"contributors":["Agostini, P.","Aksakal, H.","Alekhin, S.","Allport, P. P.","Andari, N.","Andre, K. D. J.","Angal-Kalinin, D.","Antusch, S.","Aperio Bella, L.","Apolinario, L.","Apsimon, R.","Apyan, A.","Arduini, G.","Ari, Burcak Aktürk","Armbruster, A.","Armesto, N.","Auchmann, B.","Aulenbacher, K.","Azuelos, G.","Backovic, S.","Bailey, Alice","Bailey, S.","Balli, F.","Behera, S.","Behnke, O.","Ben-Zvi, no-firstname","Benedikt, M.","Bernauer, J.","Bertolucci, S.","Biswal, S. S.","Bluemlein, J.","Bogacz, A.","Bonvini, M.","Boonekamp, M.","Bordry, F.","Boroun, G. R.","Bottura, L.","Bousson, S.","Bouzas, A. O.","Bracco, C.","Bracinik, J.","Britzger, D.","Brodsky, S. J.","Bruni, C.","Bruning, O.","Burkhardt, H.","Cakir, O.","Calaga, R.","Caldwell, A.","Caliskan, A.","Camarda, S.","Catalan-Lasheras, N. C.","Cassou, K.","Cepila, J.","Cetinkaya, Semra","Chetvertkova, no-firstname","Cole, B.","Coleppa, B.","Cooper-Sarkar, A.","Cormier, E.","Cornell, A. S.","Corsini, R.","Cruz-Alaniz, E.","Currie, J.","Curtin, D.","D'Onofrio, M.","Dainton, J.","Daly, E.","Das, A.","Das, S. P.","Dassa, L.","de Blas, J.","Delle Rose, L.","Denizli, H.","Deshpande, K. S.","Douglas, D.","Duarte, L.","Dupraz, K.","Dutta, S.","Efremov, A.","Eichhorn, R.","Eskola, K. J.","Ferreiro, E. G.","Fischer, O.","Flores-Sanchez, O.","Forte, S.","Gaddi, A.","Gao, J.","Gehrmann, T.","Gehrmann-De Ridder, A.","Gerigk, F.","Gilbert, A.","Giuli, F.","Glazov, A.","Glover, N.","Godbole, R. M.","Goddard, B.","Goncalves, Rodrigo","Gonzalez-Sprinberg, G. A.","Goyal, A.","Grames, J.","Granados, E.","Grassellino, A.","Gunaydin, Y. O.","Guo, Y. C.","Guzey, no-firstname","Gwenlan, C.","Hammad, A.","Han, C. C.","Harland-Lang, L.","Haug, F.","Hautmann, F.","Hayden, D.","Hessler, J.","Helenius, Dorte","Henry, J.","Hernandez-Sanchez, J.","Hesari, H.","Hobbs, T. J.","Hod, N.","Hoffstaetter, G. H.","Holzer, B.","Honorato, C. G.","Hounsell, B.","Hu, N.","Hug, F.","Huss, A.","Hutton, A.","Islam, R.","Iwamoto, S.","Jana, S.","Jansova, M.","Jensen, E.","Jones, T.","Jowett, J