{"abstract":"In the process of fault diagnosis for complicated mechatronic equipment such as actuators, the fault diagnosis method is usually calculated on the equipment side. When computing devices are not easy to be installed at the object end, the embedded device can be used for real-time diagnosis, so as to meet the requirement of no network, low bandwidth, low power consumption, and low delay, at the same time improve the availability of the fault diagnosis device. While ensuring the recognition rate and the diagnosis effect, the security, and portability of the equipment are improved. In this paper, an online fault diagnosis system for mechatronic actuators based on the STM32 embedded platform is developed. This system uses a backpropagation neural network and a support vector machine fusion model to diagnose the actuator faults and reduces the memory usage by compressing the model, discretizing the attributes, and reducing the number of input features. Real-time data acquisition, feature extraction, fusion fault diagnosis, and data storage are implemented on this embedded system.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Chen, Shaowei","Huang, Yanping","Liu, Hengyu","Wen, Pengfei","Yang, Ning","Zhao, Shuai"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-069890"],"event":{"end":"2021-10-17","place":"Nanjing, cn","start":"2021-10-15","title":"12th IEEE Global Reliability and Prognostics and Health Management, PHM-Nanjing 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Aviation Industry Corporation of China","Northwestern Polytechnical University Xian"],"keyword":["Embedded diagnosis","Fault diagnosis","Neural network","STM32"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development of an online fault diagnostic system based on stm000000000032 for actuators","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85123444061&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-069890","identifier":[{"id":"85123444061","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-448ef4f8-f34c-4de3-b01c-cb3494af9b35"],"keyword":["Embedded diagnosis","Fault diagnosis","Neural network","STM32"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B8DCB69C98647B81418B0602D424663E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"northwestern polytechnical university xian","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northwestern Polytechnical University Xian","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"aviation industry corporation of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Aviation Industry Corporation of China","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Applied Power Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronics System Integration and Materials","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Reliability of Power Electronic Converters"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shaowei","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Shaowei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yanping","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Yanping","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hengyu","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Hengyu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pengfei","key":"wenpau","last":"Wen","name":"Wen, Pengfei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ning","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Ning","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Shuai","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","locid":"db7c3194-c9e3-4d1d-bd94-dfe12a676317","name":"Zhao, Shuai","orcid":"0000-0001-7441-5434","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wei","key":"guopedh","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Wei","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Steven","key":"lipedh","last":"Li","name":"Li, Steven","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/phm-nanjing52125.2021.9612802","eisbn":["9781665401319"],"isbn":["9781665401302","9781665429795"],"publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"2021 Global Reliability and Prognostics and Health Management, PHM-Nanjing 2021"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85123444061"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-448ef4f8-f34c-4de3-b01c-cb3494af9b35"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Development of an Online Fault-Diagnostic-System Based on STM32 for Actuators","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-069890","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"COVID-19 is the first global scale crisis since the inception of Bitcoin. We compare the contagion phenomenon of Bitcoin and other financial markets or assets pre and during the COVID-19 shock in both contemporaneous and non-contemporaneous manner. This paper uses the directed acyclic graph (DAG), spillover index, and network topology to provide strong evidence on the directional contagion outcomes of Bitcoin and other assets. The empirical results show that the contagion effect between Bitcoin and developed markets is strengthened during the COVID-19 crisis. Particularly, European market has a dominant role. Excluding Bitcoin’s own shocks, United State and European markets are the main contagion sources to Bitcoin. European market also works as a intermediary to deliver infectious from United State and market fear. The findings show that gold always has contagion effect with Bitcoin, while gold, US dollar and bond market are the contagion receivers of Bitcoin under the shock of COVID-19. The empirical results further proved the safe haven, hedge and diversifier potential of Bitcoin in economic stable time, but also shows that the sustainability of these properties is undermined during the market turmoil.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Guo, Xiaochun","Lu, Fengbin","Wei, Yunjie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-298514"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Wei, Yunjie"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","The Chinese Academy of Sciences","University of the Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Bitcoin","Contagion","Covid 19","DAG","Financial market risk"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"capture the contagion network of bitcoin evidence from pre and mid covid 000000000019","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/69698961/xiaochun_guo_et_al_capture_the_contagion_network_of_bitcoin_acceptedversion.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-298514","identifier":[{"id":"85109114102","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-f23db5f7-b14d-4c75-ab98-b12b266225a7"],"keyword":["Bitcoin","COVID-19","Contagion","DAG","Financial market risk"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-94145459E241D47FE94E2D50329FFA7A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/69698961/xiaochun_guo_et_al_capture_the_contagion_network_of_bitcoin_acceptedversion.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Politics and Philosophy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"university of the chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of the Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"the chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"The Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xiaochun","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","locid":"b73e98b1-fbe4-483d-8e01-65f92b3c9930","name":"Guo, Xiaochun","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Fengbin","key":"lupau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Fengbin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yunjie","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Yunjie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ribaf.2021.101484","issn":["02755319"],"journal":"Research in International Business and Finance","paperid":"101484","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Research in International Business and Finance","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85109114102"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-f23db5f7-b14d-4c75-ab98-b12b266225a7"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Capture the Contagion Network of Bitcoin : Evidence from Pre and Mid COVID-19","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-298514","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The combination of hydrogen energy and renewable energy generation is one of the important ways to achieve the goals of carbon neutrality and the peak of carbon dioxide emissions, where power electronic converters are widely used. In order to realize the efficient operation of the electrolysis hydrogen production system, the power electronic converter is required to have the characteristics of low voltage and high current capability, low output current ripple, high step-down ratio, and high reliability. Firstly, this paper analyzes the electrolyzer model, and studies the characteristics and technical indicators of the existing commercial electrolyzer. Secondly, this paper sorts and classifies the power electronic converters applied in various electrolysis hydrogen production systems including the alkaline electrolyzer, the polymer exchange membrane electrolyzer and the solid oxide electrolyzer, and various topologies are analyzed and compared. Meanwhile, the potential applications, existing problems and development trends of power electronic converters for producing hydrogen from renewable energy sources are discussed and summarized.TFoundation:his work is supported by Science and Technology Innovation Project of CHN Energy (No. GJNY-19-136), National Key R&D Program of China (No. 2018YFB1503100), and Science Fund for Creative Research Groups of Hebei Provincial Natural Science Foundation of China (No. F2020203013).","author_count":9,"contributors":["Guo, Xiaoqiang","Wei, Yupeng","Wan, Yanming","Zhou, You","Kong, Lingguo","Zhang, Zhe","Lu, Zhigang","Hua, Changchun","Malinowski, Mariusz"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-324121"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["China","Poland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CHN Energy Investment Group Co. Ltd.","Northeast Electric Power University","Warsaw University of Technology","Yanshan University"],"keyword":["Current ripple","Electrolyzer","Hydrogen energy","Power electronic converter","Renewable energy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"review on power electronic converters for producing hydrogen from renewable energy sources","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85117594425","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-324121","identifier":[{"id":"85117594425","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-41aef944-e4de-4e76-829f-90f6aad27b53"],"keyword":["Current ripple","Electrolysis hydrogen production","Electrolyzer","Hydrogen energy","Power electronic converter","Renewable energy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-EDE99F8C7A3F54F9A432164AB4CED75F"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"yanshan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Yanshan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chn energy investment group co ltd","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CHN Energy Investment Group Co. Ltd.","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"northeast electric power university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northeast Electric Power University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineeri