bdc-b377-47a3-bdc0-4deccfda761c","name":"Zhang, Guojie","orcid":"0000-0001-6860-1521","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Qi","key":"zhouqipau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Qi","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33408157"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1101/gr.271569.120","issn":["10889051","15495469"],"issn_org":["10889051"],"issue":"3","journal":"Genome Research","pages":"497-511","status":"p","title":"Genome Research","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85102538622"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c40c1655-678e-42a2-83ff-19c5657678b3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A new emu genome illuminates the evolution of genome configuration and nuclear architecture of avian chromosomes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-510466","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"We present the first results from the ongoing, intensive, multiwavelength monitoring program of the luminous Seyfert 1 galaxy Mrk 817. While this active galactic nucleus was, in part, selected for its historically unobscured nature, we discovered that the X-ray spectrum is highly absorbed, and there are new blueshifted, broad, and narrow UV absorption lines, which suggest that a dust-free, ionized obscurer located at the inner broad-line region partially covers the central source. Despite the obscuration, we measure UV and optical continuum reverberation lags consistent with a centrally illuminated Shakura-Sunyaev thin accretion disk, and measure reverberation lags associated with the optical broad-line region, as expected. However, in the first 55 days of the campaign, when the obscuration was becoming most extreme, we observe a de-coupling of the UV continuum and the UV broad emission-line variability. The correlation recovered in the next 42 days of the campaign, as Mrk 817 entered a less obscured state. The short C iv and Ly alpha lags suggest that the accretion disk extends beyond the UV broad-line region.","author_count":74,"contributors":["Kara, Erin","Mehdipour, Missagh","Kriss, Gerard A.","Cackett, Edward M.","Arav, Nahum","Barth, Aaron J.","Byun, Doyee","Brotherton, Michael S.","De Rosa, Gisella","Gelbord, Jonathan","Hernandez Santisteban, Juan V.","Hu, Chen","Kaastra, Jelle","Landt, Hermine","Li, Yan-Rong","Miller, Jake A.","Montano, John","Partington, Ethan","Aceituno, Jesus","Bai, Jin-Ming","Bao, Dongwei","Bentz, Misty C.","Brink, Thomas G.","Chelouche, Doron","Chen, Yong-Jie","Colmenero, Encarni Romero","Bonta, Elena Dalla","Dehghanian, Maryam","Du, Pu","Edelson, Rick","Ferland, Gary J.","Ferrarese, Laura","Fian, Carina","Filippenko, Alexei V.","Fischer, Travis","Goad, Michael R.","Gonzalez Buitrago, Diego H.","Gorjian, Varoujan","Grier, Catherine J.","Guo, Wei-Jian","Hall, Patrick B.","Ho, Luis C.","Homayouni, Y.","Horne, Keith","Ilic, Dragana","Jiang, Bo-Wei","Joner, Michael D.","Kaspi, Shai","Kochanek, Christopher S.","Korista, Kirk T.","Kynoch, Daniel","Li, Sha-Sha","Liu, Jun-Rong","cHardy, Ian M. M.","McLane, Jacob N.","Mitchell, Jake A. J.","Netzer, Hagai","Olson, Kianna A.","Pogge, Richard W.","Popovic, Luka C.","Proga, Daniel","Storchi-Bergmann, Thaisa","Strasburger, Erika","Treu, Tommaso","Vestergaard, Marianne","Wang, Jian-Min","Ward, Martin J.","Waters, Tim","Williams, Peter R.","Yang, Sen","Yao, Zhu-Heng","Zastrocky, Theodora E.","Zhai, Shuo","Zu, Ying"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-518429"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","America, Central","America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Brazil","Canada","China","Czechia","Germany","Israel","Italy","Mexico","Netherlands","Serbia","South Africa","Spain","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Astron Observ","Brigham Young University","Czech Academy of Sciences","Durham University","Eureka Sci Inc, Eureka Scientific","Federal University of Rio Grande do Sul","Georgia State University","Jet Prop Lab, National Aeronautics & Space Administration (NASA), NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory (JPL)","Leiden University","Massachusetts Institute of Technology","NRC Herzberg Astronomy and Astrophysics Research Centre, 5071 West Saanich Road, Victoria, BC, V9E 2E7, Canada 0000-0002-8224-1128","Ohio State University","Peking University","Shanghai Jiao Tong University","South African Large Telescope Fdn","Space Telescope Sci Inst, Space Telescope Science Institute, AURA ESA","Space Telescope Science Institute","Spectral Sci Inc, Spectral Sciences Inc","Tel Aviv University","The Spanish National Research Council (CSIC)","Univ Haifa, University of Haifa, Haifa Res Ctr Theoret Phys & Astrophys","Universidad Nacional Autónoma de México","University of Arizona","University of California at Berkeley","University of California at Irvine","University of California at Los Angeles","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","University of Hamburg","University of Kentucky","University of Leicester","University of Nevada, Las Vegas","University of Padua","University of Southampton","University of St Andrews","University of Wyoming","Virginia Polytechnic Institute and State University","Wayne State University","Western Michigan University","York University Toronto"],"keyword":["Active galactic nuclei","BROAD LINE REGION","DRIVEN DISK WINDS","EMISSION LINES","Light curves","SPACE TELESCOPE","Supermassive black holes","accretion disk"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Chinese Acad Sci, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Institute of High Energy Physics, CAS, Inst High Energy Phys, Key Lab Particle Astrophys"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"agn storm 000000000002 i first results a change in the weather of mrk 000000000817","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2105.05840.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-518429","identifier":[{"id":"85120832752","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000722730500001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-d133e22a-6665-4923-bc0b-e973461f2267"],"keyword":["ACCRETION-DISK","ACTIVE GALACTIC NUCLEI","BROAD-LINE REGION","DRIVEN DISK WINDS","EMISSION-LINES","LIGHT CURVES","NGC 5548","SPACE TELESCOPE","SUPERMASSIVE BLACK-HOLES","X-RAY REVERBERATION"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A2AB3D5A45A139033772CCF916FA286E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2105.05840.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":