"affno":"","first":"Joel N.","key":"hirschhornjoelnpau","last":"Hirschhorn","name":"Hirschhorn, Joel N.","rank":514,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sekar","key":"kathiresansekarpau","last":"Kathiresan","name":"Kathiresan, Sekar","rank":515,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"boehnkemichaelpau","last":"Boehnke","name":"Boehnke, Michael","rank":516,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pradeep","key":"natarajanpradeeppau","last":"Natarajan","name":"Natarajan, Pradeep","rank":517,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gina M.","key":"pelosoginampau","last":"Peloso","name":"Peloso, Gina M.","rank":518,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christopher D.","key":"brownchristopherdpau","last":"Brown","name":"Brown, Christopher D.","rank":519,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrew P.","key":"morrisandrewppau","last":"Morris","name":"Morris, Andrew P.","rank":520,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Themistocles L.","key":"assimesthemistocleslpau","last":"Assimes","name":"Assimes, Themistocles L.","rank":521,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Panos","key":"deloukaspanospau","last":"Deloukas","name":"Deloukas, Panos","rank":522,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yan V.","key":"sunyanvpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Yan V.","rank":523,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34887591"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41586-021-04064-3","issn":["00280836","14764687"],"issn_org":["00280836"],"issue":"7890","journal":"Nature","pages":"675-679","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature","volume":"600"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121605114"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-82197af4-0844-4350-80c2-a858a2138491","sdu-a20f86a2-5b61-4a06-a7a5-9bdecb434faa"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The power of genetic diversity in genome-wide association studies of lipids","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.00-043943","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Stream biofilms are complex aggregates of diverse organism groups that play a vital role in global carbon and nitrogen cycles. Most of the current studies on stream biofilm focus on a limited number of organism groups (e.g., bacteria and algae), and few have included both prokaryote and eukaryote communities simultaneously. In this study, we incubated artificial substrates in five Danish lowland streams exhibiting different hydrological and physico-chemical conditions and explored the dynamics of community composition and diversity of the benthic biofilm, including both prokaryotes and eukaryotes. We found that few phyla in the prokaryote (Gammaproteobacteria and Bacteroidetes) and eukaryote (Cercozoa) communities accounted for over two-thirds of the total abundance at most of the sites. Both prokaryotic and eukaryotic diversity displayed the same temporal patterns, i.e., diversity peaked in July and January. We also found that hydrological and physico-chemical variables significantly explained the variation in the community composition at phylum level for both prokaryotes and eukaryotes. However, a large proportion of variation remained unexplained, which can be ascribed to important but unmeasured variables like light intensity and biological factors such as trophic and non-trophic interactions as revealed by network analysis. Therefore, we suggest that use of a multitrophic level perspective is needed to study biofilm i.e., the “microbial jungles”, where high occurrences of trophic and non-trophic interactions are expected.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Guo, Kun","Wu, Naicheng","Li, Wei","Baattrup-Pedersen, Annette","Riis, Tenna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-172822"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Wu, Naicheng"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","East China Normal University","Montana State University","Ningbo University"],"keyword":["Eukaryote","Hydrology","Microbial diversity","Prokaryote"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microbial biofilm community dynamics in five lowland streams","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85111188879","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-172822","identifier":[{"id":"85111188879","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34329932","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-4c55c782-9a2f-4854-b114-ffc2c22a1e47"],"keyword":["Eukaryote","Hydrology","Microbial diversity","Prokaryote","Stream biofilm"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C84FB9D656797E7C48C61AD478CA43E5"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Aquatic Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"east china normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"East China Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"ningbo university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Ningbo University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"montana state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Montana State University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kun","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","locid":"973d018e-eff5-49b1-b07a-d029aa30e497","name":"Guo, Kun","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Naicheng","key":"wupau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Naicheng","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Wei","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Annette","key":"baattruppedersenpau","last":"Baattrup-Pedersen","locid":"e4f5886d-70a8-4174-a224-b21d0dfc8689","name":"Baattrup-Pedersen, Annette","orcid":"0000-0002-3118-344X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tenna","key":"riispau","last":"Riis","locid":"63e9c033-4056-4f18-8c91-44244963ef37","name":"Riis, Tenna","orcid":"0000-0003-2501-4444","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34329932"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scitotenv.2021.149169","issn":["00489697","18791026"],"issn_org":["00489697"],"journal":"Science of the Total Environment","paperid":"149169","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Science of the Total Environment","volume":"798"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111188879"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4c55c782-9a2f-4854-b114-ffc2c22a1e47"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Microbial biofilm community dynamics in five lowland streams","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-172822","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Farm-animal species play crucial roles in satisfying demands for meat on a global scale, and they are genetically being developed to enhance the efficiency of meat production. In particular, one of the important breeders’ aims is to increase skeletal muscle growth in farm animals. The enhancement of muscle development and growth is crucial to meet consumers’ demands regarding meat quality. Fetal skeletal muscle development involves myogenesis (with myoblast proliferation, differentiation, and fusion), fibrogenesis, and adipogenesis. Typically, myogenesis is regulated by a convoluted network of intrinsic and extrinsic factors monitored by myogenic regulatory factor genes in two or three phases, as well as genes that code for kinases. Marker-assisted selection relies on candidate genes related positively or negatively to muscle development and can be a strong supplement to classical selection strategies in farm animals. This comprehensive review covers important (candidate) genes that regulate muscle development and growth in farm animals (cattle, sheep, chicken, and pig). The identification of these genes is an important step toward the goal of increasing meat yields and improves meat quality.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Mohammadabadi, Mohammadreza","Bordbar, Farhad","Jensen, Just","Du, Min","Guo, Wei"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-174175"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bordbar, Farhad"],"country":["Iran","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Shahid Bahonar University of Kerman","University of Wisconsin-Madison","Washington State University Pullman"],"keyword":["Adipogenesis","Candidate gene","Muscle Development","Myogenesis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"key genes regulating skeletal muscle development and growth in farm animals","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ani11030835","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-174175","identifier":[{"id":"85102436697","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33809500","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7999090","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-4ebedde1-bf71-421f-a70a-9d3417b8f6cc"],"keyword":["Adipogenesis","Candidate gene","Meat yield","Muscle development","Myogenesis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-78F4226783CA6368F623611B2639B046"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ani11030835","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ir","key":"shahid bahonar university of kerman","loc":["Iran","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Shahid Bahonar University of Kerman","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Center for Quantitative Genetics and Genomics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"washington state university pullman","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Washington State University Pullman","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of wisconsin madison","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Wisconsin-Madison","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammadreza","key":"mohammadabadipau","last":"Mohammadabadi","name":"Mohammadabadi, Mohammadreza","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Farhad","key":"bordbarpau","last":"Bordbar","name":"Bordbar, Farhad","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Just","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"fd33639a-638e-4eca-b152-71c93ab91293","name":"Jensen, Just","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Min","key":"dupau","last":"Du","name":"Du, Min","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Wei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33809500"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/ani11030835","issn":["20762615"],"issue":"3","journal":"Animals","paperid":"835","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Animals","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85102436697"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4ebedde1-bf71-421f-a70a-9d3417b8f6cc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Key genes regulating skeletal muscle development and growth in farm animals","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-174175","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Gastrointestinal tract (GIT) microbiomes in ruminants play major roles in host health and thus animal production. However, we lack an integrated understanding of microbial community structure and function as prior studies. are predominantly biased towards the rumen. Therefore, to acquire a microbiota inventory of the discrete GIT compartments, In this study, we used shotgun metagenomics to profile the microbiota of 370 samples that represent 10 GIT regions of seven ruminant species. Results: Our analyses reconstructed a GIT microbial reference catalog with > 154 million nonredundant genes and identified 8745 uncultured candidate species from over 10,000 metagenome-assembled genomes. The integrated gene catalog across the GIT regions demonstrates spatial associations between the microbiome and physiological adaptations, and 8745 newly characterized genomes substantially expand the genomic landscape of ruminant microbiota, particularly those from the lower gut. This substantially expands the previously known set of endogenous microbial diversity and the taxonomic classification rate of the GIT microbiome. These candidate species encode hundreds of enzymes and novel biosynthetic gene clusters that improve our understanding concerning methane production and feed efficiency in ruminants. Overall, this study expands the characterization of the ruminant GIT microbiota at unprecedented spatial resolution and offers clues for improving ruminant livestock production in the future. Conclusions: Having access to a comprehensive gene catalog and collections of microbial genomes provides the ability to perform efficiently genome-based analysis to achieve a detailed classification of GIT microbial ecosystem composition. Our study will bring unprecedented power in future association studies to investigate the impact of the GIT microbiota in ruminant health and production.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Xie, Fei","Jin, Wei","Si, Huazhe","Yuan, Yuan","Tao, Ye","Liu, Junhua","Wang, Xiaoxu","Yang, Chengjian","Li, Qiushuang","Yan, Xiaoting","Lin, Limei","Jiang, Qian","Zhang, Lei","Guo, Changzheng","Greening, Chris","Heller, Rasmus","Guan, Le Luo","Pope, Phillip B.","Tan, Zhiliang","Zhu, Weiyun","Wang, Min","Qiu, Qiang","Li, Zhipeng","Mao, Shengyong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-463678"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Shanghai Biozeron Biotechnology Co., Ltd (Biz)"],"keyword":["Alphaproteobacteria","Complex","Cow","Efficiency","Evolution","Feed efficiency","Gastrointestinal Microbiome","Insights","Metagenome assembled genomes","Read alignment","Reveals","Rumen microbiome","Ruminant","TOOL"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an integrated gene catalog and over 000000000010 000000000000 metagenome assembled genomes from the gastrointestinal microbiome of ruminants","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40168-021-01078-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-463678","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8199421","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34118976","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85107896416","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000663032200003","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-7577b911-3d7d-4c7e-a763-33f4f56ff619"],"keyword":["Alphaproteobacteria","COMPLEX","COW","EFFICIENCY","EVOLUTION","Feed efficiency","Gastrointestinal microbiome","INSIGHTS","Metagenome-assembled genomes","READ ALIGNMENT","REVEALS","RNA-SEQ DATA","RUMEN MICROBIOME","Ruminant","TOOL"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5D2B2D117A6AB83F60B4093F9E7119FC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40168-021-01078-x","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/273372105/An_integrated_gene_catalog_and_over_10_000_metagenome_assembled_genomes_from_the_gastrointestinal_microbiome_of_ruminants.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"shanghai biozeron biotechnology co ltd","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai Biozeron Biotechnology Co., Ltd (Biz)","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Computational and RNA Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Fei","key":"xiefeipau","last":"Xie","name":"Xie, Fei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wei","key":"jinweipau","last":"Jin","name":"Jin, Wei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Huazhe","key":"sihuazhepau","last":"Si","name":"Si, Huazhe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yuan","key":"yuanyuanpau","last":"Yuan","name":"Yuan, Yuan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ye","key":"taoyepau","last":"Tao","name":"Tao, Ye","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Junhua","key":"liujunhuapau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Junhua","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiaoxu","key":"wangxiaoxupau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Xiaoxu","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Chengjian","key":"yangchengjianpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Chengjian","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Qiushuang","key":"liqiushuangpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Qiushuang","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiaoting","key":"yanxiaotingpau","last":"Yan","name":"Yan, Xiaoting","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Limei","key":"linlimeipau","last":"Lin","name":"Lin, Limei","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Qian","key":"jiangqianpau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Qian","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lei","key":"zhangleipau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Lei","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Changzheng","key":"guochangzhengpau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Changzheng","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Chris","key":"greeningchrispau","last":"Greening","name":"Greening, Chris","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rasmus","key":"hellerrasmuspau","last":"Heller","locid":"efbe80a4-e869-43e8-b962-989c40c79f93","name":"Heller, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0001-6583-6923","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Le Luo","key":"guanleluopau","last":"Guan","name":"Guan, Le Luo","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Phillip B.","key":"popephillipbpau","last":"Pope","name":"Pope, Phillip B.","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Zhiliang","key":"tanzhiliangpau","last":"Tan","name":"Tan, Zhiliang","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Weiyun","key":"zhuweiyunpau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Weiyun","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Min","key":"wangminpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Min","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Qiang","key":"qiuqiangpau","last":"Qiu","name":"Qiu, Qiang","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Zhipeng","key":"lizhipengpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Zhipeng","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Shengyong","key":"maoshengyongpau","last":"Mao","name":"Mao, Shengyong","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34118976"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s40168-021-01078-x","issn":["20492618"],"journal":"Microbiome","paperid":"137","status":"p","title":"Microbiome","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85107896416"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7577b911-3d7d-4c7e-a763-33f4f56ff619"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An integrated gene catalog and over 10,000 metagenome-assembled genomes from the gastrointestinal microbiome of ruminants","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-463678","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The tumor immune microenvironment is influenced by the epigenetic landscape of the tumor. Here, we have identified the SETDB1–TRIM28 complex as a critical suppressor of antitumor immunity. An epigenetic CRISPR–Cas9 screen of 1,218 chromatin regulators identified TRIM28 as a suppressor of PD-L1 expression. We then revealed that expression of the SETDB1–TRIM28 complex negatively correlated with infiltration of effector CD8+ T cells. Inhibition of SETDB1–TRIM28 simultaneously upregulated PD-L1 and activated the cyclic GMP–AMP synthase (cGAS)–stimulator of interferon genes (STING) innate immune response pathway to increase infiltration of CD8+ T cells. Mechanistically, SETDB1–TRIM28 inhibition led to micronuclei formation in the cytoplasm, which is known to activate the cGAS–STING pathway. Thus, SETDB1–TRIM28 inhibition bridges innate and adaptive immunity. Indeed, SETDB1 knockout enhanced the antitumor effects of immune checkpoint blockade with anti–PD-L1 in a mouse model of ovarian cancer in a cGAS-dependent manner. Our findings establish the SETDB1–TRIM28 complex as a regulator of antitumor immunity and demonstrate that its loss activates cGAS–STING innate immunity to boost the antitumor effects of immune checkpoint blockade.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Lin, Jianhuang","Guo, Dajiang","Liu, Heng","Zhou, Wei","Wang, Chen","Müller, Iris","Kossenkov, Andrew, V","Drapkin, Ronny","Bitler, Benjamin G.","Helin, Kristian","Zhang, Rugang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-541597"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the setdb000000000001 trim000000000028 complex suppresses antitumor immunity","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8647838/","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-541597","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8647838","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34848497","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85121972916","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000727264200001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-f830c32e-200f-4812-b7de-eee5d7487b60"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6B51D6A0C28BECECAF5229A546C0CA0A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8647838/","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, BRIC, Helin Group","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, The Danish Stem Cell Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"memorial sloan kettering cancer center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Jianhuang","key":"linpau","last":"Lin","name":"Lin, Jianhuang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Dajiang","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Dajiang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Heng","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Heng","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wei","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Wei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Chen","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Chen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Iris","key":"mullerpau","last":"Muller","locid":"485e7da4-f9b0-4038-ac4d-46dc32d66b12","name":"Müller, Iris","name_org":"Muller, Iris","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrew, V","key":"kossenkovpau","last":"Kossenkov","name":"Kossenkov, Andrew, V","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ronny","key":"drapkinpau","last":"Drapkin","name":"Drapkin, Ronny","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Benjamin G.","key":"bitlerpau","last":"Bitler","name":"Bitler, Benjamin G.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Kristian","key":"helinpau","last":"Helin","locid":"b95e097b-b1b4-44db-b097-0c3990dadf63","name":"Helin, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0003-1975-6097","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rugang","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Rugang","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34848497"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1158/2326-6066.cir-21-0754","issn":["23266066","23266074"],"issn_org":["23266066"],"issue":"12","journal":"Cancer Immunology Research","pages":"1413-1424","status":"p","title":"Cancer Immunology Research","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121972916"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f830c32e-200f-4812-b7de-eee5d7487b60"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The SETDB1-TRIM28 Complex Suppresses Antitumor Immunity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-541597","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In 2008 we published the first set of guidelines for standardizing research in autophagy. Since then, research on this topic has continued to accelerate, and many new scientists have entered the field. Our knowledge base and relevant new technologies have also been expanding. Accordingly, it is important to update these guidelines formonitoring autophagy in different organisms. Various reviews have described the range of assays that have been used for this purpose. Nevertheless, there continues to be confusion regarding acceptable methods to measure autophagy, especially in multicellular eukaryotes. A key point that needs to be emphasized is that there is a Do not distribute. difference between measurements that monitor the numbers or volume of autophagic elements (e.g., autophagosomes or autolysosomes) at any stage of the autophagic process vs. those that measure flux through the autophagy pathway (i.e., the complete process); thus, a block in macroautophagy that results in autophagosome accumulation needs to be differentiated fromstimuli that result in increased autophagic activity, defined as increased autophagy induction coupled with increased delivery to, and degradation within, lysosomes (in most higher eukaryotes and some protists such as Dictyostelium) or the vacuole (in plants and fungi). In other words, it is especially important that investigators new to the field understand that the appearance of more autophagosomes does not necessarily equate withmore autophagy. In fact, in many cases, autophagosomes accumulate because of a block in trafficking to lysosomes without a concomitant change in autophagosome biogenesis,whereas an increase in autolysosomes may reflect a reduction in degradative activity. Here, we present a set of guidelines for the selection and interpretation of methods for use by investigators who aim to examine macroautophagy and related processes, as well as for reviewers who need to provide realistic and reasonable critiques of papers that are focused on these processes. These guidelines are not meant to be a formulaic set of rules, because the appropriate assays depend in part on the question being asked and the system being used. In addition, we emphasize that no individual assay is guaranteed to be themost appropriate one in every situation, and we strongly recommend the use of multiple assays to monitor autophagy. In these guidelines, we consider these various methods of assessing autophagy and what information can, or cannot, be obtained from them. Finally, by discussing the merits and limits of particular autophagy assays, we hope to encourage technical innovation in the field.","author_count":2922,"contributors":["Klionsky, Daniel J","Abdel-Aziz, Amal Kamal","Abdelfatah, Sara","Abdellatif, Mahmoud","Abdoli, Asghar","Abel, Steffen","Abeliovich, Hagai","Abildgaard, Marie H","Abudu, Yakubu Princely","Acevedo-Arozena, Abraham","Adamopoulos, Iannis E","Adeli, Khosrow","Adolph, Timon E","Adornetto, Annagrazia","Aflaki, Elma","Agam, Galila","Agarwal, Anupam","Aggarwal, Bharat B","Agnello, Maria","Agostinis, Patrizia","Agrewala, Javed N","Agrotis, Alexander","Aguilar, Patricia V","Ahmad, S Tariq","Ahmed, Zubair M","Ahumada-Castro, Ulises","Aits, Sonja","Aizawa, Shu","Akkoc, Yunus","Akoumianaki, Tonia","Akpinar, Hafize Aysin","Al-Abd, Ahmed M","Al-Akra, Lina","Al-Gharaibeh, Abeer","Alaoui-Jamali, Moulay A","Alberti, Simon","Alcocer-Gómez, Elísabet","Alessandri, Cristiano","Ali, Muhammad","Alim Al-Bari, M Abdul","Aliwaini, Saeb","Alizadeh, Javad","Almacellas, Eugènia","Almasan, Alexandru","Alonso, Alicia","Alonso, Guillermo D","Altan-Bonnet, Nihal","Altieri, Dario C","Álvarez, Élida M C","Alves, Sara","Alves da Costa, Cristine","Alzaharna, Mazen M","Amadio, Marialaura","Amantini, Consuelo","Amaral, Cristina","Ambrosio, Susanna","Amer, Amal O","Ammanathan, Veena","An, Zhenyi","Andersen, Stig U","Andrabi, Shaida A","Andrade-Silva, Magaiver","Andres, Allen M","Angelini, Sabrina","Ann, David",