{"abstract":"Purpose: This study aimed to investigate the prevalence, risk factors, and effects of primary nocturnal enuresis (PNE) on physical and mental health in young adults in mainland China. Methods: An anonymous questionnaire was used to collect information including the sociodemographic characteristics, history of PNE, family history, daytime voiding symptoms, Pittsburgh Sleep Quality Index (PSQI) scores, Self-Esteem Scale (SES), and Self-Rating Depression Scale (SDS). A total of 22,500 university students from 23 provinces and 368 cities in mainland China were included. Results: In total, 21,082 questionnaires were collected, and 20,345 of them qualified for statistical analysis. The PNE prevalence was 1.17%, and the distribution of monosymptomatic nocturnal enuresis (MNE) and nonmonosymptomatic nocturnal enuresis (NMNE) was 66.1% and 33.9%, respectively. In total, 28% of respondents with PNE reported bedwetting daily, 31.6% between 1 and 7 times weekly, and 40.4% between 1 and 4 times monthly; 80% of PNE cases had no history of treatment. The prevalence of PNE in patients with a family history, frequency, urgency, urinary incontinence, and recurrent urinary tract infections was significantly higher than in those without these conditions (P<0.001). PNE was significantly correlated with the PSQI total score (sleep quality) (P=0.011). The SES score was lower and the SDS was higher (P<0.001) in the PNE group than in those without PNE. Conclusions: In mainland China, the PNE prevalence among young adults was found to be high, and PNE had significant effects on physical and mental health. Risk factors included a family history, daytime voiding symptoms, and lack of treatment.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Hu, Hui Jie","Zhang, Zhen Wei","Liang, Yu","Luo, Yan Yan","Dou, Qi Feng","Song, Cui Ping","Zhang, Hui Min","Zhao, Ying","Tian, Guang Run","Zhang, Ke","Mao, Qiu Fang","Song, Jing Gui","Rittig, Søren","Wen, Jian Guo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-147871"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Zhengzhou University"],"keyword":["Mental health","Prevalence","Risk Factors","Young adults"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prevalence risk factors and psychological effects of primary nocturnal enuresis in chinese young adults","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85104501168","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-147871","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8022166","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85104501168","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33819961","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-205d354e-84c4-44dc-a616-146a23736c04"],"keyword":["Mental health","Prevalence","Primary nocturnal enuresis","Risk factors","Young adults"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-849BA6B799111BA6105F99FE8317FF89"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"zhengzhou university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhengzhou University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hui Jie","key":"huhuijiepau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Hui Jie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhen Wei","key":"zhangzhenweipau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Zhen Wei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yu","key":"liangyupau","last":"Liang","name":"Liang, Yu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yan Yan","key":"luoyanyanpau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Yan Yan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qi Feng","key":"douqifengpau","last":"Dou","name":"Dou, Qi Feng","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cui Ping","key":"songcuipingpau","last":"Song","name":"Song, Cui Ping","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hui Min","key":"zhanghuiminpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Hui Min","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ying","key":"zhaoyingpau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Ying","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guang Run","key":"tianguangrunpau","last":"Tian","name":"Tian, Guang Run","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ke","key":"zhangkepau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Ke","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qiu Fang","key":"maoqiufangpau","last":"Mao","name":"Mao, Qiu Fang","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jing Gui","key":"songjingguipau","last":"Song","name":"Song, Jing Gui","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Soren","key":"rittigsørenpau","last":"Rittig","locid":"04c8afe2-7baf-4f75-a08b-d2ee25d66d09","name":"Rittig, Søren","name_org":"Rittig, Soren","orcid":"0000-0001-7038-1652","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jian Guo","key":"wenjianguopau","last":"Wen","name":"Wen, Jian Guo","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33819961"],"pub":{"doi":"10.5213/inj.2040398.149","issn":["20934777","20936931"],"issn_org":["20934777"],"issue":"1","journal":"International neurourology journal","pages":"84-92","publisher":"Korean Continence Society","status":"p","title":"International neurourology journal","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85104501168"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-205d354e-84c4-44dc-a616-146a23736c04"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Prevalence, Risk Factors, and Psychological Effects of Primary Nocturnal Enuresis in Chinese Young Adults","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-147871","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Extractive distillation (ED) can be used to separate mixtures with low relative volatilities that are even close to unity. It is widely adopted for the separation of aromatics and nonaromatics in the petrochemical industry. Selecting a suitable solvent is of paramount importance to ED processes. Ionic liquids (ILs) are increasingly being considered as potential options to replace organic solvents in ED processes due to their favorable properties including high boiling points and extremely low volatilities. In this work, a nonexperimental solvent screening approach, i.e., computer-aided ionic liquid design (CAILD), is employed to identify the optimal ILs. Using a novel design objective and several structural and property constraints on IL, we have identified 1,3-dimethylpyridinium tetrafluoroborate ([C1mPy][BF4]) as the best IL solvent by solving a formulated CAILD-based mixed-integer nonlinear programming problem. The separation performance of this IL is further evaluated with rigorous process simulation in Aspen Plus. Besides, process simulation of the aromatic ED process using sulfolane as the benchmark organic solvent is performed. Furthermore, a systematic analysis of the energy consumption and the process economy is conducted by investigating the optimized simulation results of the studied aromatic ED process. The [C1mPy][BF4]-based process with an assumed IL price of 50 $/kg can reduce the capital cost by 35.2%, the operating cost by 11.8%, and the total annual cost by 31.2%. The IL price at the break-even point of replacing sulfolane with [C1mPy][BF4] in the aromatic ED process is 91.03 $/kg.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Lei, Yang","Zhou, Yuhang","Wei, Zhiqiang","Chen, Yuqiu","Guo, Fen","Yan, Wei"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-308403"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Chen, Yuqiu","Lei, Yang"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","SINOPEC","Wuhan University of Science and Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"optimal design of an ionic liquid il based aromatic extractive distillation process involving energy and economic evaluation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85102036986","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was financially supported by the National Nature Science Foundation of China project (No. 21706198) and the China Scholarship Council project (Nos. 201908420380 and 201708440264)."],"id":"S01-000.00-308403","identifier":[{"id":"85102036986","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-0cb992a9-9a76-4999-aaad-64ddcfff360a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E21E8AF5D8FEC2585632A50B8D3321F3"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"wuhan university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Wuhan University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"sinopec","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"SINOPEC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yang","key":"leipau","last":"Lei","locid":"0ef8bae4-720a-4e83-94c9-9450d43fb75d","name":"Lei, Yang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuhang","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Yuhang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhiqiang","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Zhiqiang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yuqiu","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","locid":"82b0f303-9c7b-4fd2-a066-c87732faa675","name":"Chen, Yuqiu","orcid":"0000-0003-0706-160X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Fen","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Fen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Wei","key":"yanpau","last":"Yan","locid":"23ab3789-6a8a-465d-9f5f-bb8c94fddb4d","name":"Yan, Wei","orcid":"0000-0002-8810-2479","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.iecr.0c05183","issn":["08885885","15205045"],"issn_org":["08885885"],"issue":"9","journal":"Industrial & Engineering Chemistry Research","pages":"3605-3616","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Industrial & Engineering Chemistry Research","title_org":"Industrial and Engineering Chemistry Research","volume":"60"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85102036986"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-0cb992a9-9a76-4999-aaad-64ddcfff360a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Optimal design of an ionic liquid (IL)-based aromatic extractive distillation process involving energy and economic evaluation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-308403","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Chinese mahogany (Toona sinensis) is a woody plant that is widely cultivated in China and Malaysia. Toona sinensis is important economically, including as a nutritious food source, as material for traditional Chinese medicine and as a high-quality hardwood. However, the absence of a reference genome has hindered in-depth molecular and evolutionary studies of this plant. In this study, we report a high-quality T. sinensis genome assembly, with scaffolds anchored to 28 chromosomes and a total assembled length of 596 Mb (contig N50 = 1.5 Mb and scaffold N50 = 21.5 Mb). A total of 34,345 genes were predicted in the genome after homology-based and de novo annotation analyses. Evolutionary analysis showed that the genomes of T. sinensis and Populus trichocarpa diverged ~99.1-103.1 million years ago, and the T. sinensis genome underwent a recent genome-wide duplication event at ~7.8 million years and one more ancient whole genome duplication event at ~71.5 million years. These results provide a high-quality chromosome-level reference genome for T. sinensis and confirm its evolutionary position at the genomic level. Such information will offer genomic resources to study the molecular mechanism of terpenoid biosynthesis and the formation of flavour compounds, which will further facilitate its molecular breeding. As the first chromosome-level genome assembled in the family Meliaceae, it will provide unique insights into the evolution of members of the Meliaceae.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Ji, Yun-Tao","Xiu, Zhihui","Chen, Chun-Hai","Wang, Youru","Yang, Jing-Xia","Sui, Juan-Juan","Jiang, San-Jie","Wang, Ping","Yue, Shao-Yun","Zhang, Qian-Qian","Jin, Ji-Liang","Wang, Guo-Shu","Wei, Qian-Qian","Wei, Bing","Wang, Juan","Zhang, Hai-Lin","Zhang, Qiu-Yan","Liu, Jun","Liu, Chang-Jin","Jian, Jianbo","Qu, Chang-Qing"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-352288"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Jian, Jianbo","Liu, Chang-Jin","Liu, Jun","Qu, Chang-Qing"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI Group","Chinese Academy of Forestry","Forestry Nursery of Taihe County","Fuyang Normal University","Hubei Normal University","Tianjin University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Evolution","Hi C","Nanopore","Whole genome duplication"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long read sequencing of i toona sinensis i a juss roem a chromosome level reference genome for the family meliaceae","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85099921388","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-352288","identifier":[{"id":"85099921388","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33421343","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-9fe3bc61-5c33-4308-963c-87ee932ae42f"],"keyword":["Evolution","Hi-C","Nanopore","Toona sinensis","Whole genome duplication"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-74F7902AD50A9B0F9A6A2AB566B74007"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"fuyang normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Fuyang Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"bgi group","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI Group","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"hubei normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hubei Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"forestry nursery of taihe county","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Forestry Nursery of Taihe County","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of forestry","lo