All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-87bf00a0-26c7-4e8a-9c46-0155101801db"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Multi-ancestry genome-wide gene-sleep interactions identify novel loci for blood pressure","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-474629","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Biological aging estimators derived from DNA methylation data are heritable and correlate with morbidity and mortality. Consequently, identification of genetic and environmental contributors to the variation in these measures in populations has become a major goal in the field. Results: Leveraging DNA methylation and SNP data from more than 40,000 individuals, we identify 137 genome-wide significant loci, of which 113 are novel, from genome-wide association study (GWAS) meta-analyses of four epigenetic clocks and epigenetic surrogate markers for granulocyte proportions and plasminogen activator inhibitor 1 levels, respectively. We find evidence for shared genetic loci associated with the Horvath clock and expression of transcripts encoding genes linked to lipid metabolism and immune function. Notably, these loci are independent of those reported to regulate DNA methylation levels at constituent clock CpGs. A polygenic score for GrimAge acceleration showed strong associations with adiposity-related traits, educational attainment, parental longevity, and C-reactive protein levels. Conclusion: This study illuminates the genetic architecture underlying epigenetic aging and its shared genetic contributions with lifestyle factors and longevity.","author_count":51,"contributors":["McCartney, Daniel L.","Min, Josine L.","Richmond, Rebecca C.","Lu, Ake T.","Sobczyk, Maria K.","Davies, Gail","Broer, Linda","Guo, Xiuqing","Jeong, Ayoung","Jung, Jeesun","Kasela, Silva","Katrinli, Seyma","Kuo, Pei Lun","Matias-Garcia, Pamela R.","Mishra, Pashupati P.","Nygaard, Marianne","Palviainen, Teemu","Patki, Amit","Raffield, Laura M.","Ratliff, Scott M.","Richardson, Tom G.","Robinson, Oliver","Sørensen, Mette","Sun, Dianjianyi","Tsai, Pei Chien","van der Zee, Matthijs D.","Walker, Rosie M.","Wang, Xiaochuan","Wang, Yunzhang","Xia, Rui","Xu, Zongli","Yao, Jie","Zhao, Wei","Correa, Adolfo","Boerwinkle, Eric","Dugué, Pierre Antoine","Durda, Peter","Elliott, Hannah R.","Gieger, Christian","de Geus, Eco J.C.","Harris, Sarah E.","Hemani, Gibran","Imboden, Medea","Kähönen, Mika","Kardia, Sharon L.R.","Kresovich, Jacob K.","Li, Shengxu","Lunetta, Kathryn L.","Mengel-From, Jonas","Christensen, Kaare","Marioni, Riccardo E"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-621626"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["NHLBI Trans-Omics for Precision Medicine (TOPMed) Consortium","The Genetics of DNA Methylation Consortium"],"corresponding_author":["Marioni, Riccardo E"],"country":["Australia","China","Estonia","Finland","Germany","Netherlands","Sweden","Switzerland","Taiwan","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Amsterdam Public Health","Boston University School of Public Health","Bristol Medical School","Cancer Council Victoria","Chang Gung Memorial Hospital","Chang Gung University","Children's Minnesota","Emory University","Erasmus University Medical Center Rotterdam","Institute of Human Genetics, Helmholtz Zentrum München","Karolinska Institute","King's College London","Los Angeles Biomedical Research Institute","MRC Integrative Epidemiology Unit","McGovern Medical School and School of Dentistry UT Health at Houston","Monash University","National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences","National Institute on Aging","National Institutes of Health","Peking University","Swiss Tropical and Public Health Institute (Swiss TPH)","Tampere University","Tampere University Hospital","Technical University of Munich","The University of Edinburgh","The University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston","University of Alabama at Birmingham","University of Basel","University of Helsinki","University of Melbourne","University of Michigan","University of Mississippi Medical Center","University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill","University of Southern California","University of Tartu","University of Vermont","Vrije University Amsterdam"],"keyword":["DNA methylation","Epigenetic clock","GWAS"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genome wide association studies identify 000000000137 genetic loci for dna methylation biomarkers of aging","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13059-021-02398-9","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["REM, SH, and AL are supported by a National Institute of Health U01 grant, U01AG060908–01. REM and DLM are supported by Alzheimer’s Research UK major project grant, ARUK-PG2017B-10. RCR is a de Pass Vice Chancellor’s Research Fellow at the University of Bristol. CR and RCR receive support from a Cancer Research UK Program Grant (C18281/A191169). CLR, JLM, and RCR are members of the UK Medical Research Council Integrative Epidemiology Unit at the University of Bristol (MC_UU_00011/5). IJD is supported by Age UK (Disconnected Mind program), UKRI Medical Research Council grant, MR/R0245065/1, and by National Institute of Health R01 grant, 1R01AG054628-01A1. GD is supported by the University of Edinburgh School of Philosophy, Psychology and Language Sciences. Molecular data for the Trans-Omics in Precision Medicine (TOPMed) program was supported by the National Heart, Lung and Blood Institute (NHLBI). Core support including centralized genomic read mapping and genotype calling, along with variant quality metrics and filtering were provided by the TOPMed Informatics Research Center (3R01HL-117626-02S1; contract HHSN268201800002I). Core support including phenotype harmonization, data management, sample-identity QC, and general program coordination were provided by the TOPMed Data Coordinating Center (R01HL-120393; U01HL-120393; contract HHSN268201800001I). We gratefully acknowledge the studies and participants who provided biological samples and data for TOPMed. Cohort-specific acknowledgements are presented in Additional file ."],"id":"S01-000.00-621626","identifier":[{"id":"85109008239","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8243879","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34187551","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-a90c7edb-1405-4e99-93ff-87a5891adcba"],"keyword":["DNA methylation","Epigenetic clock","GWAS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-35F71059E8546238FCB81706ADB4CABA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13059-021-02398-9","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/184337761/s13059_021_02398_9.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"the university of edinburgh","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"The University of Edinburgh","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"mrc integrative epidemiology unit","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"MRC Integrative Epidemiology Unit","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"bristol medical school","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Bristol Medical School","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of southern california","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Southern California","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"nl","key":"erasmus university medical center rotterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Erasmus University Medical Center Rotterdam","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"los angeles biomedical research institute","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Los Angeles Bi