{"abstract":"The consensus of the Asia Pacific Heart Rhythm Society (APHRS) on stroke prevention in atrial fibrillation (AF) has been published in 2017 which provided useful clinical guidance for cardiologists, neurologists, geriatricians, and general practitioners in Asia-Pacific region. In these years, many important new data regarding stroke prevention in AF were reported. The Practice Guidelines subcommittee members comprehensively reviewed updated information on stroke prevention in AF, and summarized them in this 2021 focused update of the 2017 consensus guidelines of the APHRS on stroke prevention in AF. We highlighted and focused on several issues, including the importance of AF Better Care (ABC) pathway, the advantages of non–vitamin K antagonist oral anticoagulants (NOACs) for Asians, the considerations of use of NOACs for Asian patients with AF with single 1 stroke risk factor beyond gender, the role of lifestyle factors on stroke risk, the use of oral anticoagulants during the “coronavirus disease 2019” (COVID-19) pandemic, etc. We fully realize that there are gaps, unaddressed questions, and many areas of uncertainty and debate in the current knowledge of AF, and the physician's decision remains the most important factor in the management of AF.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Chao, Tze Fan","Joung, Boyoung","Takahashi, Yoshihide","Lim, Toon Wei","Choi, Eue Keun","Chan, Yi Hsin","Guo, Yutao","Sriratanasathavorn, Charn","Oh, Seil","Okumura, Ken","Lip, Gregory Y H"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-064665"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Chao, Tze Fan"],"country":["China","Japan","Singapore","South Korea","Taiwan","Thailand","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chang Gung Memorial Hospital","Chang Gung University","General Hospital of People's Liberation Army","Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","National University Hospital, Singapore","National Yang Ming Chiao Tung University","Saiseikai Kumamoto Hospital","Seoul National University Hospital","Siriraj Hospital","Tokyo Medical and Dental University","University of Liverpool","Veterans General Hospital-Taipei","Yonsei University"],"keyword":["APHRS","Atrial fibrillation","Consensus guidelines","Stroke prevention"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000002021 focused update of the 000000002017 consensus guidelines of the asia pacific heart rhythm society aphrs on stroke prevention in atrial fibrillation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/joa3.12652","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Tze‐Fan Chao: None. Boyoung Joung: Boyoung Joung has served as a speaker for Bayer, BMS/Pfizer, Medtronic, and Daiichi‐Sankyo and received research funds from Samjin, Medtronic and Abbott. No fees have been received directly or personally. Yoshihide Takahashi: Research grants from Medtronic Japan, Boston Scientific, Japan Lifeline, WIN International, Abbott and Biosense‐Webster, and speaker honoraria from Abbott and Biosense‐Webster. Toon‐Wei Lim: None. Eue‐Keun Choi: None. Yi‐Hsin Chan: None. Yutao Guo: None. Charn Sriratanasathavorn: None. Seil Oh: None. Ken Okumura: None. Gregory Lip: Consultant and speaker for BMS/Pfizer, Boehringer Ingelheim and Daiichi‐Sankyo. No fees are received personally."],"id":"S01-000.00-064665","identifier":[{"id":"34887945","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85119258572","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-327491d0-d203-4221-977d-c7eb5067e4db"],"keyword":["APHRS","atrial fibrillation","consensus guidelines","stroke prevention"],"lang":"English","l