{"abstract":"Power converters have been key enablers of many energy conversion fields, and it is a trend to apply artificial intelligent (AI) technology to power converters to improve stability. A novel fault diagnosis method based on the combination of random forests (RFs) and feature transformation is proposed in this paper. Firstly, the three-phase AC fault currents of threephase PWM rectifier are analyzed as examples. Secondly, the feature transformation, a novel current trajectories slopes based method, is adopted to transform the fault currents data. With the help of feature transformation, the fault diagnosis classifier can obtain a good load adaptability. And then the RFs based method, a data-driven method, is employed to train the fault diagnosis classifier with the fault current trajectories slopes data. Finally, the proposed method is carried out on an three-phase PWM rectifier system, which can detect and locate the open-circuit faults of IGBTs.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Kou, Lei","Liu, Chuang","Cai, Guo-wei","Zhang, Zhe","Li, Xue-jiao","Yuan, Quan-de"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-350605"],"event":{"end":"2020-12-02","place":"Nanjing, cn","start":"2020-11-29","title":"2020 IEEE 9<sup>th</sup> International Power Electronics and Motion Control Conference","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Changchun Institute of Technology","Harbin Institute of Technology","Northeast Electric Power University"],"keyword":["Data driven","Fault diagnosis","Power converters","Random forests"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fault diagnosis for power converters based on random forests and feature transformation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/235513485/Wed9_7_Fault_Diagnosis_for_Power_Converters_Based_on_Random_Forests_and_Feature_Transformation.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-350605","identifier":[{"id":"85103187786","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9a65457c-49be-4d81-813c-eb5cd10bf94b"],"keyword":["Current trajectories slopes","Data-driven","Fault diagnosis","Feature transformation","Power converters","Random forests"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-9ACBB07CCD2AB26F9D75F4C70C5B44C0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/235513485/Wed9_7_Fault_Diagnosis_for_Power_Converters_Based_on_Random_Forests_and_Feature_Transformation.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"northeast electric power university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northeast Electric Power University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Electronics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"harbin institute of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Harbin Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"changchun institute of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Changchun Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lei","key":"koupau","last":"Kou","name":"Kou, Lei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chuang","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Chuang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guo-wei","key":"caipau","last":"Cai","name":"Cai, Guo-wei","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhe","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"eebd7cda-144d-4f72-a6a7-2e8339aec75e","name":"Zhang, Zhe","orcid":"0000-0001-8407-3167","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Xue-jiao","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xue-jiao","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Quan-de","key":"yuanpau","last":"Yuan","name":"Yuan, Quan-de","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ipemc-ecceasia48364.2020.9367970","isbn":["9781728153025"],"pages":"1821-1826","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2020 IEEE 9<sup>th</sup> International Power Electronics and Motion Control Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9a65457c-49be-4d81-813c-eb5cd10bf94b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Fault Diagnosis for Power Converters based on Random Forests and Feature Transformation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-350605","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Ducks have a typical avian karyotype that consists of macro-and microchromosomes, but a pair of much less differentiated ZW sex chromosomes compared to chickens. To elucidate the evolution of chromosome architectures between ducks and chickens, and between birds and mammals, we produced a nearly complete chromosomal assembly of a female Pekin duck by combining long-read sequencing and multiplatform scaffolding techniques. Results: A major improvement of genome assembly and annotation quality resulted from the successful resolution of lineage-specific propagated repeats that fragmented the previous Illumina-based assembly. We found that the duck topologically associated domains (TAD) are demarcated by putative binding sites of the insulator protein CTCF, housekeeping genes, or transitions of active/inactive chromatin compartments, indicating conserved mechanisms of spatial chromosome folding with mammals. There are extensive overlaps of TAD boundaries between duck and chicken, and also between the TAD boundaries and chromosome inversion breakpoints. This suggests strong natural selection pressure on maintaining regulatory domain integrity, or vulnerability of TAD boundaries to DNA double-strand breaks. The duck W chromosome retains 2.5-fold more genes relative to chicken. Similar to the independently evolved human Y chromosome, the duck W evolved massive dispersed palindromic structures, and a pattern of sequence divergence with the Z chromosome that reflects stepwise suppression of homologous recombination. Conclusions: Our results provide novel insights into the conserved and convergently evolved chromosome features of birds and mammals, and also importantly add to the genomic resources for poultry studies.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Li, Jing","Zhang, Jilin","Liu, Jing","Zhou, Yang","Cai, Cheng","Xu, Luohao","Dai, Xuelei","Feng, Shaohong","Guo, Chunxue","Rao, Jinpeng","Wei, Kai","Jarvis, Erich D.","Jiang, Yu","Zhou, Zhengkui","Zhang, Guojie","Zhou, Qi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-416714"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI"],"keyword":["Chromosome Inversion","Sex Chromosomes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a new duck genome reveals conserved and convergently evolved chromosome architectures of birds and mammals","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/gigascience/giaa142","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-416714","identifier":[{"id":"85100230777","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7787181","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33406261","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-26e20b5e-3f00-4c47-8e9c-83a6334a12ec"],"keyword":["chromosome inversion","duck genome","sex chromosomes","topologically associated domain"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-145784F98DD4DF771039E5775866020D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/257324621/A_new_duck_genome_reveals_conserved_and_convergently_evolved_chromosome_architectures_of_birds_and_mammals.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/gigascience/giaa142","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"bgi","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","lo