d":"0a2a7ad3-1719-43c6-bdf3-c3491a43a8af","name":"Pedersen, Oluf","name_org":"Pedersen, Oluf Borbye","orcid":"0000-0002-3321-3972","rank":41,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Zhengquan","key":"yuzhengquanpau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Zhengquan","rank":42,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"15 16","first":"Stanislav Dusko","key":"ehrlichstanislavduskopau","last":"Ehrlich","name":"Ehrlich, Stanislav Dusko","rank":43,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Fazheng","key":"renfazhengpau","last":"Ren","name":"Ren, Fazheng","rank":44,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32241904"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/gutjnl-2019-319766","issn":["00175749","14683288"],"issn_org":["00175749"],"issue":"12","journal":"Gut","pages":"2131-2142","paperid":"319766","status":"p","title":"Gut","volume":"69"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85083286914"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1e761416-f215-463e-8e35-dce1aceca15c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Aberrant gut microbiota alters host metabolome and impacts renal failure in humans and rodents","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-411567","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Bestrophin-1 (BEST1) gene is associated with a wide range of ocular phenotypes, collectively termed as bestrophinopathy. The aim of the current study was to identify the mutation spectrum of BEST1 in a large cohort of Chinese patients with bestrophinopathy. Methods: Patients clinically suspected of bestrophinopathy were screened using multigene panel testing. All BEST1 variants were confirmed by Sanger sequencing, and validated in the families. Findings: A total of 92 patients (Best vitelliform macular dystrophy (BVMD)=77; autosomal recessive bestrophinopathy (ARB)=15) from 58 unrelated families of Chinese origin and their available family members (n=65) were recruited. Overall, 39 distinct disease-causing BEST1 variants were identified, including 13 novel variants, and two reported variants but novel for ARB. Of them, 14 were associated with ARB, 23 with BVMD and two (c.604C>T and c.898G>A) with both BVMD and ARB. Most mutations associated with BVMD were missense (97.78%), while ARB was associated with more complex mutations, including missense (88.46%), splicing effect (3.85%), and frameshifts (15.38%). BEST1 hotspots were c.898G>A and c.584C>T among BVMD and ARB patients, respectively. Hot regions were located in exons 8, 2 and 6 in BVMD patients, and in exons 5 and 7 in ARB patients. The overall penetrance of BEST1 in our cohort was 71.30%, no de novo mutations were identified. Conclusion: This is the largest study to date that provides major population-based data of the BEST1 mutation spectrum in China. Our results can serve as a well-founded reference for genetic counselling for patients with bestrophinopathy of Chinese origin.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Gao, Feng-Juan","Qi, Yu-He","Hu, Fang-Yuan","Wang, Dan-Dan","Xu, Ping","Guo, Jing-Li","Li, Jian-Kang","Zhang, Yong-Jin","Li, Wei","Chen, Fang","Xu, Ge-Zhi","Liu, Wei","Chang, Qing","Wu, Ji-Hong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-436714"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI"],"keyword":["Next generation sequencing","mutation spectrum"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mutation spectrum of the bestrophin 000000000001 gene in a large chinese cohort with bestrophinopathy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-436714","identifier":[{"id":"31519547","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85072296166","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-487d415f-a542-4a0f-9b37-fd83c8d22afa"],"keyword":["BEST1","bestrophinopathy","mutation spectrum","next-generation sequencing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7E4F9786DC690BBE7D25C70B8756C8C6"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"bgi","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Genome Research and Molecular Bio Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Feng-Juan","key":"gaofengjuanpau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Feng-Juan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yu-He","key":"qiyuhepau","last":"Qi","name":"Qi, Yu-He","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Fang-Yuan","key":"hufangyuanpau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Fang-Yuan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Dan-Dan","key":"wangdandanpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Dan-Dan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ping","key":"xupingpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Ping","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jing-Li","key":"guojinglipau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Jing-Li","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jian-Kang","key":"lijiankangpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Jian-Kang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yong-Jin","key":"zhangyongjinpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yong-Jin","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Wei","key":"liweipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Wei","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Fang","key":"chenfangpau","last":"Chen","locid":"243a3415-b38a-4784-83a9-eab1a5ba3ffe","name":"Chen, Fang","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ge-Zhi","key":"xugezhipau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Ge-Zhi","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wei","key":"liuweipau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Wei","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Qing","key":"changqingpau","last":"Chang","name":"Chang, Qing","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ji-Hong","key":"wujihongpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Ji-Hong","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31519547"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bjophthalmol-2019-314679","issn":["00071161","14682079"],"issn_org":["00071161"],"issue":"6","journal":"British Journal of Ophthalmology","pages":"846-851","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Ophthalmology","volume":"104"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85072296166"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-487d415f-a542-4a0f-9b37-fd83c8d22afa"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mutation spectrum of the bestrophin-1 gene in a large Chinese cohort with bestrophinopathy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-436714","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Node similarity search on graphs has wide applications in recommendation, link prediction, to name just a few. However, existing studies are insufficient due to two reasons: (i) the scale of the real-world graph is growing rapidly, and (ii) vertices are always associated with complex attributes. In this paper, we propose an efficiently distributed framework to support node similarity search on massive graphs, which considers both graph structure correlation and node attribute similarity in metric spaces. The framework consists of preprocessing stage and query stage. In the preprocessing stage, a parallel KD-tree construction (KDC) algorithm is developed to form a newly defined graph so-called hybrid graph, in order to integrate node attribute similarity into the original graph. To equally divide graph vertices into subsets, KDC adopts the KD-tree partitioning after the pivot mapping. In addition, two metric pruning rules and an optimized allocation strategy are presented to reduce communication and computation costs. In the query stage, based on the formed hybrid graph, we develop similarity search methods using random walk with restart (RWR) to measure node similarity. To boost efficiency, we derive tight bounds to rapidly shrink the search region. Extensive experiments with three real massive graphs are conducted to verify the effectiveness, efficiency, and scalability of our proposed techniques.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Zhang, Tianming","Gao, Yunjun","Zheng, Baihua","Chen, Lu","Wen, Shiting","Guo, Wei"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-056976"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, South"],"corresponding_author":["Gao, Yunjun"],"country":["China","Singapore"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Singapore Management University","Zhejiang University Ningbo Institute of Technology","Zhejiang University of Technology"],"keyword":["Algorithm","Distributed processing","Graph"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards distributed node similarity search on graphs","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/431339008/viewcontent.cgi.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported in part by the National Key R&D Program of China under Grant No. 2018YFB1004003, the NSFC under Grants No. 61972338 and 61802344, the NSFC-Zhejiang Joint Fund under Grant No. U1609217, and the ZJU-Hikvision Joint Project. Yunjun Gao is the corresponding author of the work."],"id":"S01-000.00-056976","identifier":[{"id":"85086665268","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-1795e471-a970-49ab-9105-7545a4e5a75c"],"keyword":["Algorithm","Distributed processing","Graph","Node similarity search"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-488574F02BD24B7A4D171B97D6538841"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/431339008/viewcontent.cgi.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"sg","key":"singapore management university","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"Singapore Management University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Daisy - Center for Data-intensive Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Database, Programming and Web Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang university ningbo institute of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang University Ningbo Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tianming","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Tianming","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yunjun","key":"gaopau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Yunjun","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Baihua","key":"zhengpau","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Baihua","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lu","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","locid":"0d18cc7c-dde6-4e46-afb8-378788d31500","name":"Chen, Lu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Shiting","key":"wenpau","last":"Wen","name":"Wen, Shiting","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Wei","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11280-020-00819-6","issn":["1386145X","15731413"],"issn_org":["1386145X"],"issue":"6","journal":"World Wide Web","pages":"3025-3053","publisher":"Springer Publishing Company","status":"p","title":"World Wide Web","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85086665268"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1795e471-a970-49ab-9105-7545a4e5a75c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Towards distributed node similarity search on graphs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-056976","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The Ca2+ -sensing protein calmodulin (CaM) inhibits cardiac ryanodine receptor (RyR2)-mediated Ca2+ release. CaM mutations associated with arrhythmias and sudden cardiac death have been shown to diminish CaM-dependent inhibition of RyR2, but the underlying mechanisms are not well understood. Nearly all arrhythmogenic CaM mutations identified are located in the C-domain of CaM and exert marked effects on Ca2+ binding to CaM and on the CaM C-domain interaction with the CaM-binding domain 2 (CaMBD2) in RyR2. Interestingly, the arrhythmogenic N-domain mutation CaM-N54I has little or no effect on Ca2+ binding to CaM or the CaM C-domain-RyR2 CaMBD2 interaction, unlike all CaM C-domain mutations. This suggests that CaM-N54I may diminish CaM-dependent RyR2 inhibition by affecting CaM N-domain interactions with RyR2 CaMBDs other than CaMBD2. To explore this possibility, we assessed the effects of deleting each of the four known CaMBDs in RyR2 (CaMBD1a, -1b, -2, or -3) on the CaM-dependent inhibition of RyR2-mediated Ca2+ release in HEK293 cells. We found that removing CaMBD1a, CaMBD1b, or CaMBD3 did not alter the effects of CaM-N54I or CaM-WT on RyR2 inhibition. On the other hand, deleting RyR2-CaMBD2 abolished the effects of both CaM-N54I and CaM-WT. Our results support that CaM-N54I causes aberrant RyR2 regulation via an uncharacterized CaMBD or less likely CaMBD2, and that RyR2 CaMBD2 is required for the actions of both N- and C-domain CaM mutations. Moreover, our results show that CaMBD1a is central to RyR2 regulation, but CaMBD1a, CaMBD1b, and CaMBD3 are not required for CaM-dependent inhibition of RyR2 in HEK293 cells.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Søndergaard, Mads Toft","Liu, Yingjie","Guo, Wenting","Wei, Jinhong","Wang, Ruiwu","Brohus, Malene","Overgaard, Michael Toft","Chen, S R Wayne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-077640"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Calgary"],"keyword":["Arrhythmia","Calmodulin","Ryanodine receptor"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"role of cardiac ryanodine receptor calmodulin binding domains in mediating the action of arrhythmogenic calmodulin n domain mutation n000000000054i","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/330404124/Role_of_cardiac_ryanodine_receptor_calmodulin_binding_domains_in_mediating_the_action_of_arrhythmogenic_calmodulin_N_domain_mutation_N54I.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-077640","identifier":[{"id":"31763755","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85076779991","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-5efd2a34-01f3-486e-9283-1a793d5460ee"],"keyword":["arrhythmia","calmodulin","intracellular Ca signalling","ion channel regulation","ryanodine receptor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F9355A901CD4A05F1D2A8A655120FE46"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/330404124/Role_of_cardiac_ryanodine_receptor_calmodulin_binding_domains_in_mediating_the_action_of_arrhythmogenic_calmodulin_N_domain_mutation_N54I.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Medical Biotechnology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"university of calgary","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Calgary","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads T","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"1febcb26-0ee5-44f3-a552-5ec579cc8727","name":"Søndergaard, Mads Toft","name_org":"Søndergaard, Mads T","orcid":"0000-0001-6779-5109","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yingjie","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Yingjie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenting","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Wenting","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jinhong","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Jinhong","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ruiwu","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Ruiwu","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Malene","key":"brohuspau","last":"Brohus","locid":"3a788ff7-9622-4191-8a4f-6616be19060d","name":"Brohus, Malene","orcid":"0000-0001-9247-8551","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael T","key":"overgaardpau","last":"Overgaard","locid":"8bd43772-17bb-45d3-9190-b230a7038933","name":"Overgaard, Michael Toft","name_org":"Overgaard, Michael T","orcid":"0000-0002-1423-2481","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"S R Wayne","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, S R Wayne","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31763755"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/febs.15147","issn":["14321033","1742464X"],"issn_org":["1742464X"],"issue":"11","journal":"FEBS Journal","pages":"2256-2280","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"FEBS Journal","title_org":"The FEBS Journal","volume":"287"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85076779991"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5efd2a34-01f3-486e-9283-1a793d5460ee"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Role of cardiac ryanodine receptor calmodulin-binding domains in mediating the action of arrhythmogenic calmodulin N-domain mutation N54I","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-077640","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In summary, moderate oil refining in Chinese industries has the potential to produce good-quality edible oils that better retain naturally occurring nutrients and minimize manufacturing hazards. Conventional lipid processing may well gradually be replaced by moderate refining in the near future. Major technical challenges in moderate refining are the variation of naturally occurring nutrients in different edible oils, and the regulation of processing or refining impacts on the nutrients accordingly. The equipment for moderate refining and the utilization of by-products are also the areas deserving special attention.","author_count":3,"contributors":["He, Dongping","Wei, Wei","Guo, Zheng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-260661"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Guo, Zheng"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Jiangnan University","Wuhan Polytechnic University"],"keyword":["Processing technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"moderate edible oil refining state of the art in china","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djc","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85088953479","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-260661","identifier":[{"id":"85088953479","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000555588200001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-e602e780-ce6e-4fd3-9c1b-eb1452ae982b"],"keyword":["edible oil industry","moderate oil refining","processing technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-83046B649C7B224730BE904FCC5AE69B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"wuhan polytechnic university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Wuhan Polytechnic University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"jiangnan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jiangnan University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Engineering, Department of Engineering - Agro-Biotechnology Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dongping","key":"hepau","last":"He","name":"He, Dongping","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Wei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Zheng","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","locid":"67372258-2bc9-4585-98c9-1b93c60d0ca9","name":"Guo, Zheng","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/aocs.12407","issn":["0003021X","15589331"],"issn_org":["0003021X"],"issue":"11","journal":"Journal of the American Oil Chemists' Society","pages":"1277-1279","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American Oil Chemists' Society","volume":"97"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088953479"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e602e780-ce6e-4fd3-9c1b-eb1452ae982b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Moderate Edible Oil Refining : State-of-the-Art in China","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-260661","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"We report two reversible pressure-induced isosymmetric phase transitions in α-Ag2S that are accompanied by two compressive anomalies at 7.5 and 16 GPa, respectively. The first transition arises from a sudden and drastic puckering of the wrinkled Ag-S layers, which leads to an anomalous structural softening at high pressure and gives rise to the ultrahigh compressive ductility in α-Ag2S. The second transition stems from a pressure-driven electronic state crossover from a conventional semiconductor to a topological metal. The band-crossing points near the Fermi energy form a nodal-line structure due to the preservation of the time-reversal and space-inversion symmetries under pressure. Our findings not only reveal the underlying mechanism responsible for the ultrahigh ductility in this class of inorganic semiconductors, but also provide a distinctive member to the growing family of topological metals and semimetals.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Liang, Yongcheng","Ahmad, Azkar Saeed","Zhao, Jianzhou","Song, Guozhu","Zhou, Xuefeng","Ji, Jialin","Zhang, Wei","Han, Zhilin","Liu, Jixuan","Ståhl, Kenny","Pakhomova, Anna","Glazyrin, Konstantin","Zhang, Guo Jun","Zhang, Wenqing","Zhao, Yusheng","Yu, Rui","Wang, Shanmin","Zhang, Peihong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-311327"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Liang, Yongcheng"],"country":["China","Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Donghua University","Fujian Normal University","German Electron Synchrotron","SUNY Buffalo","Southern University of Science and Technology","Southwest University of Science and Technology","Wuhan University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"isosymmetric phase transitions ultrahigh ductility and topological nodal lines in α a g000000000002 s","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.102.140101","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We acknowledge the financial support from the National Natural Science Foundation of China (Grants No. 52032001, No. 51671126, and No. 11674077) and the Fundamental Research Funds for the Central Universities (Grants No. 2232019A3-13 and No. 2232018D3-32). Work at Southern University of Science and Technology (SUSTech) was supported by the Shenzhen Peacock Plan (Grant No. KQTD2016053019134356), the Guangdong Innovative & Entrepreneurial Research Team Program (Grants No. 2016ZT06C279 and No. 2017ZT07C062), the Key Research Platforms and Projects of Universities in Guangdong Province (Grant No. 2018KZDXM062), the Shenzhen Pengcheng-Scholarship Program, the Shenzhen Development and Reform Commission Foundation for Shenzhen Engineering Research Center for Frontier Materials Synthesis at High Pressure, and the Research Platform for Crystal Growth & Thin-Film Preparation at SUSTech. Work at UB was supported by the US NSF (Grants No. DMR-1506669 and No. DMREF-1626967). We also acknowledge DESY (Hamburg, Germany), a member of the Helmholtz Association HGF, for performing synchrotron XRD experiments at the beamline P02.2 of PETRA III."],"id":"S01-000.00-311327","identifier":[{"id":"85094599362","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-166cc373-a061-4f31-a511-7c8b536e96e5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5FCCE14ED1B9642C15700BD31173450D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/223484404/PhysRevB.102.140101.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.102.140101","version":"Published Ver