{"abstract":"It remains elusive whether some of the associations identified in genome-wide association studies of prostate cancer (PrCa) may be due to regulatory effects of genetic variants on CpG sites, which may further influence expression of PrCa target genes. To search for CpG sites associated with PrCa risk, here we establish genetic models to predict methylation (N = 1,595) and conduct association analyses with PrCa risk (79,194 cases and 61,112 controls). We identify 759 CpG sites showing an association, including 15 located at novel loci. Among those 759 CpG sites, methylation of 42 is associated with expression of 28 adjacent genes. Among 22 genes, 18 show an association with PrCa risk. Overall, 25 CpG sites show consistent association directions for the methylation-gene expression-PrCa pathway. We identify DNA methylation biomarkers associated with PrCa, and our findings suggest that specific CpG sites may influence PrCa via regulating expression of candidate PrCa target genes.","author_count":46,"contributors":["Wu, Lang","Yang, Yaohua","Guo, Xingyi","Shu, Xiao Ou","Cai, Qiuyin","Shu, Xiang","Li, Bingshan","Tao, Ran","Wu, Chong","Nikas, Jason B.","Sun, Yanfa","Zhu, Jingjing","Roobol, Monique J.","Giles, Graham G.","Brenner, Hermann","John, Esther M.","Clements, Judith","Grindedal, Eli Marie","Park, Jong Y.","Stanford, Janet L.","Kote-Jarai, Zsofia","Haiman, Christopher A.","Eeles, Rosalind A.","Zheng, Wei","Long, Jirong","Eeles, Rosalind A.","Henderson, Brian E.","Haiman, Christopher A.","Kote-Jarai, Zsofia","Schumacher, Fredrick R.","Easton, Douglas","Benlloch, Sara","Olama, Ali Amin Al","Muir, Kenneth","Berndt, Sonja I.","Conti, David V.","Wiklund, Fredrik","Chanock, Stephen","Gapstur, Susan M.","Stevens, Victoria L.","Tangen, Catherine M.","Batra, Jyotsna","Clements, Judith","Gronberg, Henrik","Pashayan, Nora","Schleutker, Johanna","Albanes, Demetrius","Weinstein, Stephanie","Wolk, Alicja","Nordestgaard, Børge G"],"cuid":["S02-093.33-029492"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["BPC3 Consortium","CAPS Consortium","CRUK Consortium","PEGASUS Consortium","The PRACTICAL Consortium"],"corresponding_author":["Wu, Lang"],"country":["Australia","China","Finland","Germany","Netherlands","Norway","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","American Cancer Society","Cancer Council Victoria","Case Western Reserve University","Erasmus University Rotterdam","Florida State University","Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center","Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center","Genomix Inc.","German Cancer Research Center","German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ)","Karolinska Institutet","Longyan University","Melbourne School of Population and Global Health","National Institutes of Health","Queensland University of Technology","Royal Marsden Hospital London","Royal Marsden NHS Foundation Trust","Stanford University","Strangeways Research Laboratory","Translational Research Institute","University College London","University of Cambridge","University of Hawai'i at Mānoa","University of Hawaii at Manoa","University of Manchester","University of Melbourne","University of Oslo","University of South Florida","University of Southern California","University of Turku","University of Warwick","University of Washington","Uppsala University","Vanderbilt University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an integrative multi omics analysis to identify candidate dna methylation biomarkers related to prostate cancer risk","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all