{"abstract":"In this study, bufalin was glycosylated by an efficient chemo-enzymatic strategy. Firstly, 2-chloro-4-nitrophenyl-1-O-β-D-glucoside (sugar donors) was obtained by chemical synthesis. Then, the glycosylation of the bufalin was achieved with the synthesized sugar donor under the catalysis of two glycosyltransferases (Loki and ASP). Finally, two glycosides, i. e., bufalin-3-O-β-D-glucopyranoside and bufalin-3-O-[β-D-glucopyranosyl-(1→2)-β-D-glucopyranoside)], were obtained by preparative HPLC. Compared to our previously reported sole chemical (total yield 10 % in four steps) or enzymatic methods (30 %), our combined chemo-enzymatic strategy in this article greatly improves the yields of monoglycoside (68 %) and diglycoside (21 %) and decreased the experimental cost (90 %). Furthermore, we tested the water solubility of these glycosides and found that the water solubilities of the two glycosides were 13.1 and 53.7 times of bufalin, respectively. In addition, the inhibitory activity of these glycosides against Na+, K+-ATPase were evaluated. The mono-glycosylated compound showed more potent activity than bufalin, while the diglycosylated compound was less potent.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Liu, Yan","Xu, Wei","Huang, Zhao He","Guo, Jun","Fedosova, Natalya","Jiang, Ren Wang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-241727"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Fedosova, Natalya","Jiang, Ren Wang"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Jinan University"],"keyword":["Glycosylation","Na K ATPase","Water solubility"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an efficient strategy for the chemo enzymatic synthesis of bufalin glycosides with improved water solubility and inhibition against na sup sup k sup sup atpase","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85093525568","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-241727","identifier":[{"id":"32939944","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85093525568","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c4eee4d1-5c98-4225-880f-5d3e400192aa"],"keyword":["Bufalin","Na, K-ATPase","glycosylation","water solubility"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9280BCA386B2721DD1B0E0358925E223"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"jinan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jinan University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Vest"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yan","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Yan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Wei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhao He","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Zhao He","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jun","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Jun","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Natalya","key":"fedosovapau","last":"Fedosova","locid":"03b713c0-96d2-4c6b-ad02-3abf1c285e31","name":"Fedosova, Natalya","orcid":"0000-0002-1706-6108","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ren Wang","key":"jiangpau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Ren Wang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32939944"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/cbdv.202000529","issn":["16121872","16121880"],"issn_org":["16121872"],"issue":"11","journal":"Chemistry & Biodiversity","paperid":"e2000529","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Chemistry & Biodiversity","title_org":"Chemistry and Biodiversity","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c4eee4d1-5c98-4225-880f-5d3e400192aa"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"An Efficient Strategy for the Chemo-Enzymatic Synthesis of Bufalin Glycosides with Improved Water Solubility and Inhibition against Na<sup>+</sup>, K<sup>+</sup>-ATPase","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-241727","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In vivo chemical reactions activated by the tumor microenvironment (TME) are particularly promising for antitumor treatments. Herein, employing Cu2-xSe-Au Janus nanoparticles (NPs), photothermal conversion-coordinated Fenton-like and photocatalytic reactions are demonstrated in vitro/vivo. The amorphous form of Cu2-xSe and the catalytic effect of Au benefit the [rad]OH generation, and the photo-induced electron‒hole separation of the Janus NPs produces additional [rad]OH. The plasmonic electrons of Au facilitate the conversion from Cu2+ to Cu+. Both Cu2-xSe and Au contributes to the efficient photothermal conversion, further promoting the reactions. As a result, the H2O2 utilization rate is largely increased, and remarkable generation of reactive oxygen species is achieved by cell endogenous H2O2 in vitro/vivo. A competent tumor inhibition effect is afforded, with high-contrast multimodal imaging. This work opens up the route synergistically integrating photothermal therapy with chemodynamic therapy and photocatalytic therapy into tri-combination antitumor therapy, simply by heterojunction of semiconductor and noble metal.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Wang, Yuanlin","Li, Zhenglin","Hu, Ying","Liu, Jing","Guo, Mengyu","Wei, Hengxiang","Zheng, Shanliang","Jiang, Tingting","Sun, Xiang","Ma, Zhuo","Sun, Ye","Besenbacher, Flemming","Chen, Chunying","Yu, Miao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-260526"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Yu, Miao"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harbin Institute of Technology","National Center for Nanoscience and Technology"],"keyword":["Chemodynamic therapy","Multimodal Imaging","Photocatalytic therapy","Photothermal therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"photothermal conversion coordinated fenton like and photocatalytic reactions of cu sub 000000000002 x sub se au janus nanoparticles for tri combination antitumor therapy","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85086387883","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-260526","identifier":[{"id":"85086387883","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32540756","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-e5be3bfb-3e18-42e5-b74f-177344c05d91"],"keyword":["Chemodynamic therapy","In vivo chemical Reaction","Multimodal imaging","Photocatalytic therapy","Photothermal therapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6396423EEBDD85F798B375F4536BC632"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"harbin institute of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Harbin Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"national center for nanoscience and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"National Center for Nanoscience and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuanlin","key":"wangyuanlinpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Yuanlin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhenglin","key":"lizhenglinpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Zhenglin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ying","key":"huyingpau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Ying","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jing","key":"liujingpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Jing","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mengyu","key":"guomengyupau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Mengyu","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hengxiang","key":"weihengxiangpau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Hengxiang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shanliang","key":"zhengshanliangpau","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Shanliang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tingting","key":"jiangtingtingpau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Tingting","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiang","key":"sunxiangpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Xiang","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhuo","key":"mazhuopau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Zhuo","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ye","key":"sunyepau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Ye","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Flemming","key":"besenbacherflemmingpau","last":"Besenbacher","locid":"0aa89800-dd75-4f15-a575-c419dda7a69f","name":"Besenbacher, Flemming","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Chunying","key":"chenchunyingpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Chunying","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Miao","key":"yumiaopau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Miao","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32540756"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.biomaterials.2020.120167","issn":["01429612","18785905"],"issn_org":["01429612"],"journal":"Biomaterials","paperid":"120167","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Biomaterials","volume":"255"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85086387883"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e5be3bfb-3e18-42e5-b74f-177344c05d91"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Photothermal conversion-coordinated Fenton-like and photocatalytic reactions of Cu<sub>2-x</sub>Se-Au Janus nanoparticles for tri-combination antitumor therapy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-260526","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Panel-based targeted exome sequencing was applied to identify the pathogenic variants and genetic characteristics of retinitis pigmentosa (RP) in two Chinese families, and to gain a deeper understanding of the relationship between clinical manifestations and genotypes. Methods: A total of 17 subjects, comprising two probands (total patients: four subjects) and their family member, were recruited in this study. All subjects underwent comprehensive ophthalmic examinations and clinical evaluations, and the complete history and medical records were collected according to the standard procedures. All participants were screened using the multigene panel test (Target_Eye_792_V2 chip), and Sanger sequencing was used to confirm the candidate variants. Results: Among these two families, a total of three novel mutations in the EYS gene were identified in patients, including a homozygous frameshift mutation c.9252_9253insT detected in two patients in one family, and the compound heterozygous splicesite mutation c.5644+2T>C and frameshift mutation c.1920_1923delTGAG detected in two patients in the another family. All patients in both families had early onset of night blindness and poor visual acuity, and with typical posterior capsule opacification. The mutation co-segregated within all recruited individuals. In addition, one patient with compound heterozygous mutations was found to have typical blue-blindness symptoms and detected a previously reported disease-causing mutation c.235G>A in OPN1SW gene, which caused blue blindness manifestations and was first discovered in patient combined with RP causative genes. Conclusions: Panel-based targeted exome sequencing was used to identify three novel variants of RP causative gene, and we also detected a known pathogenic variants of blue-blindness causative genes in two patients. Our finding will provide a powerful basis for genetic counseling and enhance our current understanding of the genetics factors for RP families.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Sun, Yan","Li, Jian-kang","He, Wei","Wang, Zhuo-shi","Bai, Jin-yue","Xu, Ling","Xing, Bo","Zhang, Jian-guo","Wang, Lusheng","Li, Wei","Chen, Fang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-458188"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI"],"keyword":["Retinitis pigmentosa","mutation spectrum"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic and clinical analysis in chinese patients with retinitis pigmentosa caused by i eys i mutations","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/mgg3.1117","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-458188","identifier":[{"id":"85078033053","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7057104","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31944634","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-6c6b28ed-9c20-411c-8a95-a089e7746c68"],"keyword":["blue blindness","mutation spectrum","panel-based targeted exome sequencing","retinitis pigmentosa"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-80624ED1BBE6429B27549CD72D80F475"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/mgg3.1117","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/237323702/Genetic_and_clinical_analysis_in_Chinese_patients_with_retinitis_pigmentosa_caused_by_EYS_mutations.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"bgi","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Genome Research and Molecular Bio Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Yan","key":"sunyanpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Yan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jian-kang","key":"lijiankangpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Jian-kang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wei","key":"heweipau","last":"He","name":"He, Wei","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Zhuo-shi","key":"wangzhuoshipau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Zhuo-shi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jin-yue","key":"baijinyuepau","last":"Bai","name":"Bai, Jin-yue","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ling","key":"xulingpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Ling","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bo","key":"xingbopau","last":"Xing","name":"Xing, Bo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jian-guo","key":"zhangjianguopau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Jian-guo","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lusheng","key":"wanglushengpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Lusheng","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wei","key":"liweipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Wei","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Fang","key":"chenfangpau","last":"Chen","locid":"243a3415-b38a-4784-83a9-eab1a5ba3ffe","name":"Chen, Fang","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31944634"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/mgg3.1117","issn":["23249269"],"issue":"3","journal":"Molecular Genetics & Genomic Medicine","paperid":"e1117","status":"p","title":"Molecular Genetics & Genomic Medicine","title_org":"Molecular Genetics and Genomic Medicine","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85078033053"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6c6b28ed-9c20-411c-8a95-a089e7746c68"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Genetic and clinical analysis in Chinese patients with retinitis pigmentosa caused by <i>EYS</i> mutations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-458188","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Current management of patients with atrial fibrillation (AF) is limited by low detection of AF, non-adherence to guidelines, and lack of consideration of patients' preferences, thus highlighting the need for a more holistic and integrated approach to AF management. OBJECTIVE: The objective of this study was to determine whether a mobile health (mHealth) technology-supported AF integrated management strategy would reduce AF-related adverse events, compared with usual care. METHODS: This is a cluster randomized trial of patients with AF older than 18 years of age who were enrolled in 40 cities in China. Recruitment began on June 1, 2018 and follow-up ended on August 16, 2019. Patients with AF were randomized to receive usual care, or integrated care based on a mobile AF Application (mAFA) incorporating the ABC (Atrial Fibrillation Better Care) Pathway: A, Avoid stroke; B, Better symptom management; and C, Cardiovascular and other comorbidity risk reduction. The primary composite outcome was a composite of stroke/thromboembolism, all-cause death, and rehospitalization. Rehospitalization alone was a secondary outcome. Cardiovascular events were assessed using Cox proportional hazard modeling after adjusting for baseline risk. RESULTS: There were 1,646 patients allocated to mAFA intervention (mean age, 67.0 years; 38.0% female) with mean follow-up of 262 days, whereas 1,678 patients were allocated to usual care (mean age, 70.0 years; 38.0% female) with mean follow-up of 291 days. Rates of the composite outcome of 'ischemic stroke/systemic thromboembolism, death, and rehospitalization' were lower with the mAFA intervention compared with usual care (1.9% vs. 6.0%; hazard ratio [HR]: 0.39; 95% confidence interval [CI]: 0.22 to 0.67; p < 0.001). Rates of rehospitalization were lower with the mAFA intervention (1.2% vs. 4.5%; HR: 0.32; 95% CI: 0.17 to 0.60; p < 0.001). Subgroup analyses by sex, age, AF type, risk score, and comorbidities demonstrated consistently lower HRs for the composite outcome for patients receiving the mAFA intervention compared with usual care (all p < 0.05). CONCLUSIONS: An integrated care approach to holistic AF care, supported by mHealth technology, reduces the risks of rehospitalization and clinical adverse events. (Mobile Health [mHealth] technology integrating atrial fibrillation screening and ABC management approach trial; ChiCTR-OOC-17014138).","author_count":22,"contributors":["Guo, Yutao","Lane, Deirdre A.","Wang, Limin","Zhang, Hui","Wang, Hao","Zhang, Wei","Wen, Jing","Xing, Yunli","Wu, Fang","Xia, Yunlong","Liu, Tong","Wu, Fan","Liang, Zhaoguang","Liu, Fan","Zhao, Yujie","Li, Rong","Li, Xin","Zhang, Lili","Guo, Jun","Burnside, Girvan","Chen, Yundai","Lip, Gregory Y H"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-070805"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["mAF-App II Trial investigators"],"corresponding_author":["Lip, Gregory Y H"],"country":["China","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Capital Medical University","Chinese Center for Disease Control and Prevention","Dalian Medical University","First Affiliated Hospital of Guangzhou University of Chinese Medicine","First Affiliated Hospital of Haerbing Medical University","General Hospital of People's Liberation Army","Haidian Hospital","Hebei Medical University","Henan Cardiovascular Hospital Affiliated to Southern Medical University","Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","Longhua People's Hospital","Nanjing Medical University","PLA General Hospital","Shanghai Jiao Tong University","Tianjin Medical University","University of Liverpool"],"keyword":["Adverse events","Atrial fibrillation","Integrated care","Mobile health"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Liverpool Centre for Cardiovascular Sciences, University of Liverpool and Liverpool Heart & Chest Hospital, United Kingdom"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mobile health technology to improve care for patients with atrial fibrillation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85082052574&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors thank the Huawei Heart Health Research Team for the photoplethysmography-based pulse rhythm monitoring for Better symptom management with patient-centered, symptom-directed decisions on rate or rhythm control, headed by Mr. Xiaoxiang He. Team members include Jiabing Yan, Wenjuan Chen, Qin Chen, Jie Zhang, Xi Huang, and Hongbao Li. We are grateful to Tong Xinyuan, from the Statistics Teaching and Research Office, Medical School of Chinese People's Liberation Army, Beijing, China, to Liu Miao, from the Centre for Epidemiology and Biostatistics, National Center for Geriatrics Clinical Research Center, Beijing, China, for statistical analysis, and for Luo Yanxia for her contribution to frailty Cox model analysis, who works for Capital Medical University, China."],"id":"S01-000.00-070805","identifier":[{"id":"32241367","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85082052574","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-4799f6de-63ed-405e-a99b-7b98611acc67"],"keyword":["adverse events","atrial fibrillation","integrated care","mobile health"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-31568DB81D4C3B6C03ABBA5795A58E19"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"general hospital of people s liberation army","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"General Hospital of People's Liberation Army","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Aalborg Thrombosis Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Liverpool Centre for Cardiovascular Sciences, University of Liverpool and Liverpool Heart & Chest Hospital, United Kingdom"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"chinese center for disease control and prevention","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Center for Disease Control and Prevention","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"haidian hospital","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Haidian Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"cn","key":"capital medical university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Capital Medical University","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"cn","key":"shanghai jiao tong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai Jiao Tong University","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"cn","key":"dalian medical university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Dalian Medical University","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"cn","key":"tianjin medical university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tianjin Medical University","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"cn","key":"first affiliated hospital of haerbing medical university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"First Affiliated Hospital of Haerbing Medical University","used":1},{"affno":"11","country":"cn","key":"hebei medical university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hebei Medical University