{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: Genome-wide association studies (GWAS) represent a powerful approach to detecting candidate genes for economically important traits in livestock. Our aim was to identify promising candidate muscle development genes that affect net meat weight (NMW) and validate these candidate genes in cattle. MATERIALS AND METHODS: Using a next-generation sequencing (NGS) dataset, we applied ~ 12 million imputed single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) from 1,252 Simmental cattle to detect genes influencing net meat yield by way of a linear mixed model method. Haplotype and linkage disequilibrium (LD) blocks were employed to augment support for identified genes. To investigate the role of MTPN in bovine muscle development, we isolated myoblasts from the longissimus dorsi of a bovine foetus and treated the cells during proliferation, differentiation and hypertrophy. RESULTS: We identified one SNP (rs100670823) that exceeded our stringent significance threshold (P = 8.58 × 10-8 ) for a putative NMW-related quantitative trait locus (QTL). We identified a promising candidate gene, myotrophin (MTPN), in the region around this SNP Myotrophin had a stimulatory effect on six muscle-related markers that regulate differentiation and myoblast fusion. During hypertrophy, myotrophin promoted myotube hypertrophy and increased myotube diameters. Cell viability assay and flow cytometry showed that myotrophin inhibited myoblast proliferation. CONCLUSIONS: The present experiments showed that myotrophin increases differentiation and hypertrophy of skeletal muscle cells, while inhibiting their proliferation. Our examination of GWAS results with in vitro biological studies provides new information regarding the potential application of myotrophin to increase meat yields in cattle and helpful information for further studies.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Bordbar, Farhad","Jensen, Just","Du, Min","Abied, Adam","Guo, Wei","Xu, Lingyang","Gao, Huijiang","Zhang, Lupei","Li, Junya"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-133468"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Junya","Zhang, Lupei"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Agricultural Sciences","University of Wisconsin-Madison","Washington State University Pullman"],"keyword":["Differentiation","GWAS","NGS","Proliferation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identification and validation of a novel candidate gene regulating net meat weight in simmental beef cattle based on imputed next generation sequencing","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/cpr.12870","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-133468","identifier":[{"id":"85088595859","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000552876500001","type":"wos"},{"id":"32722873","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-073f36ae-8fc6-45b1-8bcf-c6a362c0a68e"],"keyword":["Differentiation","GWAS","NGS","NMW","Proliferation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C68A25AEF1F86DE3A8D5586F9404EAE9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/cpr.12870","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of agricultural sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Agricultural Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Center for Quantitative Genetics and Genomics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"washington state university pullman","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Washington State University Pullman","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of wisconsin madison","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Wisconsin-Madison","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Farhad","key":"bordbarpau","last":"Bordbar","name":"Bordbar, Farhad","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Just","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"fd33639a-638e-4eca-b152-71c93ab91293","name":"Jensen, Just","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Min","key":"dupau","last":"Du","name":"Du, Min","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Adam","key":"abiedpau","last":"Abied","name":"Abied, Adam","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Wei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lingyang","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Lingyang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Huijiang","key":"gaopau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Huijiang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lupei","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Lupei","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Junya","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Junya","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32722873"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/cpr.12870","issn":["09607722","13652184"],"issn_org":["09607722"],"issue":"9","journal":"Cell Proliferation","paperid":"e12870","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"Cell Proliferation","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088595859"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-073f36ae-8fc6-45b1-8bcf-c6a362c0a68e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Identification and validation of a novel candidate gene regulating net meat weight in Simmental beef cattle based on imputed next-generation sequencing","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-133468","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"A fault diagnosis method for power electronics converters based on deep feedforward network and wavelet compression is proposed in this paper. The transient historical data after wavelet compression are used to realize the training of fault diagnosis classifier. Firstly, the correlation analysis of the voltage or current data running in various fault states is performed to remove the redundant features and the sampling point. Secondly, the wavelet transform is used to remove the redundant data of the features, and then the training sample data is greatly compressed. The deep feedforward network is trained by the low frequency component of the features, while the training speed is greatly accelerated. The average accuracy of fault diagnosis classifier can reach over 97%. Finally, the fault diagnosis classifier is tested, and final diagnosis result is determined by multiple-groups transient data, by which the reliability of diagnosis results is improved. The experimental result proves that the classifier has strong generalization ability and can accurately locate the open-circuit faults in IGBTs.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kou, Lei","Liu, Chuang","Cai, Guo wei","Zhang, Zhe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-317843"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Liu, Chuang"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Northeast Electric Power University"],"keyword":["Deep Feedforward Network","Fault diagnosis","Power electronics converters"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fault diagnosis for power electronics converters based on deep feedforward network and wavelet compression","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/222640419/Fault_Diagnosis_for_Power_Electronics_Converters_based_on_Deep_Feedforward_Network_and_Wavelet_Compression_post_print.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This research is funded by National Key R&D Program of China under grant number 2017YFB0903300."],"id":"S01-000.00-317843","identifier":[{"id":"85084730921","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-2c8f7154-a331-4e5a-8b8e-c03ffa1b583e"],"keyword":["Deep Feedforward Network","Fault Diagnosis","Haar Transform","Power Electronics Converters","Transient Features","Wavelet Compression"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5B54F07E9C7E7E1E3F403FC5996B7083"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/222640419/Fault_Diagnosis_for_Power_Electronics_Converters_based_on_Deep_Feedforward_Network_and_Wavelet_Compression_post_print.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"northeast electric power university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northeast Electric Power University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering, Electronics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lei","key":"koupau","last":"Kou","name":"Kou, Lei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chuang","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Chuang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guo wei","key":"caipau","last":"Cai","name":"Cai, Guo wei","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zhe","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"eebd7cda-144d-4f72-a6a7-2e8339aec75e","name":"Zhang, Zhe","orcid":"0000-0001-8407-3167","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.epsr.2020.106370","issn":["03787796","18732046"],"issn_org":["03787796"],"journal":"Electric Power Systems Research","paperid":"106370","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Electric Power Systems Research","volume":"185"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084730921"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-2c8f7154-a331-4e5a-8b8e-c03ffa1b583e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Fault Diagnosis for Power Electronics Converters based on Deep Feedforward Network and Wavelet Compression","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-317843","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The Global Burden of Diseases, Injuries, and Risk Factors Study (GBD) 2019 provides a rules-based synthesis of the available evidence on levels and trends in health outcomes, a diverse set of risk factors, and health system responses. GBD 2019 covered 204 countries and territories, as well as first administrative level disaggregations for 22 countries, from 1990 to 2019. Because GBD is highly standardised and comprehensive, spanning both fatal and non-fatal outcomes, and uses a mutually exclusive and collectively exhaustive list of hierarchical disease and injury causes, the study provides a powerful basis for detailed and broad insights on global health trends and emerging challenges. GBD 2019 incorporates data from 281 586 sources and provides more than 3.5 billion estimates of health outcome and health system measures of interest for global, national, and subnational policy dialogue. All GBD estimates are publicly available and adhere to the Guidelines on Accurate and Transparent Health Estimate Reporting. From this vast amount of information, five key insights that are important for health, social, and economic development strategies have been distilled. These insights are subject to the many limitations outlined in each of the component GBD capstone papers.","author_count":1599,"contributors":["Abbafati, Cristiana","Abbas, Kaja M.","Abbasi, Mohammad","Abbasifard, Mitra","Abbasi-Kangevari, Mohsen","Abbastabar, Hedayat","Abd-Allah, Foad","Abdelalim, Ahmed","Abdollahi, Mohammad","Abdollahpour, Ibrahim","Abedi, Aidin","Abedi, Parisa","Abegaz, Kedir Hussein","Abolhassani, Hassan","Abosetugn, Akine Eshete","Aboyans, Victor","Abrams, Elissa M.","Abreu, Lucas Guimaraes","Abrigo, Michael R. M.","Abu Haimed, Abdulaziz Khalid","Abualhasan, Ahmed","Abu-Gharbieh, Eman","Abu-Raddad, Laith Jamal","Abushouk, Abdelrahman I.","Acebedo, Alyssa","Ackerman, Ilana N.","Adabi, Maryam","Adair, Tim","Adamu, Abdu A.","Adebayo, Oladimeji M.","Adedeji, Isaac Akinkunmi","Adeka