["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Current Options and Recommendations for the Treatment of Thoracic Aortic Pathologies Involving the Aortic Arch : An Expert Consensus Document of the European Association for Cardio-Thoracic Surgery (EACTS) &amp; the European Society for Vascular Surgery (ESVS)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-599461","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: Female sex has been linked with worse prognosis in patients with atrial fibrillation (AF). Clinical risk stratification of women with AF may help decision-making before catheter ablation (CA). Aim: To evaluate arrhythmia outcomes and the predictive value of clinical scores for arrhythmia recurrence in a large cohort of Chinese patients with AF undergoing CA. Methods: A total 1410 of patients (68.1% men) who underwent AF ablation with scheduled follow-up were analysed retrospectively. Baseline characteristics and ablation outcome were compared between men and women. The predictive values of risk scoring systems for AF recurrence were assessed in women. Results: Recurrence, early recurrence and complications after CA were similar in women and men over similar follow-up periods (20.7 ± 8.0 vs 20.7 ± 9.1 months; P > 0.05). Compared with men, women with AF recurrence were older and had a larger left atrial diameter (LAD), less paroxysmal AF, lower left ventricular ejection fraction, lower estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) and higher serum concentrations of B-type natriuretic peptide (BNP) and C-reactive protein (CRP) (all P < 0.01). Multivariable analysis showed that age, non-paroxysmal AF, body mass index, coronary artery disease, LAD, early recurrence, eGFR, BNP and CRP were independent risk factors with sex differences (all P < 0.05) in the whole cohort. In women, only non-paroxysmal AF, early recurrence, BNP, CRP (all P < 0.01) and history of stroke/transient ischaemic attack (P = 0.016) were independent risk factors. Of the clinical scoring systems tested, MB-LATER, APPLE, CAAP-AF and BASE-AF2 scores (C-indexes 0.73, 0.72, 0.68 and 0.72, respectively; all P < 0.01) had a modest predictive value for AF recurrence after CA in women. Conclusions: CA for AF has similar recurrence risks in women and men, but there are sex differences in the clinical characteristics and risk factors associated with AF recurrence.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Deng, Hai","Shantsila, Alena","Guo, Pi","Potpara, Tatjana S.","Zhan, Xianzhang","Fang, Xianhong","Liao, Hongtao","Liu, Yang","Wei, Wei","Fu, Lu","Xue, Yumei","Wu, Shulin","Lip, Gregory Y H"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-065399"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Lip, Gregory Y H"],"country":["China","Serbia","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Clinical Center of Serbia","Guangdong Provincial People's Hospital","Shantou University","University of Belgrade","University of Birmingham","University of Liverpool"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sex related risks of recurrence of atrial fibrillation after ablation insights from the guangzhou atrial fibrillation ablation registry","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85060347191&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was conducted with support from the Guangzhou Science and Technology Project (Grant No. 201508020261 and No. 2014Y200196) and the Natural Science Funds of Guangdong Province (Grant No. 2016A030313795)."],"id":"S01-000.00-065399","identifier":[{"id":"85060347191","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-34e90818-a4c4-42ec-a857-b75e1905188d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0965D57A781FF6D286B9E5BDC1452968"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of birmingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Birmingham","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"guangdong provincial people s hospital","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Guangdong Provincial People's Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"shantou university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shantou University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"rs","key":"clinical center of serbia","loc":["Serbia","Europe, Non-EU"],"name":"Clinical Center of Serbia","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"rs","key":"university of belgrade","loc":["Serbia","Europe, Non-EU"],"name":"University of Belgrade","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Aalborg Thrombosis Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"gb","key":"university of liverpool","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Liverpool","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hai","key":"dengpau","last":"Deng","name":"Deng, Hai","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alena","key":"shantsilapau","last":"Shantsila","name":"Shantsila, Alena","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Pi","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Pi","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Tatjana S.","key":"potparapau","last":"Potpara","name":"Potpara, Tatjana S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xianzhang","key":"zhanpau","last":"Zhan","name":"Zhan, Xianzhang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xianhong","key":"fangpau","last":"Fang","name":"Fang, Xianhong","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hongtao","key":"liaopau","last":"Liao","name":"Liao, Hongtao","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yang","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Yang","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Wei","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lu","key":"fupau","last":"Fu","name":"Fu, Lu","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yumei","key":"xuepau","last":"Xue","name":"Xue, Yumei","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Shulin","key":"wupau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Shulin","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5 6 7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregory Y.H.","key":"lippau","last":"Lip","locid":"8fa30e84-7381-41b4-8037-afc032238a3d","name":"Lip, Gregory Y H","name_org":"Lip, Gregory Y.H.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.acvd.2018.10.006","issn":["18752128","18752136"],"issn_org":["18752136"],"issue":"3","journal":"Archives of Cardiovascular Diseases","pages":"171-179","publisher":"Elsevier Masson s.r.l.","status":"p","title":"Archives of Cardiovascular Diseases","volume":"112"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85060347191"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-34e90818-a4c4-42ec-a857-b75e1905188d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Sex-related risks of recurrence of atrial fibrillation after ablation : Insights from the Guangzhou Atrial Fibrillation Ablation Registry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-065399","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Anaerobic ammonium oxidation coupled to iron reduction (Feammox) is a recently discovered pathway contributing to nitrogen loss in various ecosystems such as paddy soils and sediments. However, little is known about the microbes driving Feammox in an agricultural ecosystem. Here, we demonstrated the occurrence of Feammox in paddy soils of Southern China using a 15 N isotopic tracing technique, and examined the microbial communities associated with Feammox using RNA based stable isotope probing (RNA-SIP) combined with Illumina sequencing. Feammox was detected in all collected soils with direct N 2 production as the dominant Feammox pathway. It was estimated that approximately 6.91% of the applied nitrogen fertilizers were lost through Feammox in the paddy soils. RNA-SIP results showed that the composition of enriched active microbial communities were dependent on soil properties, especially the soil pH and grain size. Geobacter were enriched in most soils across various properties. The abundance of enriched GOUTA19 were significantly higher in soils with low pH than those in soils with medium pH and high pH, and the relative abundance of active Nitrososphaeraceae and Pseudomonas only increased in soils with medium and high pH during 4-day of incubation. These results suggested Feammox is a ubiquitous and important process for N loss. Geobacter, GOUTA19, Nitrososphaeraceae and Pseudomonas were active during the incubation that favored Feammox and the growth of Feammox microbes, suggesting these microbes were potentially associated with Feammox in natural agricultural soils.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Li, Hu","Su, Jian Qiang","Yang, Xiao Ru","Zhou, Guo Wei","Lassen, Simon Bo","Zhu, Yong Guan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-414961"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences","State Key Laboratory of Environmental Chemistry and Ecotoxicology, Research Center for Eco-Environmental Sciences, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rna stable isotope probing of potential feammox population in paddy soil","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85065090038&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-414961","identifier":[{"id":"30978017","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85065090038","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-24135ee0-18dc-480d-a801-a1e41d8b342d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4761A7BCEF926D849FED29F7FA2583F3"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"state key laboratory of environmental chemistry and ecotoxicology research center for eco environmental sciences chinese academy of sciences beijing","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"State Key Laboratory of Environmental Chemistry and Ecotoxicology, Research Center for Eco-Environmental Sciences, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Microbial Ecology and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Hu","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Hu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jian Qiang","key":"supau","last":"Su","name":"Su, Jian Qiang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiao Ru","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Xiao Ru","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Guo Wei","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Guo Wei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Simon Bo","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"7550f1f0-7813-4a66-8524-1287b55f402a","name":"Lassen, Simon Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-9781-1939","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Yong Guan","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Yong Guan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30978017"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.est.8b05016","issn":["0013936X","15205851"],"issn_org":["0013936X"],"issue":"9","journal":"Environmental Science & Technology","pages":"4841-4849","status":"p","title":"Environmental Science & Technology","title_org":"Environmental Science and Technology","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85065090038"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-24135ee0-18dc-480d-a801-a1e41d8b342d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"RNA Stable Isotope Probing of Potential Feammox Population in Paddy Soil","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-414961","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Diets of soil-feeding earthworms contain abundant nitrate and iron(III) oxides, which are potential electron acceptors for mineralization of organic compounds. The earthworm gut provides an ideal habitat for ingested iron(III)-reducing microorganisms. However, little is known about iron(III) reduction and its interaction with other processes in the guts of earthworms. Here, we determined the dynamics of iron(III) and revealed its interaction with the turnover of organic acids and nitrate in the gut of the earthworm Pheretima guillelmi. Samples from gut contents combined with anoxic incubation were used for chemical analysis and 16S rRNA based Illumina sequencing. Chemical analysis showed that higher ratios of iron(II)/iron(III), nitrite/nitrate, and more abundant organic acids were contained in the in vivo gut of the earthworm P. guillelmi than those in the in situ soil. A higher rate of iron(III) reduction was detected in treatments of microcosmic incubation with gut contents (IG gut) than that with soil (IG soil), and nitrate reduction occurred earlier than iron(III) reduction in both treatments. Potential iron(III) reducers were dominated by fermentative genera Clostridium, Bacillus, and Desulfotomaculum in the treatment of IG gut, while they were dominated by dissimilatory iron(III)-reducing genera Geobacter in the treatment of IG soil. The iron(III)-reducing microbial community shared several genera with denitrifers in the treatment of IG gut, revealing a close link between iron(III) reduction and denitrification in the gut of earthworms. Collectively, our findings demonstrated that iron(III) reduction occurred along the gut and provided novel insights into the great contribution of earthworm gut microbiota on Fe and the associated C and N cycling in soil environments.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Zhou, Guo Wei","Yang, Xiao Ru","Sun, An Qi","Li, Hu","Lassen, Simon Bo","Zheng, Bang Xiao","Zhu, Yong Guan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-434473"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["China","Finland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Huaqiao University","State Key Laboratory of Environmental Chemistry and Ecotoxicology, Research Center for Eco-Environmental Sciences, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing","University of Helsinki"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mobile incubator for iron iii reduction in the gut of the soil feeding earthworm i pheretima guillelmi i and interaction with denitrification","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85064106817&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-434473","identifier":[{"id":"30882209","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85064106817","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-44b39f75-dec3-4640-8dec-2b52b024b664"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-544D9A3358C8671A29AC3EF7162FD028"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"state key laboratory of environmental chemistry and ecotoxicology research center for eco environmental sciences chinese academy of sciences beijing","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"State Key Laboratory of Environmental Chemistry and Ecotoxicology, Research Center for Eco-Environmental Sciences, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"huaqiao university","lo