{"abstract":"Impedance-source inverters using coupled inductors have been investigated as alternatives for providing high step-up voltages. However, leakage inductances of the coupled inductors have commonly led to lower overall effectiveness, in addition to generating high dc-link voltage spikes. The latter raises voltage stresses of switches, which in turn, may reduce the power levels of the inverters. A high step-up Y-source inverter has therefore been proposed in this paper to provide a high boost with a smooth dc-link voltage ensured by proper recycling of the leakage energy. These features have been verified by comparing simulation and experimental results of an existing Y-source and the proposed inverters. Factors compared are their respective boost ratios, voltage stresses, current stresses, and dc-link voltage spikes.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Liu, Hongpeng","Zhou, Zichao","Liu, Kuan","Loh, Poh Chiang","Wang, Wei","Xu, Dian Guo","Blaabjerg, Frede"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-053249"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China","Hong Kong"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese University of Hong Kong","Harbin Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Impedance source inverter","Y source inverters YSI","voltage spikes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high step up y source inverter with reduced dc link voltage spikes","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/306356049/High_Step_Up_Y_Source_Inverter_with_Reduced_DC_Link_Voltage_Spikes.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-053249","identifier":[{"id":"85052670912","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-0b0aad00-46ad-4f77-82bd-cba03fff8c2c"],"keyword":[", leakage and coupled inductances","Impedance-source inverter","Y-source inverters (YSI)","voltage spikes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1D39F16F617576BB095EAA98A68BAD82"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/306356049/High_Step_Up_Y_Source_Inverter_with_Reduced_DC_Link_Voltage_Spikes.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"harbin institute of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Harbin Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"hk","key":"chinese university of hong kong","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese University of Hong Kong","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hongpeng","key":"liuhongpengpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Hongpeng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zichao","key":"zhouzichaopau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Zichao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kuan","key":"liukuanpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Kuan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Poh Chiang","key":"lohpohchiangpau","last":"Loh","name":"Loh, Poh Chiang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"wangweipau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Wei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dian Guo","key":"xudianguopau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Dian Guo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frede","key":"blaabjergfredepau","last":"Blaabjerg","locid":"22b09e36-1f7b-4d33-90bf-918730e1d09a","name":"Blaabjerg, Frede","orcid":"0000-0001-8311-7412","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tpel.2018.2866635","issn":["08858993","19410107"],"issn_org":["08858993"],"issue":"6","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Power Electronics","pages":"5487-5499","paperid":"8444091","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Power Electronics","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85052670912"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0b0aad00-46ad-4f77-82bd-cba03fff8c2c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"High Step-Up Y-Source Inverter with Reduced DC-Link Voltage Spikes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-053249","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Reachability computation is a fundamental graph functionality with a wide range of applications. In spite of this, little work has as yet been done on efficient reachability queries over temporal graphs, which are used extensively to model time-varying networks, such as communication networks, social networks, and transportation schedule networks. Moreover, we are faced with increasingly large real-world temporal networks that may be distributed across multiple data centers. This state of affairs motivates the paper’s study of efficient reachability queries on distributed temporal graphs. We propose an efficient index, called Temporal Vertex Labeling (TVL), which is a labeling scheme for distributed temporal graphs. We also present algorithms that exploit TVL to achieve efficient support for distributed reachability querying over temporal graphs in Pregel-like systems. The algorithms exploit several optimizations that hinge upon non-trivial lemmas. Extensive experiments using massive real and synthetic temporal graphs are conducted to provide detailed insight into the efficiency and scalability of the proposed methods, covering both index construction and query processing. Compared with the state-of-the-art methods, the TVL based query algorithms are capable of up to an order of magnitude speedup with lower index construction overhead.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Zhang, Tianming","Gao, Yunjun","Chen, Lu","Guo, Wei","Pu, Shiliang","Zheng, Baihua","Jensen, Christian S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-059968"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, South"],"country":["China","Singapore"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Singapore Management University","Zhejiang University"],"keyword":["Algorithm","Distributed processing","Graph","Query processing","Reachability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"efficient distributed reachability querying of massive temporal graphs","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/391444990/Green_Open_Access_Manuscript_4_end.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-059968","identifier":[{"id":"85074091447","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-221d6fa6-7c5f-4576-8394-2344dc8df7ab"],"keyword":["Algorithm","Distributed processing","Graph","Query processing","Reachability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-583F9FE5AE7486502AACC23F408D773F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/391444990/Green_Open_Access_Manuscript_4_end.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Database, Programming and Web Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"sg","key":"singapore management university","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"Singapore Management University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tianming","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Tianming","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yunjun","key":"gaopau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Yunjun","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lu","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","locid":"0d18cc7c-dde6-4e46-afb8-378788d31500","name":"Chen, Lu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Wei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shiliang","key":"pupau","last":"Pu","name":"Pu, Shiliang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Baihua","key":"zhengpau","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Baihua","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian S.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"56b675d6-bbf5-4dec-a799-50327f3fc66a","name":"Jensen, Christian S.","orcid":"0000-0002-9697-7670","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00778-019-00572-x","issn":["0949877X","10668888"],"issn_org":["10668888"],"issue":"6","journal":"VLDB Journal","pages":"871-896","publisher":"Springer Publishing Company","status":"p","title":"VLDB Journal","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85074091447"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-221d6fa6-7c5f-4576-8394-2344dc8df7ab"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Efficient distributed reachability querying of massive temporal graphs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-059968","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The active damping method based on proportional voltage feedforward is usually used to solve the inherent resonance and low-order harmonics of LCL filter. However, in the case of low short-circuit capacity and high impedance of weak grid, the grid impedance has a great influence on the control performance, especially for high-frequency inverters based on SiC MOSFET. In order to improve the stability of the inverter, this paper proposes a robust composite control method, which combines grid-connected current feedback active damping, full voltage feedforward and improved current controller. This method can not only adapt to the wide range of changes in grid impedance, but also suppress background harmonics. The simulation and experimental results verify the effectiveness of the proposed method.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Liu, Guihua","Guo, Lei","Wang, Wei","Blaabjerg, Frede"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-076706"],"event":{"end":"2019-05-30","place":"Busan, kr","start":"2019-05-27","title":"2019 10th International Conference on Power Electronics and ECCE Asia (ICPE 2019 - ECCE Asia)","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harbin Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Robust control","Voltage feedforward","Weak grid"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a robust composite control method for lcl grid connected inverter based on sic mosfets under weak grid","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/8796906","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-076706","identifier":[{"id":"85071640052","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-5bc6926d-405a-479c-a99d-c3b3aa97653a"],"keyword":["High-frequency inverter","Robust control","Voltage feedforward","Weak grid"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F855712BB3287A7D4E884BE0CE569B45"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"harbin institute of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Harbin Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guihua","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Guihua","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lei","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Lei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Wei","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frede","key":"blaabjergpau","last":"Blaabjerg","locid":"22b09e36-1f7b-4d33-90bf-918730e1d09a","name":"Blaabjerg, Frede","orcid":"0000-0001-8311-7412","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788957083130"],"isbn":["9781728116129"],"issn":["21506078"],"pages":"2840-2845","place":"Korea","publisher":"IEEE Press","series":"International Conference on Power Electronics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2019 10th International Conference on Power Electronics and ECCE Asia (ICPE 2019 - ECCE Asia)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85071640052"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5bc6926d-405a-479c-a99d-c3b3aa97653a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A Robust Composite Control Method for LCL Grid-connected Inverter Based on SiC MOSFETs under Weak Grid","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-076706","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Genome-wide association study-identified prostate cancer risk variants explain only a relatively small fraction of its familial relative risk, and the genes responsible for many of these identified associations remain unknown. To discover novel prostate cancer genetic loci and possible causal genes at previously identified risk loci, we performed a transcriptome- wide association study in 79,194 cases and 61,112 controls of European ancestry. Using data from the Genotype-Tissue Expression Project, we established genetic models to predict gene expression across the transcriptome for both prostate models and cross-tissue models and evaluated model performance using two independent datasets. We identified significant associations for 137 genes at P < 2.61 × 10 -6, a Bonferroni-corrected threshold, including nine genes that remained significant at P < 2.61 × 10 -6 after adjusting for all known prostate cancer risk variants in nearby regions. Of the 128 remaining associated genes, 94 have not yet been reported as potential target genes at known loci. We silenced 14 genes and many showed a consistent effect on viability and colony-forming efficiency in three cell lines. Our study provides substantial new information to advance our understanding of prostate cancer genetics and biology.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Wu, Lang","Wang, Jifeng","Cai, Qiuyin","Cavazos, Taylor B","Emami, Nima C","Long, Jirong","Shu, Xiao-Ou","Lu, Yingchang","Guo, Xingyi","Bauer, Joshua A","Pasaniuc, Bogdan","Penney, Kathryn L","Freedman, Matthew L","Kote-Jarai, Zsofia","Witte, John S","Haiman, Christopher A","Eeles, Rosalind A","Zheng, Wei"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-188959"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["PRACTICAL, CRUK, BPC3, CAPS, PEGASUS Consortia"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard University","Institute of Cancer Research","University of California at Los Angeles","University of California at San Francisco","University of Hawaii at Manoa","University of Southern California","Vanderbilt University"],"keyword":["Biomarkers Tumor genetics","Case Control Studies","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Genome Wide Association Study","Humans","Male","Polymorphism Single Nucleotide","Prostatic Neoplasms genetics","Quantitative Trait Loci","Risk","Transcriptome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identification of novel susceptibility loci and genes for prostate cancer risk a transcriptome wide association study in over 000000000140 000000000000 european descendants","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6606384/pdf/nihms-1529542.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-188959","identifier":[{"id":"85068861305","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31101764","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6606384","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-6860e8e5-dd9a-4ca7-9e9c-7a1127ca7765"],"keyword":["Biomarkers, Tumor/genetics","Case-Control Studies","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Genome-Wide Association Study","Humans","Male","Polymorphism, Single Nucleotide","Prostatic Neoplasms/genetics","Quantitative Trait Loci","Risk","Transcriptome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B32D7B7F481FFDA15BA2DBA1A269CDCE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6606384/pdf/nihms-1529542.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key"