rst":"Xiaoting","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiaoting","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Wei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ji","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","locid":"05f23b9e-16c0-478d-840b-18a8d914c393","name":"Chen, Ji","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.7515/jee181002","journal":"Journal of Environment Earth","pages":"16-27","status":"p","title":"Journal of Environment Earth","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b0b98a56-a7ca-4f12-9b0d-9e553b0f7a36"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A review of the influence factors of plant phenology under different climate types (In Chinese with English Abstract)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-230159","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"A greenhouse experiment was conducted in which two leguminous species commonly used in the Yellow River Delta for vegetation restoration, Robinia pseudoacacia and Amorpha fruticosa, were subjected to five salt treatments: 0, 50, 100, 150, and 200 mmol L-1. We aimed to determine which of the two species would be better suited for growth in a saline environment, and whether the acclimation capacity to salinity resulted from an inherently higher phenotypic plasticity. The results showed that salinity affected most growth and biomass parameters but had no effects on most leaf traits and physiological parameters of the two species. Height, relative growth rate of crown area, root biomass, and leaf mass ratio of R. pseudoacacia were reduced by higher salinity, while A. fruticosa was not affected. Chlorophyll a-to-chlorophyll b ratio and total antioxidative capacity of A. fruticosa increased with higher salinity, whereas those of R. pseudoacacia remained unchanged. Root mass ratio and vitamin C concentration of both species were not affected by salinity, whereas vitamin C concentration of A. fruticosa was higher than that of R. pseudoacacia. The root-to-shoot ratio of A. fruticosa was higher than that of R. pseudoacacia in most salt treatments. Of all leaf traits, only leaf area differed between treatments. R. pseudoacacia generally exhibited a greater plasticity than A. fruticosa in response to salinity, but A. fruticosa was more resistant to the higher salinities than R. pseudoacacia, and was thus a better candidate for vegetation restoration in saline areas.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Guo, Xiao","Ren, Xiao-Huang","Eller, Franziska","Li, Ming-Yan","Wang, Ren-Qing","Du, Ning","Guo, Wei-Hua"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-242507"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Guo, Wei-Hua"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Qingdao Agricultural University","Shandong University"],"keyword":["Biochemical","Chlorophyll fluorescence","Climate change","GROWTH","Morphological","Oxidative damage","Phenotypic plasticity","Photosynthesis","Plants","River delta","Salinity tolerance","Salt stress","Water stress"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"higher phenotypic plasticity does not confer higher salt resistance to i robinia pseudoacacia i than i amorpha fruticosa i","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85044770795","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-242507","identifier":[{"id":"85044770795","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000429450600015","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-c63ab490-f304-48d2-8689-b1e82707f15b"],"keyword":["Black locust","CHLOROPHYLL FLUORESCENCE","CLIMATE-CHANGE","GROWTH","Indigo bush","Morphological","OXIDATIVE DAMAGE","PHOTOSYNTHESIS","PHRAGMITES-AUSTRALIS POPULATIONS","PLANTS","Phenotypic plasticity","RIVER DELTA","SALINITY TOLERANCE","Salt stress","WATER-STRESS","and physiological parameters","biochemical"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-14CBA0841D347F430421562E05CB13BD"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"qingdao agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Qingdao Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"shandong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Aquatic Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"guoxiaopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Xiao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao-Huang","key":"renxiaohuangpau","last":"Ren","name":"Ren, Xiao-Huang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Franziska","key":"ellerfranziskapau","last":"Eller","locid":"15509be6-9a31-4be1-9fab-9bf9db482917","name":"Eller, Franziska","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ming-Yan","key":"limingyanpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Ming-Yan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ren-Qing","key":"wangrenqingpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Ren-Qing","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ning","key":"duningpau","last":"Du","name":"Du, Ning","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei-Hua","key":"guoweihuapau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Wei-Hua","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11738-018-2654-3","issn":["01375881","18611664"],"issn_org":["01375881"],"issue":"4","journal":"Acta Physiologiae Plantarum","paperid":"79","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"Acta Physiologiae Plantarum","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85044770795"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c63ab490-f304-48d2-8689-b1e82707f15b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Higher phenotypic plasticity does not confer higher salt resistance to <i>Robinia pseudoacacia </i>than<i> Amorpha fruticosa</i>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-242507","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The breast cancer risk variants identified in genome-wide association studies explain only a small fraction of the familial relative risk, and the genes responsible for these associations remain largely unknown. To identify novel risk loci and likely causal genes, we performed a transcriptome-wide association study evaluating associations of genetically predicted gene expression with breast cancer risk in 122,977 cases and 105,974 controls of European ancestry. We used data from the Genotype-Tissue Expression Project to establish genetic models to predict gene expression in breast tissue and evaluated model performance using data from The Cancer Genome Atlas. Of the 8,597 genes evaluated, significant associations were identified for 48 at a Bonferroni-corrected threshold of P < 5.82 × 10-6, including 14 genes at loci not yet reported for breast cancer. We silenced 13 genes and showed an effect for 11 on cell proliferation and/or colony-forming efficiency. Our study provides new insights into breast cancer genetics and biology.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Wu, Lang","Shi, Wei","Long, Jirong","Guo, Xingyi","Michailidou, Kyriaki","Beesley, Jonathan","Bolla, Manjeet K","Shu, Xiao-Ou","Lu, Yingchang","Cai, Qiuyin","Al-Ejeh, Fares","Rozali, Esdy","Wang, Qin","Dennis, Joe","Li, Bingshan","Zeng, Chenjie","Feng, Helian","Gusev, Alexander","Barfield, Richard T","Andrulis, Irene L","Anton-Culver, Hoda","Arndt, Volker","Aronson, Kristan J","Auer, Paul L","Barrdahl, Myrto","Baynes, Caroline","Beckmann, Matthias W","Benitez, Javier","Bermisheva, Marina","Blomqvist, Carl","Bogdanova, Natalia V","Bojesen, Stig E","Brauch, Hiltrud","Brenner, Hermann","Brinton, Louise","Broberg, Per","Brucker, Sara Y","Burwinkel, Barbara","Caldés, Trinidad","Canzian, Federico","Carter, Brian D","Castelao, J Esteban","Chang-Claude, Jenny","Chen, Xiaoqing","Cheng, Ting-Yuan David","Christiansen, Hans","Clarke, Christine L","Flyger, Henrik","Nielsen, Sune F","Nordestgaard, Børge G"],