.00-593422","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The aim of this study was to investigate the drug release profiles of biodegradable polymer sirolimus- or paclitaxel-eluting stents with asymmetrical coating (BPSES-A or BPPES-A) both in vitro and in vivo. In vitro, the drug release profile was characterized by measuring the drug concentration by HPLC over a time-course. In vivo, a porcine aorta stenting model was employed. The results showed that the drug release rates of BPSES-A and BPPES-A were slower, more stable and less burst releasing than those of conventionally coated stents (BPSES-C and BPPES-C respectively), both in vitro and in vivo. Based on the in vivo results, the sirolimus and paclitaxel content of the local coronary wall was maintained at a higher and more effective level with BPSES-A and BPPES-A than with BPSES-C and BPPES-C, respectively. The drug levels in peripheral tissue samples were below detection levels. These data demonstrated the effectiveness of both sirolimus and paclitaxel as stent coating agents, and revealed the favorable drug release kinetics and pharmacokinetics of asymmetrical coated stents compared with conventional coated stents.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Zhang, Haijun","Li, Xiaodong","Deng, Wei","Wang, Xiangfei","Wang, Shen-guo","Ge, Junbo","Toft, Egon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-118697"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"drug release kinetics from a drug eluting stent with asymmetrical coat","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.bioscience.org/2017/v22/af/4491/list.htm","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-118697","identifier":[{"id":"85039979312","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27814621","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000397910500002","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-ec407d74-78df-4bf6-b4a2-3fe753f0a3d9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CDD39F9DA650059DFB1FE93C986684DB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Sensory-Motor Interaction"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Haijun","key":"zhanghaijunpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"fc55809a-389e-4351-ae30-77433cd63adc","name":"Zhang, Haijun","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaodong","key":"lixiaodongpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiaodong","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"dengweipau","last":"Deng","name":"Deng, Wei","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiangfei","key":"wangxiangfeipau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Xiangfei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Shen-guo","key":"wangshenguopau","last":"Wang","locid":"79aca400-9da4-435b-8fea-895d3f8ac66e","name":"Wang, Shen-guo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Junbo","key":"gejunbopau","last":"Ge","name":"Ge, Junbo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Egon","key":"toftegonpau","last":"Toft","locid":"f82c9f05-794b-4506-b684-d5d56e98a6a0","name":"Toft, Egon","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27814621"],"pub":{"issn":["10934715","10939946"],"issn_org":["10939946"],"journal":"Frontiers in Bioscience","pages":"407-415","publisher":"Frontiers in Bioscience","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Bioscience","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85039979312"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ec407d74-78df-4bf6-b4a2-3fe753f0a3d9"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Drug release kinetics from a drug-eluting stent with asymmetrical coat","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-118697","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Much has been done to address the challenges of biological invasions, but fundamental questions (e.g., which species invade? Which habitats are invaded? How can invasions be effectively managed?) still need to be answered before the spread and impact of alien taxa can be effectively managed. Questions on the role of biogeography (e.g., how does biogeography influence ecosystem susceptibility, resistance and resilience against invasion?) have the greatest potential to address this goal by increasing our capacity to understand and accurately predict invasions at local, continental and global scales. This paper proposes a framework for the development of ‘Global Networks for Invasion Science’ to help generate approaches to address these critical and fundamentally biogeographic questions. We define global networks on the basis of their focus on research questions at the global scale, collection of primary data, use of standardized protocols and metrics, and commitment to long-term global data. Global networks are critical for the future of invasion science because of their potential to extend beyond the capacity of individual partners to identify global priorities for research agendas and coordinate data collection over space and time, assess risks and emerging trends, understand the complex influences of biogeography on mechanisms of invasion, predict the future of invasion dynamics, and use these new insights to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of evidence-based management techniques. While the pace and scale of global change continues to escalate, strategic and collaborative global networks offer a powerful approach to inform responses to the threats posed by biological invasions.","author_count":26,"contributors":["Packer, Jasmin G.","Meyerson, Laura A.","Richardson, David M.","Brundu, Giuseppe","Allen, Warwick J.","Bhattarai, Ganesh P.","Brix, Hans","Canavan, Susan","Castiglione, Stefano","Cicatelli, Angela","Čuda, Jan","Cronin, James T.","Eller, Franziska","Guarino, Francesco","Guo, Wei Hua","Guo, Wen Yong","Guo, Xiao","Hierro, José L.","Lambertini, Carla","Liu, Jian","Lozano, Vanessa","Mozdzer, Thomas J.","Skálová, Hana","Villarreal, Diego","Wang, Ren Qing","Pyšek, Petr"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-137923"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Packer, Jasmin G."],"country":["Argentina","China","Czechia","Italy","South Africa","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bryn Mawr College","Charles University","Czech Academy of Sciences","Laboratory of Integrative and Systems Physiology, School of Life Sciences, École Polytechnique Fédérale, 1015 Lausanne, Switzerland.","Louisiana State University","Qingdao Agricultural University","Shandong University","South African National Biodiversity Institute","Universidad Nacional de La Pampa","University of Florida","University of Rhode Island","University of Salerno","University of Sassari","University of Stellenbosch"],"keyword":["Biological invasions","Collaboration","Global change","Transdisciplinary"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"global networks for invasion science benefits challenges and guidelines","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84994707534","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-137923","identifier":[{"id":"84994707534","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-0ef41c23-baca-46ee-8878-3f4426a48db5"],"keyword":["Biogeographic","Biological invasions","Collaboration","Global change","Global research ne