{"abstract":"Purpose: To identify disease-causing mutations in a Chinese patient with retinitis pigmentosa (RP). Methods: A detailed clinical examination was performed on the proband. Targeted next-generation sequencing (NGS) combined with bioinformatics analysis was performed on the proband to detect candidate disease-causing mutations. Sanger sequencing was performed on all subjects to confirm the candidate mutations and assess cosegregation within the family. Results: Clinical examinations of the proband showed typical characteristics of RP. Three candidate heterozygous mutations in 3 genes associated with RP were detected in the proband by targeted NGS. The 3 mutations were confirmed by Sanger sequencing and the deletion (c.357_358delAA) in PRPF31 was shown to cosegregate with RP phenotype in 7 affected family members, but not in 3 unaffected family members. Conclusions: The deletion (c.357_358delAA) in PRPF31 was the disease-causing mutation for the proband and his affected family members with RP. To our knowledge, this is the second report of the deletion and the first report of the other 2 mutations in the Chinese population. Targeted NGS combined with bioinformatics analysis proved to be an effective molecular diagnostic tool for RP.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Xiao, Jianping","Guo, Xueqin","Wang, Yong","Shao, Mingkun","Wei, Xiaoming","Du, Lique","Li, Long","Sun, Yan","Yang, Yun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-398405"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","Central South University","Nanjing Medical University","The Second Hospital Affiliated Kunming Medical University"],"keyword":["PRPF31","Retinitis pigmentosa","Targeted next generation sequencing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identification of a disease causing mutation in a chinese patient with retinitis pigmentosa by targeted next generation sequencing","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85035032476&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-398405","identifier":[{"id":"28430325","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85035032476","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-083f7b69-8c00-4fbe-90e1-f2a02d14ea7c"],"keyword":["PRPF31","Retinitis pigmentosa","Targeted next-generation sequencing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-47671B78C883CB84D0A8CF84026F581D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"nanjing medical university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing Medical University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"bgi","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"central south university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Central South University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"the second hospital affiliated kunming medical university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"The Second Hospital Affiliated Kunming Medical University","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Genome Research and Molecular Bio Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jianping","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Jianping","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Xue