{"abstract":"This paper presents a theoretical study with experimental validation of a circulating-current suppression method for parallel operation of three-phase voltage source inverters (VSI), which may be suitable for modular parallel uninterruptible power supply systems or hybrid AC/DC microgrid applications. The basic concept of the proposed circulating-current suppression method is to modify the original current references by using the current difference among the parallel inverters. In the proposed approach, both of cross circulating-current and zero-sequence circulating-current are considered, and added into the conventional droop plus virtual impedance control. In the control architecture, the reference voltages of the inverters are generated by the primary control loop which consists of a droop control and a virtual impedance. The secondary control is used to compensate the voltage drop on the virtual impedance. Further, a circulating-current control loop is added to improve the average current-sharing performance among parallel VSIs. Experimental results are presented to show the effectiveness of the proposed control method to suppress both of the cross and zero-sequence circulating-currents.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Wei, Baoze","Guerrero, Josep M.","Vasquez, Juan C.","Guo, Xiaoqiang"],"cuid":["S02-085.35-003768"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Yanshan University"],"keyword":["Common DC and AC buses","Cross circulating current","Parallel connected","Voltage source inverter","Zero sequence","Zero sequence circulating current"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a circulating current suppression method for parallel connected voltage source inverters with common dc and ac buses","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/255852807/A_Circulating_Current_Suppression_Method_for_Para.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-085.35-003768","identifier":[{"id":"85029824599","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000407137700057","type":"wos"},{"id":"WOS:000407137700057","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-4cfc98bf-603c-4de0-9922-bda9711b7172","aau-88057015-d7d9-431b-8711-7c3516cddc0d"],"keyword":["Common DC and AC buses","Cross circulating-current","Parallel connected","Voltage source inverter","Zero sequence circulating current","Zero-sequence"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-EBAA5D48BB84F77F0057E578F93458D8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/255852807/A_Circulating_Current_Suppression_Method_for_Para.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"yanshan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Yanshan University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Baoze","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","locid":"c1d10e1a-3851-4908-acbf-fe7172fa3a2d","name":"Wei, Baoze","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Josep M.","key":"guerreropau","last":"Guerrero","locid":"07d2eed6-2177-4f61-b812-a08c55b2e8af","name":"Guerrero, Josep M.","orcid":"0000-0001-5236-4592","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Juan Carlos Vasquez","key":"quinteropau","last":"Quintero","locid":"6134752e-608e-45e4-9e0e-ee922174ce38","name":"Vasquez, Juan C.","name_org":"Quintero, Juan Carlos Vasquez","orcid":"0000-0001-6332-385X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Juan C.","key":"vasquezpau","last":"Vasquez","locid":"6134752e-608e-45e4-9e0e-ee922174ce38","name":"Vasquez, Juan C.","orcid":"0000-0001-6332-385X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoqiang","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Xiaoqiang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tia.2017.2681620","issn":["00939994"],"issue":"4","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Industry Applications","pages":"3758-3769","paperid":"7876828","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Industry Applications","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Industry Applications","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85029824599"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4cfc98bf-603c-4de0-9922-bda9711b7172","aau-88057015-d7d9-431b-8711-7c3516cddc0d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A Circulating-Current Suppression Method for Parallel-Connected Voltage-Source Inverters With Common DC and AC Buses","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.35-003768","year":2017,"yearsub":2017}
{"abstract":"Hypothesis Synthetic sugar alcohol mono-behenates with high melting points, surface activity and resistance to enzymatic lipolysis, are expected to form stable single-component solid lipid nanocarriers (SC-SLNs). The preparation methods and the polar head group of the molecules should affect the size and drug encapsulation efficiency. Experiments SC-SLNs of sugar alcohol mono-behenates with varied polar heads were prepared using emulsification-diffusion method and melting-probe sonication method. Model lipophilic drug fenofibrate was formulated into nanocarriers. The drug release was assessed using the lipolysis model. The structure and drug distribution of the nanocarriers were studied using AFM and TEM. Findings Both the polar head group of the molecules and the preparation methods affect the particle size and size distribution. Nanocarriers prepared with sorbitol mono-behenates showed the smallest mean size (∼100 nm with PdI of 0.26). In addition, they displayed high entrapment efficiency of fenofibrate (95%) and long term drug release. Nanocarriers prepared by emulsification-diffusion method entrapped fenofibrate into lipid bilayers. In contrast, Nanocarriers prepared by melting-probe sonication method had a micelle structure with fenofibrate incorporated into a lipid monolayer. This study provides an insight into the systematic development of novel amphiphilic lipids for solid lipid-based drug delivery system.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Wei, Wei","Lu, Xiaonan","Wang, Zegao","Pérez, Bianca","Liu, Jingying","Wu, Chengyu","Dong, Mingdong","Feng, Fengqin","Mu, Huiling","Guo, Zheng"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-021748"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Jiangnan University","Zhejiang University"],"keyword":["Journal Article","Lipid based delivery system","Nanocarriers"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"single component solid lipid nanocarriers prepared with ultra long chain amphiphilic lipids","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85020706245","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-021748","identifier":[{"id":"28623698","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85020706245","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-7c9f9fd1-01a2-4824-b3dd-5b133a89da6b","ku-ee0358bf-5e84-41d0-9805-7079e7222e5e"],"keyword":["Amphiphilic lipids","Journal Article","Lipid-based delivery system","Nanocarriers","Single-component"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-613BD875D1522C865F436B4BC90F617A"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Engineering, Department of Engineering - Biological and Chemical Engineering, Gustav Wieds Vej"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"jiangnan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jiangnan University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Pharmaceutical Design and Drug Delivery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","locid":"eba1f296-6e64-4865-9eb0-8f10c76bc212","name":"Wei, Wei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaonan","key":"lupau","last":"Lu","locid":"faa213a8-44ee-48c1-9253-47963e89de68","name":"Lu, Xiaonan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zegao","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"2f191f69-88c1-4291-8610-6d3b85bbc312","name":"Wang, Zegao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bianca","key":"pérezpau","last":"Pérez","locid":"53fb7df0-13cb-4efd-a0eb-aa03e8db8f9c","name":"Pérez, Bianca","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Jingying","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","locid":"80b4a1c8-f180-4e84-ac1e-f0711d6362e7","name":"Liu, Jingying","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Chengyu","key":"wupau","last":"Wu","locid":"374c5173-0a33-4d31-996d-82f042d1bca4","name":"Wu, Chengyu","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"MD","key":"dongpau","last":"Dong","locid":"b54afe28-ba86-4353-9f09-6618abd83284","name":"Dong, Mingdong","name_org":"Dong, MD","orcid":"0000-0002-2025-2171","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Fengqin","key":"fengpau","last":"Feng","name":"Feng, Fengqin","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Huiling","key":"mupau","last":"Mu","locid":"f112da1b-f1ab-4891-bf6a-3c799d71d4cc","name":"Mu, Huiling","orcid":"0000-0001-9246-3931","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zheng","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","locid":"67372258-2bc9-4585-98c9-1b93c60d0ca9","name":"Guo, Zheng","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28623698"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jcis.2017.06.022","issn":["00219797","10957103"],"issn_org":["00219797"],"journal":"Journal of Colloid and Interface Science","pages":"392-401","publisher":"Academic Press Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Colloid and Interface Science","volume":"505"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85020706245"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7c9f9fd1-01a2-4824-b3dd-5b133a89da6b","ku-ee0358bf-5e84-41d0-9805-7079e7222e5e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Single-component solid lipid nanocarriers prepared with ultra-long chain amphiphilic lipids","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-021748","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Microinfarcts occur commonly in the aging brain as a consequence of diffuse embolic events and are associated with the development of vascular dementia and Alzheimer's disease. However, the manner in which disperse microscopic lesions reduce global cognitive function and increase the risk for Alzheimer's disease is unclear. The glymphatic system, which is a brain-wide perivascular network that supports the recirculation of CSF through the brain parenchyma, facilitates the clearance of interstitial solutes including amyloid β and tau. We investigated whether glymphatic pathway function is impaired in a murine model of multiple microinfarcts induced by intraarterial injection of cholesterol crystals. The analysis showed that multiple microinfarcts markedly impaired global influx of CSF along the glymphatic pathway. Although suppression of global glymphatic function was transient, resolving within 2 weeks of injury, CSF tracers also accumulated within tissue associated with microinfarcts. The effect of diffuse microinfarcts on global glymphatic pathway function was exacerbated in the mice aged 12 months compared with the 2- to 3-month-old mice. These findings indicate that glymphatic function is focally disrupted around microinfarcts and that the aging brain is more vulnerable to this disruption than the young brain. These observations suggest that microlesions may trap proteins and other interstitial solutes within the brain parenchyma, increasing the risk of amyloid plaque formation.SIGNIFICANCE STATEMENT Microinfarcts, small (<1 mm) ischemic lesions, are strongly associated with age-related dementia. However, how these microscopic lesions affect global cognitive function and predispose to Alzheimer's disease is unclear. The glymphatic system is a brain-wide network of channels surrounding brain blood vessels that allows CSF to exchange with interstitial fluid, clearing away cellular wastes such as amyloid β. We observed that, in mice, microinfarcts impaired global glymphatic function and solutes from the CSF became trapped in tissue associated with microinfarcts. These data suggest that small, disperse ischemic lesions can impair glymphatic function across the brain and trapping of solutes in these lesions may promote protein aggregation and neuroinflammation and eventually lead to neurodegeneration, especially in the aging brain.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Wang, Minghuan","Ding, Fengfei","Deng, SaiYue","Guo, Xuequn","Wang, Wei","Iliff, Jeffrey J","Nedergaard, Maiken"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-476017"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"focal solute trapping and global glymphatic pathway impairment in a murine model of multiple microinfarcts","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc5354332?pdf=render","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-476017","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5354332","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85015265549","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28188218","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-8a1ef557-9eaa-4a37-8d9e-a4650282940a"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AA450392DDDBE7B14518674ED171928C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc5354332?pdf=render","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Center for Translational Neuromedicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Minghuan","key":"wangminghuanpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Minghuan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Fengfei","key":"dingfengfeipau","last":"Ding","name":"Ding, Fengfei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"SaiYue","key":"dengsaiyuepau","last":"Deng","name":"Deng, SaiYue","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xuequn","key":"guoxuequnpau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Xuequn","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wei","key":"wangweipau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Wei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jeffrey J","key":"iliffjeffreyjpau","last":"Iliff","name":"Iliff, Jeffrey J","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maiken","key":"nedergaardmaikenpau","last":"Nedergaard","locid":"75ab8cc8-65d9-4421-9612-61f446075715","name":"Nedergaard, Maiken","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28188218"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1523/jneurosci.2112-16.2017","issn":["02706474","15292401"],"issn_org":["02706474"],"issue":"11","journal":"Journal of Neuroscience","pages":"2870-2877","status":"p","title":"Journal of Neuroscience","title_org":"The Journal of neuroscience : the official journal of the Society for Neuroscience","volume":"37"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85015265549"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8a1ef557-9eaa-4a37-8d9e-a4650282940a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Focal Solute Trapping and Global Glymphatic Pathway Impairment in a Murine Model of Multiple Microinfarcts","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-476017","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"On 2017 August 17, the gravitational-wave event GW170817 was observed by the Advanced LIGO and Virgo detectors, and the gamma-ray burst (GRB) GRB 170817A was observed independently by the Fermi Gamma-ray Burst Monitor, and the Anti-Coincidence Shield for the Spectrometer for the International Gamma-Ray Astrophysics Laboratory. The probability of the near-simultaneous temporal and spatial observation of GRB 170817A and GW170817 occurring by chance is 5.0 x 10-8. We therefore confirm binary neutron star mergers as a progenitor of short GRBs. The association of GW170817 and GRB 170817A provides new insight into fundamental physics and the origin of short GRBs. We use the observed time delay of (+1.74± 0.05)s between GRB 170817A and GW170817 to: (i) constrain the difference between the speed of gravity and the speed of light to be between -3x10-15 and +7x 10-16 times the speed of light, (ii) place new bounds on the violation of Lorentz invariance, (iii) present a new test of the equivalence principle by constraining the Shapiro delay between gravitational and electromagnetic radiation. We also use the time delay to constrain the size and bulk Lorentz factor of the region emitting the gamma-rays. GRB 170817A is the closest short GRB with a known distance, but is between 2 and 6 orders of magnitude less energetic than other bursts with measured redshift. A new generation of gamma-ray detectors, and subthreshold searches in existing detectors, will be essential to detect similar short bursts at greater distances. Finally, we predict a joint detection rate for the Fermi Gamma-ray Burst Monitor and the Advanced LIGO and Virgo detectors of 0.1–1.4 per year during the 2018–2019 observing run and 0.3–1.7 per year at design sensitivity.","author_count":1153,"contributors":["Abbott, B. P.","Abbott, R.","Abbott, T. D.","Acernese, F.","Ackley, K.","Adams, C.","Adams, T.","Addesso, P.","Adhikari, R. X.","Adya, V. B.","Affeldt, C.","Afrough, M.","Agarwal, B.","Agathos, M