{"abstract":"A Gram-stain-negative and rod-shaped bacterial strain, 12-OD1T, with rock phosphate solubilizing ability was isolated from agricultural soil in Hailun, Heilongjiang, PR China. The isolate was affiliated to the genus Massilia, based on 16S rRNA gene sequence alignments, having the highest similarities with Massilia putida6 NM-7T (98.67 %), Massilia kyonggiensis TSA1T (98.28 %), and Massilia norwichensis NS9T (98.07 %), respectively. The DNA G+C content was 67.72 mol% and DNA-DNA hybridization showed low relatedness values (less than 47 %) between strain 12-OD1T and other phylogenetically related species of the genus Massilia. The predominant isoprenoid quinone was Q-8 and the polar lipid profile comprised diphosphatidylglycerol, phosphatidylglycerol and phosphatidylethanolamine. The major fatty acids were C17:0 cyclo (25.4 %), C16:0 (23.4 %) and summed feature 3 (C16:1ω7c and/or C16:1 ω6c) (22.5 %), which differentiates it from close relatives within the genus Massilia. Combined genetic, physiological and biochemical properties indicate that strain 12-OD1T is a novel species of the genus Massilia, for which the name Massilia phosphatilytica sp. nov., is proposed, with the type strain 12-OD1T (=CCTCC AB 2016251T=LMG 29956T=KCTC 52513T).","author_count":5,"contributors":["Zheng, Bang Xiao","Bi, Qing Fang","Hao, Xiuli","Zhou, Guo Wei","Yang, Xiao Ru"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-472600"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Zhejiang University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"i massilia phosphatilytica i sp nov a phosphate solubilizing bacteria isolated from a long term fertilized soil","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-472600","identifier":[{"id":"28853679","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85029535959","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8444234c-e4bc-43c8-a4ee-b07616ccf929"],"keyword":["Massilia phosphatilytica","Phosphate solubilizing ability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F6B6237727C61D738F60385A2D6C5719"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Microbial Ecology and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Bang Xiao","key":"zhengpau","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Bang Xiao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Qing Fang","key":"bipau","last":"Bi","name":"Bi, Qing Fang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Xiuli","key":"haopau","last":"Hao","locid":"6b90e69c-6a7c-41c0-8814-d0289923e44c","name":"Hao, Xiuli","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Guo Wei","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Guo Wei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiao Ru","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Xiao Ru","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28853679"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1099/ijsem.0.001916","issn":["10706259","14665026"],"issn_org":["14665026"],"issue":"8","journal":"International Journal of Systematic and Evolutionary Microbiology","pages":"2514-2519","paperid":"001916","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Systematic and Evolutionary Microbiology","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85029535959"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8444234c-e4bc-43c8-a4ee-b07616ccf929"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"<i>Massilia phosphatilytica</i> sp. nov., a phosphate solubilizing bacteria isolated from a long-term fertilized soil","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-472600","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: To assess the diagnostic performance of quantitative flow ratio (QFR) for diagnosis of hemodynamically-significant coronary stenosis defined by fractional flow reserve (FFR) ≤0.80. BACKGROUND: QFR is a novel angiography-based method for deriving FFR without pressure wire or induction of hyperemia. The accuracy of QFR when assessed online in the catheterization laboratory has not been adequately examined to date. METHODS: This prospective, multicenter trial enrolled patients who had at least one lesion with diameter stenosis of 30-90% and reference diameter ≥ 2mm by visual estimation. QFR, quantitative coronary angiography (QCA), and wire-based FFR were assessed online in blinded fashion during coronary angiography and re-analyzed offline at an independent core laboratory. The primary endpoint was that QFR would improve the diagnostic accuracy of coronary angiography such that the lower boundary of the 2-sided 95% confidence interval (CI) of this estimate exceeded 75%. RESULTS: Between June and July 2017, 308 patients were consecutively enrolled at 5 centers. Online QFR and FFR results were both obtained in 328 of 332 interrogated vessels. Patient-level and vessel-level diagnostic accuracy of QFR were 92.4% (95% CI: 88.9%-95.1%) and 92.7% (95% CI: 89.3%-95.3%), that were both significantly higher than the prespecified target value (p <0.001). Sensitivity and specificity in identifying hemodynamically-significant stenosis were significantly higher for QFR than QCA (sensitivity: 94.6% versus 62.5%, difference: 32.0%, p <0.001; specificity: 91.7% versus 58.1%, difference: 36.1%, p <0.001). Positive predictive value, negative predictive value, positive likelihood ratio, and negative likelihood ratio for QFR was 85.5%, 97.1%, 11.4, and 0.06, respectively. Offline analysis also showed vessel-level QFR had a high diagnostic accuracy of 93.3% (95% CI: 90.0%, 95.7%). CONCLUSIONS: The study met its prespecified primary performance goal for the level of diagnostic accuracy of QFR in identifying hemodynamically-significant coronary stenosis.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Xu, Bo","Tu, Shengxian","Qiao, Shubin","Qu, Xinkai","Chen, Yundai","Yang, Junqing","Guo, Lijun","Sun, Zhongwei","Li, Zehang","Tian, Feng","Fang, Weiyi","Chen, Jiyan","Li, Wei","Guan, Changdong","Holm, Niels Ramsing","Wijns, William","Hu, Shengshou"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-166797"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences","PLA General Hospital","Peking University","Shanghai Jiao Tong University"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"angiography based quantitative flow ratio for online assessment of coronary stenosis favor ii china study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85037371874","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-166797","identifier":[{"id":"85037371874","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29101020","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-41d34923-5509-4936-a5d9-3c97cd2a91a6"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-158CF20EAC9F6982D41EA15FDF31F5CA"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of medical sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"shanghai jiao tong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai Jiao Tong University","used