{"abstract":"The ecological effect of reclaimed water irrigation and fertilizer application on the soil environment is receiving more attention. Soil microbial activity and nitrogen (N) levels are important indicators of the effect of reclaimed water irrigation on environment. This study evaluated soil physicochemical properties and microbial community structure in soils irrigated with reclaimed water and receiving varied amounts of N fertilizer. The results indicated that the reclaimed water irrigation increased soil electrical conductivity (EC) and soil water content (SWC). The N treatment has highly significant effect on the ACE, Chao, Shannon (H) and Coverage indices. Based on a 16S ribosomal RNA (16S rRNA) sequence analysis, the Proteobacteria, Gemmatimonadetes and Bacteroidetes were more abundant in soil irrigated with reclaimed water than in soil irrigated with clean water. Stronger clustering of microbial communities using either clean or reclaimed water for irrigation indicated that the type of irrigation water may have a greater influence on the structure of soil microbial community than N fertilizer treatment. Based on a canonical correspondence analysis (CCA) between the species of soil microbes and the chemical properties of the soil, which indicated that nitrate N (NO3−-N) and total phosphorus (TP) had significant impact on abundance of Verrucomicrobia and Gemmatimonadetes, meanwhile the pH and organic matter (OM) had impact on abundance of Firmicutes and Actinobacteria significantly. It was beneficial to the improvement of soil bacterial activity and fertility under 120 mg kg−1N with reclaimed water irrigation.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Guo, Wei","Andersen, Mathias Neumann","Qi, Xue-bin","Li, Ping","Li, Zhong-yang","Fan, Xiang-yang","Zhou, Yuan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-239135"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Nitrogen","Soil chemical properties","reclaimed water"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of reclaimed water irrigation and nitrogen fertilization on the chemical properties and microbial community of soil","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S2095-3119(16)61391-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-239135","identifier":[{"id":"85015050166","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c06dc0b9-7fe3-4455-83c3-c8dba0ddc270"],"keyword":["16S rRNA sequence","nitrogen","reclaimed water","soil chemical properties","soil microbe community"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8D915E3A803A084E8E8588A212238D29"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S2095-3119(16)61391-6","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Climate and Water"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"guoweipau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Wei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathias Neumann","key":"andersenmathiasneumannpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"10eb9048-1aa0-4bd2-8809-35269cd68730","name":"Andersen, Mathias Neumann","orcid":"0000-0003-3845-4465","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Xue-bin","key":"qixuebinpau","last":"Qi","name":"Qi, Xue-bin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ping","key":"lipingpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Ping","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhong-yang","key":"lizhongyangpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Zhong-yang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiang-yang","key":"fanxiangyangpau","last":"Fan","name":"Fan, Xiang-yang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuan","key":"zhouyuanpau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Yuan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/s2095-3119(16)61391-6","issn":["20953119"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Integrative Agriculture","pages":"679-690","publisher":"KeAi Publishing Communications Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Integrative Agriculture","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85015050166"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c06dc0b9-7fe3-4455-83c3-c8dba0ddc270"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Effects of reclaimed water irrigation and nitrogen fertilization on the chemical properties and microbial community of soil","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-239135","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Inorganic phosphate solubilizing bacteria (iPSB) are essential to facilitate phosphorus (P) mobilization in alkaline soil, however, the phylogenetic structure of iPSB communities remains poorly characterized. Thus, we use a reference iPSB database to analyze the distribution of iPSB communities based on 16S rRNA gene illumina sequencing. Additionally, a noval pqqC primer was developed to quantify iPSB abundance. In our study, an alkaline soil with 27-year fertilization treatment was selected. The percentage of iPSB was 1.10~2.87% per sample, and the dominant iPSB genera were closely related to Arthrobacter, Bacillus, Brevibacterium and Streptomyces. Long-term P fertilization had no significant effect on the abundance of iPSB communities. Rather than P and potassium (K) additions, long-term nitrogen (N) fertilization decreased the iPSB abundance, which was validated by reduced relative abundance of pqqC gene (pqqC/16S). The decreased iPSB abundance was strongly related to pH decline and total N increase, revealing that the long-term N additions may cause pH decline and subsequent P releases relatively decreasing the demands of the iPSB community. The methodology and understanding obtained here provides insights into the ecology of inorganic P solubilizers and how to manipulate for better P use efficiency.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Zheng, Bang-Xiao","Hao, Xiuli","Ding, Kai","Zhou, Guo-Wei","Chen, Qing-Lin","Zhang, Jia-Bao","Zhu, Yong-Guan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-521725"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term nitrogen fertilization decreased the abundance of inorganic phosphate solubilizing bacteria in an alkaline soil","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/srep42284","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-521725","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5299424","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28181569","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85012055061","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d6b0d25d-bd41-42bc-b4d4-5023b28b0d6a"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C1F4452DF40FCB7C63B4A6F166CA2CFC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/srep42284","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/180763123/srep42284.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Microbial Ecology and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Bang-Xiao","key":"zhengpau","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Bang-Xiao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiuli","key":"haopau","last":"Hao","locid":"6b90e69c-6a7c-41c0-8814-d0289923e44c","name":"Hao, Xiuli","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kai","key":"dingpau","last":"Ding","name":"Ding, Kai","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Guo-Wei","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Guo-Wei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Qing-Lin","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Qing-Lin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jia-Bao","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Jia-Bao","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yong-Guan","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Yong-Guan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28181569"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/srep42284","issn":["20452322"],"journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"42284","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85012055061"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d6b0d25d-bd41-42bc-b4d4-5023b28b0d6a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Long-term nitrogen fertilization decreased the abundance of inorganic phosphate solubilizing bacteria in an alkaline soil","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-521725","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, a novel control method was proposed for current source inverters under the grid-connected working mode. The control scheme is based on a modified droop control method, with an additional current reference signal that will be generated instead of the voltage reference. Hence, there is only a current control loop with droop control in the whole control scheme without voltage control loop. So it is very suitable for grid-connected current source inverter which will simplify the design of the control scheme and combine the advantage of droop control. The parallel configuration is widely used to acquire high power demand, but the circulating current problem is a key issue that should be considered. In this paper, a simulation based on parallel current source inverters using the proposed control scheme is provided. Simulation results showed that a good circulating current suppression capability of the proposed control scheme is obtained with a proper controller design.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Wei, Baoze","Guerrero, Josep M.","Vasquez, Juan C.","Guo, Xiaoqiang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-071731"],"event":{"end":"2016-10-27","place":"Florence, it","start":"2016-10-24","title":"42nd Conference of the Industrial Electronics Society, IECON 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Yanshan University"],"keyword":["Circulating current","Current source inverter","Droop control","Grid connected"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a modified droop control method for parallel connected current source inverters","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/244530843/IECON2016_A_Modified_Droop_Control_Method_for_Parallel_Connected_Current.._.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-071731","identifier":[{"id":"85010023366","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-4ad287e8-e1dd-4c41-9cfc-7596e505ff07"],"keyword":["Circulating current","Current-source inverter","Droop control","Grid-connected"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-05F41BC8CDB8CE8621290D602233AE43"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/244530843/IECON2016_A_Modified_Droop_Control_Method_for_Parallel_Connected_Current.._.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"yanshan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Yanshan University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Baoze","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","locid":"c1d10e1a-3851-4908-acbf-fe7172fa3a2d","name":"Wei, Baoze","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Josep M.","key":"guerreropau","last":"Guerrero","locid":"07d2eed6-2177-4f61-b812-a08c55b2e8af","name":"Guerrero, Josep M.","orcid":"0000-0001-5236-4592","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Juan Carlos Vasquez","key":"quinteropau","last":"Quintero","locid":"6134752e-608e-45e4-9e0e-ee922174ce38","name":"Vasquez, Juan C.","name_org":"Quintero, Juan Carlos Vasquez","orcid":"0000-0001-6332-385X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoqiang","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Xiaoqiang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/iecon.2016.7793804","eisbn":["9781509034741"],"pages":"5195-5200","publisher":"IEEE Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of IECON 2016: The 42nd Annual Conference of IEEE Industrial Electronics Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85010023366"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4ad287e8-e1dd-4c41-9cfc-7596e505ff07"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A Modified Droop Control Method for Parallel-Connected Current Source Inverters","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-071731","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The microgrid inverter experiences the power oscillations and current harmonics in case of the unbalanced grid voltage faults. However, there is a trade-off between power oscillations and current harmonics should be considered in three phase three wire inverter systems during the conventional fault ride through control. In order to solve this problem, a novel control strategy is proposed to enhance the output current quality while mitigating the active and reactive output power oscillations. Moreover, a simple current-limited control strategy can be achieved without the necessity of the voltage/current positive/negative sequence extraction. Finally, the simulation tests of the conventional and proposed control solutions are carried out. The results verify the effectiveness of the proposed strategy.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Liu, Wenzhao","Guo, Xiaoqiang","Sulligoi, Giorgio","Guan, Yajuan","Zhao, Xin","Wei, Baoze","Savaghebi, Mehdi","Guerrero, Josep M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-120806"],"event":{"end":"2016-09-22","place":"Milwaukee, WI, us","start":"2016-09-18","title":"8th Annual IEEE Energy Conversion Congress &amp; Exposition","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["China","Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Trieste","Yanshan University"],"keyword":["Fault ride through","Unbalanced"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enhanced power quality and minimized peak current control in an inverter based microgrid under unbalanced grid faults","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/241717733/EC_0138.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-120806","identifier":[{"id":"85015365740","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f356acdd-f346-4714-87ed-a7ea6df962d2"],"keyword":["Current-limited","Fault ride through","Microgrid inverter","Unbalanced"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-249D20395A58CE34C7EFB92C2C4E470E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/241717733/EC_0138.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"yanshan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Yanshan University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"university of trieste","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Trieste","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Wenzhao","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","locid":"8b628bec-bd31-4c3d-9c00-7907ae1917dd","name":"Liu, Wenzhao","orcid":"0000-0001-7506-0663","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoqiang","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Xiaoqiang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Giorgio","key":"sulligoipau","last":"Sulligoi","name":"Sulligoi, Giorgio","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yajuan","key":"guanpau","last":"Guan","locid":"895d5c99-3647-49a9-aab7-e5f75499b973","name":"Guan, Yajuan","orcid":"0000-0002-1968-1542","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xin","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","locid":"8d3d812c-1101-4fc1-b180-e9a3527d9535","name":"Zhao, Xin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Baoze","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","locid":"c1d10e1a-3851-4908-acbf-fe7172fa3a2d","name":"Wei, Baoze","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mehdi","key":"savaghebipau","last":"Savaghebi","locid":"7b715a35-2954-4210-b5d1-05e7e074af95","name":"Savaghebi, Mehdi","orcid":"0000-0001-6188-0265","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Josep M.","key":"guerreropau","last":"Guerrero","locid":"07d2eed6-2177-4f61-b812-a08c55b2e8af","name":"Guerrero, Josep M.","orcid":"0000-0001-5236-4592","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ecce.2016.7855083","eisbn":["9781509007370"],"publisher":"IEEE Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 8th Annual IEEE Energy Conversion Congress &amp; Exposition (ECCE), 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85015365740"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f356acdd-f346-4714-87ed-a7ea6df962d2"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Enhanced Power Quality and Minimized Peak Current Control in An Inverter based Microgrid under Unbalanced Grid Faults","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-120806","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Previous genome-wide association studies among women of European ancestry identified two independent breast cancer susceptibility loci represented by single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) rs13281615 and rs11780156 at 8q24. A fine-mapping study across 2.06 Mb (chr8:127,561,724-129,624,067, hg19) in 55,540 breast cancer cases and 51,168 controls within the Breast Cancer Association Consortium was conducted. Three additional independent association signals in women of European ancestry, represented by rs35961416 (OR = 0.95, 95% CI = 0.93-0.97, conditional p = 5.8 × 10(-6) ), rs7815245 (OR = 0.94, 95% CI = 0.91-0.96, conditional p = 1.1 × 10(-6) ) and rs2033101 (OR = 1.05, 95% CI = 1.02-1.07, conditional p = 1.1 × 10(-4) ) were found. Integrative analysis using functional genomic data from the Roadmap Epigenomics, the Encyclopedia of DNA Elements project, the Cancer Genome Atlas and other public resources implied that SNPs rs7815245 in Signal 3, and rs1121948 in Signal 5 (in linkage disequilibrium with rs11780156, r(2)  = 0.77), were putatively functional variants for two of the five independent association signals. The results highlighted multiple 8q24 variants associated with breast cancer susceptibility in women of European ancestry.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Shi, Jiajun","Zhang, Yanfeng","Zheng, Wei","Michailidou, Kyriaki","Ghoussaini, Maya","Bolla, Manjeet K","Wang, Qin","Dennis, Joe","Lush, Michael","Milne, Roger L","Shu, Xiao-Ou","Beesley, Jonathan","Kar, Siddhartha","Andrulis, Irene L","Anton-Culver, Hoda","Arndt, Volker","Beckmann, Matthias W","Zhao, Zhiguo","Guo, Xingyi","Benitez, Javier","Beeghly-Fadiel, Alicia","Blot, William","Bogdanova, Natalia V","Bojesen, Stig E","Brauch, Hiltrud","Brenner, Hermann","Brinton, Louise","Broeks, Annegien","Brüning, Thomas","Burwinkel, Barbara","Cai, Hui","Canisius, Sander","Chang-Claude, Jenny","Choi, Ji-Yeob","Couch, Fergus J","Cox, Angela","Cross, Simon S","Czene, Kamila","Darabi, Hatef","Devilee, Peter","Droit, Arnaud","Dork, Thilo","Fasching, Peter A","Fletcher, Olivia","Flyger, Henrik","Fostira, Florentia","Gaborieau, Valerie","García-Closas, Montserrat","Giles, Graham G","Grip, Mervi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-441794"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["kConFab Investigators"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fine scale mapping of 000000000008q000000000024 locus identifies multiple independent risk variants for breast cancer","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-441794","identifier":[{"id":"27087578","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5110427","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84977540132","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-50fe68c8-d008-4124-ada7-762e47c1f15b"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-02DD543212284140ECA0C1BBAB07F8C3"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"kconfab investigators","name":"kConFab Investigators","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Jiajun","key":"shipau","last":"Shi","name":"Shi, Jiajun","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yanfeng","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yanfeng","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":""