{"abstract":"This paper describes a theoretical and simulation study on a control strategy for the parallel operation of three-phase current source inverters (CSI), to be applied to uninterruptible power systems (UPS). A circulating current suppression strategy for parallel CSIs is proposed in this paper based on an auxiliary current control loop used to modify the reference currents by compensating the error currents between parallel inverters. The proposed method is coordinated together with droop and virtual impedance control. In this paper, droop control is used to generate the reference voltage of each inverter, and the virtual impedance is used to fix the output impedance of the inverters. In addition, a secondary control is used in order to recover the voltage deviation caused by the virtual impedance. and the auxiliary current control loop is added to acquire a better average current sharing performance among parallel CSIs, which can effectively suppress the circulating current. Simulation results are presented in order to verify the effectiveness of the proposed control methodology.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Wei, Baoze","Vasquez, Juan C.","Guerrero, Josep M.","Guo, Xiaoqiang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-060055"],"event":{"end":"2016-05-26","place":"Hefei, cn","start":"2016-05-22","title":"8th IEEE International Power Electronics and Motion Control Conference, IPEMC-ECCE Asia 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Yanshan University"],"keyword":["Circulating current","Current source inverter","Parallel","Uninterruptible power system"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"control architecture for paralleled current source inverter csi based uninterruptible power systems ups","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/244786707/Control_architecture_for_paralleled_current_source_inverter_CSI_based_..._1.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-060055","identifier":[{"id":"84983297323","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-2267f6fe-e2eb-4ac6-8ed2-b5a8e8e7e95a"],"keyword":["Circulating current","Current source inverter","Parallel","Uninterruptible power system"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-66107FF13B0F445BEE6AF2DBE2FF49CB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/244786707/Control_architecture_for_paralleled_current_source_inverter_CSI_based_..._1.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"yanshan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Yanshan University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Baoze","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","locid":"c1d10e1a-3851-4908-acbf-fe7172fa3a2d","name":"Wei, Baoze","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Juan C.","key":"vasquezpau","last":"Vasquez","locid":"6134752e-608e-45e4-9e0e-ee922174ce38","name":"Vasquez, Juan C.","orcid":"0000-0001-6332-385X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Josep M.","key":"guerreropau","last":"Guerrero","locid":"07d2eed6-2177-4f61-b812-a08c55b2e8af","name":"Guerrero, Josep M.","orcid":"0000-0001-5236-4592","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoqiang","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Xiaoqiang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ipemc.2016.7512278","eisbn":["9781509012107"],"pages":"151-156","publisher":"IEEE Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2016 IEEE 8th International Power Electronics and Motion Control Conference, IPEMC-ECCE Asia 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84983297323"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2267f6fe-e2eb-4ac6-8ed2-b5a8e8e7e95a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Control architecture for paralleled current-source-inverter (CSI) based uninterruptible power systems (UPS)","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-060055","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"In this letter, with combined belief propagation (BP), mean field (MF), and expectation propagation (EP), an iterative receiver is designed for joint phase noise estimation, equalization, and decoding in a coded communication system. The presence of the phase noise results in a nonlinear observation model. Conventionally, the nonlinear model is directly linearized by using the first-order Taylor approximation, e.g., in the state-of-the-art soft-input extended Kalman smoothing approach (Soft-in EKS). In this letter, MF is used to handle the factor due to the nonlinear model, and a second-order Taylor approximation is used to achieve Gaussian approximation to the MF messages, which is crucial to the low-complexity implementation of the receiver with BP and EP. It turns out that our approximation is more effective than the direct linearization in the Soft-in EKS, leading to a significant performance improvement with similar complexity as demonstrated by simulation results.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Wang, Wei","Wang, Zhongyong","Zhang, Chuanzong","Guo, Qinghua","Sun, Peng","Wang, Xingye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-091892"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","North University of China","University of Western Australia","University of Wollongong","Zhengzhou University"],"keyword":["Iterative receiver","Message passing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a bp mf ep based iterative receiver for joint phase noise estimation equalization and decoding","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=84986192060&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-091892","identifier":[{"id":"84986192060","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000395013900003","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-900564fc-58d4-451b-8748-d4c4f77ea9c0"],"keyword":["Iterative receiver","Phase noise estimation","message passing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-020A8E05F61DA7EA85CCB3E733407D6F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"zhengzhou university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhengzhou University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Wireless Communication Networks"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"university of wollongong","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Wollongong","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"au","key":"university of western australia","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Western Australia","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"north university of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"North University of China","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"wangweipau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Wei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhongyong","key":"wangzhongyongpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Zhongyong","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Chuanzong","key":"zhangchuanzongpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"8ce9e340-6c3a-403d-b22e-1c272fe0a9af","name":"Zhang, Chuanzong","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Qinghua","key":"guoqinghuapau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Qinghua","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peng","key":"sunpengpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Peng","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Xingye","key":"wangxingyepau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Xingye","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/lsp.2016.2593917","issn":["10709908","15582361"],"issn_org":["10709908"],"issue":"10","journal":"IEEE Signal Processing Letters","pages":"1349-1353","paperid":"7519016","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Signal Processing Letters","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84986192060"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-900564fc-58d4-451b-8748-d4c4f77ea9c0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A BP-MF-EP Based Iterative Receiver for Joint Phase Noise Estimation, Equalization, and Decoding","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-091892","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Two arrays of behenoyl (22:0) based amphiphilic lipids with sugar alcohols as a flexible linker were synthesized through acylation of sugar alcohol mono-behenates with diacetyl tartaric anhydride or acetoxy succinic anhydride and some of the resulting products are capable of yielding stable and uniform solid lipid nanoparticles (SLNs) (mean diameter ∼100 nm, PDI < 0.2) without any additive surfactant, displaying excellent dual functions (as both a solid lipid excipient and emulsifier).","author_count":6,"contributors":["Wei, Wei","Lu, Xiaonan","Wang, Zegao","Dong, Mingdong","Feng, Fengqin","Guo, Zheng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-214981"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Jiangnan University","Zhejiang University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"synthetic ultra long chain fatty acyl based amphiphilic lipids as a dual function excipient for the production of surfactant free solid lipid nanoparticles sf slns a physico chemical study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84978795504","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-214981","identifier":[{"id":"84978795504","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-965c4ab6-d376-40d8-919b-67b5877b43b5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-337A4B1362B841ADC58CFE62C2A56BC0"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Engineering, Department of Engineering - Biological and Chemical Engineering, Gustav Wieds Vej"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"jiangnan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jiangnan University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","locid":"eba1f296-6e64-4865-9eb0-8f10c76bc212","name":"Wei, Wei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaonan","key":"lupau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Xiaonan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zegao","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"2f191f69-88c1-4291-8610-6d3b85bbc312","name":"Wang, Zegao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mingdong","key":"dongpau","last":"Dong","locid":"b54afe28-ba86-4353-9f09-6618abd83284","name":"Dong, Mingdong","orcid":"0000-0002-2025-2171","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Fengqin","key":"fengpau","last":"Feng","name":"Feng, Fengqin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zheng","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","locid":"67372258-2bc9-4585-98c9-1b93c60d0ca9","name":"Guo, Zheng","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/c6gc00866f","issn":["14639262","14639270"],"issn_org":["14639262"],"issue":"14","journal":"Green Chemistry","pages":"3962-3971","publisher":"Royal Society of Chemistry","status":"p","title":"Green Chemistry","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84978795504"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-965c4ab6-d376-40d8-919b-67b5877b43b5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Synthetic ultra-long chain fatty acyl based amphiphilic lipids as a dual function excipient for the production of surfactant-free solid lipid nanoparticles (SF-SLNs): a physico-chemical study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-214981","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Finding sustainable and commercially viable sources of occlusive materials, as an alternative to petroleum, is of great interest. Inspired by the fundamental role of long chain fatty acids in maintaining skin barrier, ultralong fatty acyl derivatives with diverse structures (varied acyl chain length and different polar head; i.e. glycerol, ethylene glycol, and diethylene glycol) were synthesized. These molecules can be feasibly obtained via enzymatic esterification of fatty acids or fractionated from commercial glycerides mixture via short path distillation. The molecular packing behaviors of compounds were characterized via differential scanning calorimetry, Fourier transform infrared, and Langmuir isotherm measurements. The structure-property relationship study reveals that a glycerol molecule monoacylated with an ultralong fatty acyl is the derivative which entails the most occlusive properties of the series of ultralong chain fatty acid derivatives. Fast Fourier transform filtering (FFTF) analysis of atomic force microscopy images verified a homogeneous monolayer packing of glyceryl monobehenate monolayer, and the water vapor transmission study demonstrated that the formulation of glyceryl monobehenate at 3% w/w in a phospholipid-containing emulsion generates an occlusive film significantly superior to a 3% w/w petrolatum formulation. This work demonstrated that natural glyceryl monobehenate can be a novel source of sustainable occlusive structuring agents and green replacements for petrolatum.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Pérez, Bianca","Bulsara, Pallav","Rawlings, Anothony Vincent","Wei, Wei","Jensen, Mads Mørk","Wang, Zegao","Dickens, Jason","Zhang, Shuai","P. Elliot, Russell","Glasius, Marianne","Dong, Mingdong","Clarke, Martyn","Guo, Zheng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-239575"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Petrolatum","Stratum corneum","Water vapor transmission rate"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ultralong fatty acyl derivatives as occlusive structure lipids for cosmetic applications synthesis and characterization","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85002112698","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-239575","identifier":[{"id":"85002112698","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c13567c5-9759-46df-a903-37b0dca32d38"],"keyword":["Glyceryl monobenhenate","Occlusive materials","Orthorhombic lateral packing","Petrolatum","Stratum corneum","Water vapor transmission rate"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-50CA8DB0573FD75FEA4DE896026B0B4E"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Engineering, Department of Engineering - Biological and Chemical Engineering, Gustav Wieds Vej"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bianca","key":"pérezpau","last":"Pérez","locid":"53fb7df0-13cb-4efd-a0eb-aa03e8db8f9c","name":"Pérez, Bianca","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pallav","key":"bulsarapau","last":"Bulsara","name":"Bulsara, Pallav","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anothony Vincent","key":"rawlingspau","last":"Rawlings","name":"Rawlings, Anothony Vincent","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","locid":"eba1f296-6e64-4865-9eb0-8f10c76bc212","name":"Wei, Wei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Mørk","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e169a325-60dc-4607-9273-07bfed6ede9e","name":"Jensen, Mads Mørk","orcid":"0000-0002-7870-9613","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zegao","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"2f191f69-88c1-4291-8610-6d3b85bbc312","name":"Wang, Zegao","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jason","key":"dickenspau","last":"Dickens","name":"Dickens, Jason","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuai","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"1b6e5a08-f4b5-44df-b8a1-a3461676093b","name":"Zhang, Shuai","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Russell","key":"pelliotpau","last":"P. Elliot","name":"P. Elliot, Russell","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marianne","key":"glasiuspau","last":"Glasius","locid":"c161fb26-0c93-4fa3-9db7-88ddd5c4b78d","name":"Glasius, Marianne","orcid":"0000-0002-4404-6989","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"MD","key":"dongpau","last":"Dong","locid":"b54afe28-ba86-4353-9f09-6618abd83284","name":"Dong, Mingdong","name_org":"Dong, MD","orcid":"0000-0002-2025-2171","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martyn","key":"clarkepau","last":"Clarke","name":"Clarke, Martyn","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zheng","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","locid":"67372258-2bc9-4585-98c9-1b93c60d0ca9","name":"Guo, Zheng","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acssuschemeng.6b02021","issn":["21680485"],"issue":"12","journal":"ACS Sustainable Chemistry & Engineering","pages":"7137-7146","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"ACS Sustainable Chemistry & Engineering","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85002112698"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c13567c5-9759-46df-a903-37b0dca32d38"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Ultralong Fatty Acyl Derivatives As Occlusive Structure Lipids for Cosmetic Applications : Synthesis and Characterization","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-239575","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Osteoclast-associated receptor (OSCAR) is an activating receptor expressed by human myeloid cells. Collagen type I (ColI) and collagen type II (ColII) serve as ligands for OSCAR. OSCAR-collagen interaction stimulates RANK-dependent osteoclastogenesis. We have recently reported that OSCAR promotes functional maturation of monocyte-derived dendritic cells. OSCAR is upregulated on monocytes from rheumatoid arthritis (RA) patients with active disease, and these monocytes show an increased proosteoclastogenic potential. In the current study, we have addressed a functional role for an OSCAR-collagen interaction on monocytes. We show that OSCAR-ColII signaling promoted the survival of monocytes. Moreover, ColII stimulated the release of proinflammatory cytokines by monocytes from healthy donors, which could be completely blocked by an anti-OSCAR monoclonal antibody. Mononuclear cells from the synovial fluid of RA patients plated on ColII secreted TNF-α and IL-8 in an OSCAR-dependent manner. Global RNA profiling showed that components of multiple signaling pathways relevant to RA pathogenesis are regulated at the transcriptional level by OSCAR in monocytes. Thus, OSCAR can play a proinflammatory role in monocyte-derived cells and may contribute crucially on multiple levels to RA pathogenesis.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Schultz, Heidi Schiøler","Guo, Li","Keller, Pernille","Fleetwood, Andrew J.","Sun, Mingyi","Guo, Wei","Ma, Chunyan","Hamilton, John A","Bjørkdahl, Olle","Berchtold, Martin Werner","Panina, Svetlana"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-437226"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"oscar collagen signaling in monocytes plays a proinflammatory role and may contribute to the pathogenesis of rheumatoid arthritis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-437226","identifier":[{"id":"84962874735","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26786702","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-495680ef-3267-4354-997f-527ca685ac24"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A205C6CFE645417522402D33F58A818C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Cell Biology and Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Heidi Schiøler","key":"schultzheidischiølerpau","last":"Schultz","locid":"d71e6952-8322-4319-ad2b-06c7f7c9acc7","name":"Schultz, Heidi Schiøler","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Li","key":"guolipau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Li","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Pernille","key":"kellerpernillepau","last":"Keller","name":"Keller, Pernille","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrew J.","key":"fleetwoodandrewjpau","last":"Fleetwood","name":"Fleetwood, Andrew J.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mingyi","key":"sunmingyipau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Mingyi","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Wei","key":"guoweipau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Wei","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Chunyan","key":"machunyanpau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Chunyan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"John A","key":"hamiltonjohnapau","last":"Hamilton","name":"Hamilton, John A","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Olle","key":"bjørkdahlollepau","last":"Bjørkdahl","name":"Bjørkdahl, Olle","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin Werner","key":"berchtoldmartinwernerpau","last":"Berchtold","locid":"f99f5ba9-cc93-40eb-adbb-370f6ba1f9a0","name":"Berchtold, Martin Werner","orcid":"0000-0001-8995-9047","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Svetlana","key":"paninasvetlanapau","last":"Panina","name":"Panina, Svetlana","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26786702"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/eji.201545986","issn":["00142980","15214141"],"issn_org":["00142980"],"issue":"4","journal":"European Journal of Immunology","pages":"952-963","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Immunology","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84962874735"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-495680ef-3267-4354-997f-527ca685ac24"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"OSCAR-collagen signaling in monocytes plays a proinflammatory role and may contribute to the pathogenesis of rheumatoid arthritis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-437226","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"AIMS/HYPOTHESIS: Genome-wide association studies (GWAS) have discovered many risk variants for type 2 diabetes. However, estimates of the contributions of risk variants to type 2 diabetes predisposition are often based on highly selected case-control samples, and reliable estimates of population-level effect sizes are missing, especially in non-European populations. METHODS: The individual and cumulative effects of 59 established type 2 diabetes risk loci were measured in a population-based China Kadoorie Biobank (CKB) study of 93,000 Chinese adults, including >7,100 diabetes cases. RESULTS: Association signals were directionally consistent between CKB and the original discovery GWAS: of 56 variants passing quality control, 48 showed the same direction of effect (binomial test, p = 2.3 × 10(-8)). We observed a consistent overall trend towards lower risk variant effect sizes in CKB than in case-control samples of GWAS meta-analyses (mean 19-22% decrease in log odds, p ≤ 0.0048), likely to reflect correction of both 'winner's curse' and spectrum bias effects. The association with risk of diabetes of a genetic risk score, based on lead variants at 25 loci considered to act through beta cell function, demonstrated significant interactions with several measures of adiposity (BMI, waist circumference [WC], WHR and percentage body fat [PBF]; all p interaction < 1 × 10(-4)), with a greater effect being observed in leaner adults. CONCLUSIONS/INTERPRETATION: Our study provides further evidence of shared genetic architecture for type 2 diabetes between Europeans and East Asians. It also indicates that even very large GWAS meta-analyses may be vulnerable to substantial inflation of effect size estimates, compared with those observed in large-scale population-based cohort studies. ACCESS TO RESEARCH MATERIALS: Details of how to access China Kadoorie Biobank data and details of the data release schedule are available from www.ckbiobank.org/site/Data+Access .","author_count":17,"contributors":["Gan, Wei","Walters, Robin G","Holmes, Michael V","Bragg, Fiona","Millwood, Iona Y","Banasik, Karina","Chen, Yiping","Du, Huaidong","Iona, Andri","Mahajan, Anubha","Yang, Ling","Bian, Zheng","Guo, Yu","Clarke, Robert J","Li, Liming","McCarthy, Mark I","Chen, Zhengming"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-460027"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["China Kadoorie Biobank Collaborative Group"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluation of type 000000000002 diabetes genetic risk variants in chinese adults findings from 000000000093 000000000000 individuals from the china kadoorie biobank","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00125-016-3920-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-460027","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4901105","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"27053236","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84962658983","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6f6def47-6c45-4876-96e2-ab6ef6814e5c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C35660A8EEB8B29BEE8916D5020014A4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00125-016-3920-9","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Human Genomics and M