{"abstract":"Glucocorticoidinduced osteoporosis (GIOP) is a widespread clinical complication following glucocorticoid therapy. This irreversible damage to boneforming and resorbing cells is essential in the pathogenesis of osteoporosis. Autophagy is a physiological process involved in the regulation of cells and their responses to diverse stimuli, however, the role of autophagy in glucocorticoidinduced damage to bone marrow mesenchymal stem cells (BMSCs) remains unclear. The current study confirmed that glucocorticoid administration impaired the proliferation of BMSCs. Transmission electron microscopy, immunohistochemistry and western blot analysis detected autophagy in vitro and in GIOP model rats (in vivo). With the addition of the autophagy inhibitor 3methyladenine, the proliferative ability of BMSCs was further reduced, while the number of apoptotic BMSCs was significantly increased. The data suggests that in response to glucocorticoid administration, induced autophagy aids to maintain proliferation and prevent apoptosis of BMSCs. Thus, it is hypothesized that autophagy may be a novel target in the treatment or prevention of osteoporosis.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Wang, L.","Fan, J.","Lin, Y. S.","Guo, Y. S.","Gao, B.","Shi, Q. Y.","Wei, B. Y.","Chen, Li","Yang, L.","Liu, J.","Luo, Z. J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-632612"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"glucocorticoids induce autophagy in rat bone marrow mesenchymal stem cells","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3892/mmr.2014.3099","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-632612","identifier":[{"id":"84921361567","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25515523","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-cf37bb1b-b3b0-469e-8e92-6eda18643388"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-747B4A6F74492198C98726F36ED7B29F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3892/mmr.2014.3099","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, KMEB - Molecular Endocrinology Department (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, L.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"fanpau","last":"Fan","name":"Fan, J.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Y. S.","key":"linpau","last":"Lin","name":"Lin, Y. S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Y. S.","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Y. S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"B.","key":"gaopau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, B.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Q. Y.","key":"shipau","last":"Shi","name":"Shi, Q. Y.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"B. Y.","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, B. Y.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","locid":"b1593ebb-9d47-47b4-9c4b-d95cd459c403","name":"Chen, Li","name_org":"Chen, L.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, L.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, J.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Z. J.","key":"luopau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Z. J.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25515523"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3892/mmr.2014.3099","issn":["17912997","17913004"],"issn_org":["17912997"],"issue":"4","journal":"Molecular Medicine Reports","pages":"2711-2716","publisher":"Spandidos Publications","status":"p","title":"Molecular Medicine Reports","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84921361567"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-cf37bb1b-b3b0-469e-8e92-6eda18643388"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Glucocorticoids induce autophagy in rat bone marrow mesenchymal stem cells","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-632612","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Throughout northeast China, the widely distributed peatlands have formed a large carbon (C) pool. However, the relationship between peatland initiation and climate controls is still poorly documented and understood. Understanding the responses of these C-rich ecosystems to past climate change will provide useful insights into projecting the fate of peatland C in the future. In this study, we present a detailed historical reconstruction of peatland development in northeast China based on 312 basal peat dates, and examine the relationship between Holocene peatland dynamics and climate sensitivity. Our results indicate that peatland initiation started in the early Holocene, and that the majority of peatlands were initiated by and developed during the late Holocene. After the most intensive initiation period of 4.2-0.8ka, the rate of peatland development slowed, which was concomitant with decreasing insolation and monsoon intensity. The widespread peatland initiation in the late Holocene might have been caused by the cool and moist climate patterns. The optimum timing of the peatland development was not uniform across northeast China, and these spatio-temporal differences indicate the influences of regional climate and terrain on peatland initiation. Peat-core data show variations in the long-term apparent rate of C accumulation (LORCA) during the Holocene, with an average rate of 37.2gCm(-2)a(-1). The peak LORCA occurred during 10.5-9.0ka, probably in response to higher temperatures and stronger East Asia summer monsoon intensities. Both temperature and humidity are important factors influencing the peatland initiation and C dynamics in this region.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Xing, Wei","Bao, Kunshan","Guo, Wen Yong","Lu, Xianguo","Wang, Guoping"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-175102"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Wang, Guoping"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Nanjing Institute of Geography and Limnology","Chinese Academy of Sciences","University of Science and Technology of China"],"keyword":["Accumulation","BP","East Asian monsoon","High resolution","Lake","Precipitation","Sediments","Tibetan Plateau"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"peatland initiation and carbon dynamics in northeast china links to holocene climate variability","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84931838968","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-175102","identifier":[{"id":"000356626400009","type":"wos"},{"id":"84931838968","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-50474fb7-f59b-44e1-96d0-6d609634fc1a"],"keyword":["ACCUMULATION","ATMOSPHERIC CH4","BP","EAST-ASIAN MONSOON","HIGH-RESOLUTION","LAKE","LATERAL EXPANSION","PRECIPITATION","SEDIMENTS","TIBETAN PLATEAU"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2616C9EA6933E6640D55D56FC58B3CEE"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"university of science and technology of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Science and Technology of China","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"cas nanjing institute of geography and limnology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Nanjing Institute of Geography and Limnology","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Bioscience - Plant Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"xingpau","last":"Xing","name":"Xing, Wei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kunshan","key":"baopau","last":"Bao","name":"Bao, Kunshan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenyong","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","locid":"0061a6f4-1828-4e8d-899f-759e877791a6","name":"Guo, Wen Yong","name_org":"Guo, Wenyong","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Xianguo","key":"lupau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Xianguo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Guoping","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Guoping","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/bor.12116","issn":["03009483","15023885"],"issn_org":["03009483"],"issue":"3","journal":"Boreas","pages":"575-587","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Boreas","volume":"44"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84931838968"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-50474fb7-f59b-44e1-96d0-6d609634fc1a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Peatland initiation and carbon dynamics in northeast China : links to Holocene climate variability","type":"Journal Article","ur