{"abstract":"We present a study of the dissociative chemisorption of NO, O2, and N2 over close-packed, stepped, kinked, and open (fcc {111}, {211}, {311}, {532}, {100}, and {110}) transition metal facets using density functional theory (DFT). The offset of the Bronsted-Evans-Polanyi (BEP) relations suggest that the {111} surface is the least reactive, and that the {110} surface is the most reactive. This observation is verified by establishing volcano-relations based on mean-field microkinetic models for each facet, showing that the maximum rate over {110} is 4 orders of magnitude larger than the maximum {111} rate. The ordering of the maximum activity over the facets is: {110} > {100} similar to {532} > {311} similar to {211} > {111}, which is in general agreement with the offset in the BEP relations. We show that the top-point location and shape of the volcano relations are approximately independent of facet. This observation lends credibility to the approach of analyzing trends in catalytic reactivity over a single low-index facet, and assuming the experimentally observed activity trends are qualitatively well-described by such a single-facet analysis. Our study suggests that a key element for generally obtaining quantitative agreement between theory and experiments is for the simulations to address in detail the propensities of the various types of active sites. Finally, we show that the ordering of NO decomposition rates among metals and facets is essentially unaltered when using BEP- and scaling relations in the microkinetics instead of explicit DFT calculations for each elementary reaction step, and that using a \"universal\" BEP relation introduces no significant additional qualitative error in trend prediction.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Falsig, Hanne","Shen, Juan","Khan, Tuhin Suvra","Guo, Wei","Jones, Glenn","Dahl, Søren","Bligaard, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-372879"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stanford University"],"keyword":["Brønsted Evans Polanyi relations","Scaling relations","Sensitivity analysis","Structure sensitivity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the structure sensitivity of direct no decomposition over low index transition metal facets","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11244-013-0164-5","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-372879","identifier":[{"id":"84896557229","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-e48608cc-a64d-4434-b3c6-cdca5312abdf"],"keyword":["Brønsted–Evans– Polanyi relations","Microkinetics","NO decomposition","Scaling relations","Sensitivity analysis","Structure sensitivity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F78420B9550E279BB45C24F3EE12C7FB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11244-013-0164-5","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Computational Atomic-scale Materials Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne","key":"falsigpau","last":"Falsig","locid":"a7fb25db-6fd0-4d47-af1e-6f294057cac3","name":"Falsig, Hanne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan","key":"shenpau","last":"Shen","locid":"b030bc35-a9d6-4eff-bdfe-edfcd43a7bdb","name":"Shen, Juan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tuhin Suvra","key":"khanpau","last":"Khan","locid":"afc9b716-06f3-428d-8d3e-352d6d658ad4","name":"Khan, Tuhin Suvra","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","locid":"db972946-3f4e-4430-add2-61f293df54f8","name":"Guo, Wei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Glenn","key":"jonespau","last":"Jones","locid":"b60fdb79-4ca4-43db-af59-127e949ec44c","name":"Jones, Glenn","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"dahlpau","last":"Dahl","locid":"f89f0ad1-f692-4dea-8a61-fbe7b1cc684d","name":"Dahl, Søren","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"bligaardpau","last":"Bligaard","name":"Bligaard, Thomas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11244-013-0164-5","issn":["10225528","15729028"],"issn_org":["10225528"],"issue":"1-4","journal":"Topics in Catalysis","pages":"80-88","publisher":"Springer New York","status":"p","title":"Topics in Catalysis","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84896557229"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-e48608cc-a64d-4434-b3c6-cdca5312abdf"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"On the Structure Sensitivity of Direct NO Decomposition over Low-Index Transition Metal Facets","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-372879","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"DNA double-strand breaks (DSBs) are highly cytotoxic lesions and pose a major threat to genome stability if not properly repaired. We and others have previously shown that a class of DSB-induced small RNAs (diRNAs) is produced from sequences around DSB sites. DiRNAs are associated with Argonaute (Ago) proteins and play an important role in DSB repair, though the mechanism through which they act remains unclear. Here, we report that the role of diRNAs in DSB repair is restricted to repair by homologous recombination (HR) and that it specifically relies on the effector protein Ago2 in mammalian cells. Interestingly, we show that Ago2 forms a complex with Rad51 and that the interaction is enhanced in cells treated with ionizing radiation. We demonstrate that Rad51 accumulation at DSB sites and HR repair depend on catalytic activity and small RNA-binding capability of Ago2. In contrast, DSB resection as well as RPA and Mre11 loading is unaffected by Ago2 or Dicer depletion, suggesting that Ago2 very likely functions directly in mediating Rad51 accumulation at DSBs. Taken together, our findings suggest that guided by diRNAs, Ago2 can promote Rad51 recruitment and/or retention at DSBs to facilitate repair by HR.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Gao, Min","Wei, Wei","Li, Ming Hua","Wu, Yong-Sheng","Ba, Zhaoqing","Jin, Kang-Xuan","Li, Miao-Miao","Liao, You-Qi","Adhikari, Samir","Chong, Zechen","Zhang, Ting","Guo, Cai-Xia","Tang, Tie-Shan","Zhu, Bing-Tao","Xu, Xing-Zhi","Mailand, Niels","Yang, Yun-Gui","Qi, Yijun","Danielsen, Jannie Michaela Rendtlew"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-439355"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Beijing Institute of Genomics","Tsinghua University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["State Key Laboratory of Biomembrane and Membrane Biotechnology, Institute of Zoology, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing 100101, China."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ago000000000002 facilitates rad000000000051 recruitment and dna double strand break repair by homologous recombination","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/cr.2014.36","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-439355","identifier":[{"id":"24662483","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4011338","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84899898213","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-4d00bc3a-c0c2-44e8-9772-435aa9102a6f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-753550AF26485C54D29729EDB4FF9B6A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/cr.2014.36","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"cas beijing institute of genomics","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Beijing Institute of Genomics","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"tsinghua university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tsinghua University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["State Key Laboratory of Biomembrane and Membrane Biotechnology, Institute of Zoology, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing 100101, China."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet,