dykconfabtlifelinescohortpau","last":"Study","name":"Study, kConFabt LifeLines Cohort","rank":201,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"InterAct","key":"consortiuminteractpau","last":"Consortium","name":"Consortium, InterAct","rank":202,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Early Growth Genetics EGG","key":"consortiearlygrowthgeneticseggpau","last":"Consorti","name":"Consorti, Early Growth Genetics EGG","rank":203,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25231870"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/nature13545","issn":["00280836","14764687"],"issn_org":["00280836"],"issue":"7520","journal":"Nature","pages":"92-97","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature","volume":"514"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84908024873"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4d4bd55d-1155-443d-8c9b-293bf1800fcb","dtu-e683c707-5dc9-4d83-93ae-5c7d29a32807","ku-c706445b-96e0-4a90-bd02-928274730760","sdu-6e792e38-06d9-4bfc-936c-7c03c4fe882b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Parent-of-origin-specific allelic associations among 106 genomic loci for age at menarche","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.44-018303","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BackgroundNearly a quarter of all avian species is either threatened or nearly threatened. Of these, 73 species are currently being rescued from going extinct in wildlife sanctuaries. One of the previously most critically-endangered is the crested ibis, Nipponia nippon. Once widespread across North-East Asia, by 1981 only seven individuals from two breeding pairs remained in the wild. The recovering crested ibis populations thus provide an excellent example for conservation genomics since every individual bird has been recruited for genomic and demographic studies.ResultsUsing high-quality genome sequences of multiple crested ibis individuals, its thriving co-habitant, the little egret, Egretta garzetta, and the recently sequenced genomes of 41 other avian species that are under various degrees of survival threats, including the bald eagle, we carry out comparative analyses for genomic signatures of near extinction events in association with environmental and behavioral attributes of species. We confirm that both loss of genetic diversity and enrichment of deleterious mutations of protein-coding genes contribute to the major genetic defects of the endangered species. We further identify that genetic inbreeding and loss-of-function genes in the crested ibis may all constitute genetic susceptibility to other factors including long-term climate change, over-hunting, and agrochemical overuse. We also establish a genome-wide DNA identification platform for molecular breeding and conservation practices, to facilitate sustainable recovery of endangered species.ConclusionsThese findings demonstrate common genomic signatures of population decline across avian species and pave a way for further effort in saving endangered species and enhancing conservation genomic efforts.","author_count":33,"contributors":["Li, Shengbin","Li, Bo","Cheng, Cheng","Xiong, Zijun","Liu, Qingbo","Lai, Jianghua","Carey, Hannah V.","Zhang, Qiong","Zheng, Haibo","Wei, Shuguang","Zhang, Hongbo","Chang, Liao","Liu, Shiping","Zhang, Shanxin","Yu, Bing","Zeng, Xiaofan","Hou, Yong","Nie, Wenhui","Guo, Youmin","Chen, Teng","Han, Jiuqiang","Wang, Jian","Wang, Jun","Chen, Chen","Liu, Jiankang","Stambrook, Peter J","Xu, Ming","Zhang, Guojie","Gilbert, M. Thomas P.","Yang, Huanming","Jarvis, Erich D","Yu, Jun","Yan, Jianqun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-404576"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","University of Wisconsin School of Veterinary Medicine","Xi'an Jiaotong University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genomic signatures of near extinction and rebirth of the crested ibis and other endangered bird species","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13059-014-0557-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-404576","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4290368","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84996489169","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25496777","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-12b8d8ff-f917-4bcd-b3da-9cb1a11f4955"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-36CD7AF5E013B471035A6CBBD2FF4B6F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/132418983/Genomic_signatures_of_near_extinction_and_rebirth.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13059-014-0557-1","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"xi a