{"abstract":"The Casimir effect for two parallel slabs immersed in an ideal Fermi sea is investigated at both zero and nonzero temperatures. It is found that the Casimir effect in a Fermi gas is distinctly different from that in an electromagnetic field or a massive Bose gas. In contrast to the familiar result that the Casimir force decreases monotonically with the increase of the separation L between two slabs in an electromagnetic field and a massive Bose gas, the Casimir force in a Fermi gas oscillates as a function of L. The Casimir force can be either attractive or repulsive, depending sensitively on the magnitude of L. In addition, it is found that the amplitude of the Casimir force in a Fermi gas decreases with the increase of the temperature, which also is contrary to the case in a Bose gas, since the bosonic Casimir force increases linearly with the increase of the temperature in the region T <T-c, where T-c is the critical temperature of the Bose-Einstein condensation.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Chen, Liwei","Su, Guozhen","Chen, Jincan","Andresen, Bjarne Bøgeskov"],"cuid":["S02-083.03-040810"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Xiamen University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"oscillating casimir force between two slabs in a fermi sea","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-083.03-040810","identifier":[{"id":"84863066784","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-222c4520-efe3-4f97-b88b-28855ab2ab05","ku-40ac4252-2d74-4c56-a647-2f2b95f1b11a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-70A8C9D80F37719EF68AF22D65584701"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"xiamen university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Xiamen University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Condensed Matter Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Liwei","key":"chenliweipau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Liwei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chen","key":"liweichenpau","last":"Li-Wei","name":"Li-Wei, Chen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Guozhen","key":"suguozhenpau","last":"Su","name":"Su, Guozhen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Su","key":"guozhensupau","last":"Guo-Zhen","name":"Guo-Zhen, Su","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jincan","key":"chenjincanpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Jincan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chen","key":"jincanchenpau","last":"Jin-Can","name":"Jin-Can, Chen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Bjarne Bøgeskov","key":"andresenbjarnebøgeskovpau","last":"Andresen","locid":"fc81eeff-5e4d-48bf-b2eb-c26af47a176c","name":"Andresen, Bjarne Bøgeskov","orcid":"0000-0003-2657-3424","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/1674-1056/21/1/010501","issn":["16741056","20583834"],"issn_org":["16741056"],"issue":"1","journal":"Chinese Physics B","paperid":"010501","status":"p","title":"Chinese Physics B","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84863066784"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-222c4520-efe3-4f97-b88b-28855ab2ab05","ku-40ac4252-2d74-4c56-a647-2f2b95f1b11a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Oscillating Casimir force between two slabs in a Fermi sea","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-083.03-040810","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Oxidation behavior of hot forged textured ZrB2–20vol% MoSi2 ceramics with platelet ZrB2 grains was investigated at 1500°C for exposure time from 0.5 to 12h. Compared to untextured ceramics, the textured ceramics showed obvious anisotropic oxidation behavior and the surface normal to the hot forging pressure demonstrated better oxidation resistance. Such improvement in the oxidation resistance is primarily considered as a higher intrinsic ZrB2 atomic density on the orientated {00l} planes in the textured ceramics. It is expectable that the anisotropic textured ZrB2–MoSi2 ceramics can offer better oxidation resistance when a certain surface with higher oxidation resistance is exposed to air at elevated temperature.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Liu, Hai-Tao","Zou, Ji","Ni, De Wei","Liu, Ji-Xuan","Zhang, Guo-Jun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-373592"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Shanghai Institute of Ceramics"],"keyword":["Anisotropy","Borides","Oxidation resistance","Silicides"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"anisotropy oxidation of textured zrb sub 000000000002 sub mosi sub 000000000002 sub ceramics","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jeurceramsoc.2012.03.036","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-373592","identifier":[{"id":"84862492692","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-e6dd10b4-64da-4bcb-9624-2b67b1a6ac6c"],"keyword":["Anisotropy","Borides","Oxidation resistance","Silicides"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1CDC4C131E09CFD547F5BEFA20F17AC9"],"oa