","first":"Xue-Jun","key":"zhangxuejunpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Xue-Jun","rank":29,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22972947"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/jmedgenet-2012-100868","issn":["00222593","14686244"],"issn_org":["00222593"],"journal":"Journal of Medical Genetics","pages":"563-568","status":"p","title":"Journal of Medical Genetics","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84870282813"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-02cb4450-d9b7-4768-9b96-154d99256add"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exome sequencing identifies a <em>COL14A1</em> mutation in a large Chinese pedigree with punctate palmoplantar keratoderma","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-395148","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The constant self renewal and differentiation of adult intestinal stem cells maintains a functional intestinal mucosa for a lifetime. However, the molecular mechanisms that regulate intestinal stem cell division and epithelial homeostasis are largely undefined. We report here that the small GTPases Cdc42 and Rab8a are critical regulators of these processes in mice. Conditional ablation of Cdc42 in the mouse intestinal epithelium resulted in the formation of large intracellular vacuolar structures containing microvilli (microvillus inclusion bodies) in epithelial enterocytes, a phenotype reminiscent of human microvillus inclusion disease (MVID), a devastating congenital intestinal disorder that results in severe nutrient deprivation. Further analysis revealed that Cdc42-deficient stem cells had cell division defects, reduced capacity for clonal expansion and differentiation into Paneth cells, and increased apoptosis. Cdc42 deficiency impaired Rab8a activation and its association with multiple effectors, and prevented trafficking of Rab8a vesicles to the midbody. This impeded cytokinesis, triggering crypt apoptosis and disrupting epithelial morphogenesis. Rab8a was also required for Cdc42-GTP activity in the intestinal epithelium, where continued cell division takes place. Furthermore, mice haploinsufficient for both Cdc42 and Rab8a in the intestine demonstrated abnormal crypt morphogenesis and epithelial transporter physiology, further supporting their functional interaction. These data suggest that defects of the stem cell niche can cause MVID. This hypothesis represents a conceptual departure from the conventional view of this disease, which has focused on the affected enterocytes, and suggests stem cell-based approaches could be beneficial to infants with this often lethal condition.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Sakamori, Ryotaro","Das, Soumyashree","Yu, Shiyan","Feng, Shanshan","Stypulkowski, Ewa","Guan, Yinzheng","Douard, Veronique","Tang, Waixing","Ferraris, Ronaldo P","Harada, Akihiro","Brakebusch, Cord","Guo, Wei","Gao, Nan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-518955"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Animals","Biological Transport","Cell Differentiation","Cell Survival","Cell cycle","Gene Expression Regulation","HeLa Cells","Humans","Intestines","Mice","Models Biological","Models Genetic","Phenotype","Stem cells","cdc42 GTP Binding Protein","rab GTP Binding Proteins"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cdc000000000042 and rab000000000008a are critical for intestinal stem cell division survival and differentiation in mice","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1172/JCI60282","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-518955","identifier":[{"id":"22354172","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3287229","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84863393793","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d20c9c1a-6884-4cfb-838c-f853a9f5e13d"],"keyword":["Animals","Biological Transport","Cell Cycle","Cell Differentiation","Cell Survival","Gene Expression Regulation","HeLa Cells","Humans","Intestines","Mice","Models, Biological","Models, Genetic","Phenotype","Stem Cells","cdc42 GTP-Binding Protein","rab GTP-Binding Proteins"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-E8AFE1642DD0981A93712D935E32836C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1172/JCI60282","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Nutritional Immunology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Ryotaro","key":"sakamoripau","last":"Sakamori","name":"Sakamori, Ryotaro","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Soumyashree","key":"daspau","last":"Das","name":"Das, Soumyashree","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Shiyan","key":"yupau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Shiyan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Shanshan","key":"fengpau","last":"Feng","name":"Feng, Shanshan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ewa","key":"stypulkowskipau","last":"Stypulkowski","name":"Stypulkowski, Ewa","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yinzheng","key":"guanpau","last":"Guan","name":"Guan, Yinzheng","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Veronique","key":"douardpau","last":"Douard","name":"Douard, Veronique","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Waixing","key":"tangpau","last":"Tang","name":"Tang, Waixing","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ronaldo P","key":"ferrarispau","last":"Ferraris","name":"Ferraris, Ronaldo P","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Akihiro","key":"haradapau","last":"Harada","name":"Harada, Akihiro","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Cord","key":"brakebuschpau","last":"Brakebusch","locid":"03565624-9960-4f23-a1b1-ee653c4106f7","name":"Brakebusch, Cord","orcid":"0000-0002-9342-1634","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wei","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Wei","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nan","key":"gaopau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Nan","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22354172"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1172/jci60282","issn":["00219738","15588238"],"issn_org":["00219738"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Clinical Investigation","pages":"1052-65","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Investigation","volume":"122"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84863393793"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d20c9c1a-6884-4cfb-838c-f853a9f5e13d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cdc42 and Rab8a are critical for intestinal stem cell division, survival, and differentiation in mice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-518955","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The whipworm, Trichuris trichiura, causes trichuriasis in ~600 million people worldwide, mainly in developing countries. Whipworms also infect other animal hosts, including pigs (T. suis), dogs (T. vulpis) and non-human primates, and cause disease in these hosts, which is similar to trichuriasis of humans. Although Trichuris species are considered to be host specific, there has been considerable controversy, over the years, as to whether T. trichiura and T. suis are the same or distinct species. Here, we characterised the entire mitochondrial genomes of human-derived Trichuris and pig-derived Trichuris, compared them and then tested the hypothesis that the parasites from these two host species are genetically distinct in a phylogenetic analysis of the sequence data. Taken together, the findings support the proposal that T. trichiura and T. suis are separate species, consistent with previous data for nuclear ribosomal DNA. Using molecular analytical tools, employing genetic markers defined herein, future work should conduct large-scale studies to establish whether T. trichiura is found in pigs and T. suis in humans in endemic regions.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Liu, Guo-Hua","Gasser, Robin B.","Su, Ang","Nejsum, Peter","Peng, Lifei","Lin, Rui-Qing","Li, Ming-Wei","Xu, Min-Jun","Zhu, Xing-Quan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-432306"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Agricultural Sciences","Guangdong Medical College","Guangdong Ocean University","South China Agricultural University","University of Melbourne"],"keyword":["Animals","Cluster Analysis","DNA Mitochondrial","Humans","Molecular Sequence Data","Phylogeny","Sequence Analysis DNA","Swine","Trichuriasis","Trichuris"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"clear genetic distinctiveness between human and pig derived em trichuris em based on analyses of mitochondrial datasets","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pntd.0001539","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-432306","identifier":[{"id":"84857827799","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22363831","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3283558","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-40ffe8bd-afd9-4ced-b959-cfc1b7ced4eb"],"keyword":["Animals","Cluster Analysis","DNA, Mitochondrial","Humans","Molecular Sequence Data","Phylogeny","Sequence Analysis, DNA","Swine","Trichuriasis","Trichuris"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B3AAD1872D86B1F291B6CCB15C955D26"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pntd.0001539","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of agricultural sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Agricultural Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"university of melbourne","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Melbourne","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Veterinary Disease Biology, Section of Parasitology, Health and Development"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"guangdong medical college","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Guangdong Medical College","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"south china agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"South China Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"cn","key":"guangdong ocean university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Guangdong Ocean University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Guo-Hua","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Guo-Hua","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Robin B.","key":"gasserpau","last":"Gasser","name":"Gasser, Robin B.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ang","key":"supau","last":"Su","name":"Su, Ang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"nejsumpau","last":"Nejsum","locid":"a21a2f45-b747-46f8-8b4b-b369c9aba7d1","name":"Nejsum, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-6673-8505","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Lifei","key":"pengpau","last":"Peng","name":"Peng, Lifei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Rui-Qing","key":"linpau","last":"Lin","name":"Lin, Rui-Qing","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Ming-Wei","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Ming-Wei","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Min-Jun","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Min-Jun","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xing-Quan","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Xing-Quan","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22363831"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pntd.0001539","issn":["19352735"],"issue":"2","journal":"PLoS Neglected Tropical Diseases","status":"p","title":"PLoS Neglected Tropical Diseases","title_org":"P L o S Neglected Tropical Diseases (Online)","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84857827799"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-40ffe8bd-afd9-4ced-b959-cfc1b7ced4eb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Clear genetic distinctiveness between human- and pig-derived <em>Trichuris</em> based on analyses of mitochondrial datasets","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-432306","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The Pacific oyster Crassostrea gigas belongs to one of the most species-rich but genomically poorly explored phyla, the Mollusca. Here we report the sequencing and assembly of the oyster genome using short reads and a fosmid-pooling strategy, along with transcriptomes of development and stress response and the proteome of the shell. The oyster genome is highly polymorphic and rich in repetitive sequences, with some transposable elements still actively shaping variation. Transcriptome studies reveal an extensive set of genes responding to environmental stress. The expansion of genes coding for heat shock protein 70 and inhibitors of apoptosis is probably central to the oyster's adaptation to sessile life in the highly stressful intertidal zone. Our analyses also show that shell formation in molluscs is more complex than currently understood and involves extensive participation of cells and their exosomes. The oyster genome sequence fills a void in our understanding of the Lophotrochozoa.","author_count":85,"contributors":["Zhang, Guofan","Fang, Xiaodong","Guo, Ximing","Li, Li","Luo, Ruibang","Xu, Fei","Yang, Pengcheng","Zhang, Linlin","Wang, Xiaotong","Qi, Haigang","Xiong, Zhiqiang","Que, Huayong","Xie, Yinlong","Holland, Peter","Paps, Jordi","Zhu, Yabing","Wu, Fucun","Chen, Yuanxin","Wang, Jiafeng","Peng, Chunfang","Meng, Jie","Yang, Lan","Liu, Jun","Wen, Bo","Zhang, Na","Huang, Zhiyong","Zhu, Qihui","Feng, Yue","Mount, Andrew","Hedgecock, Dennis","Xu, Zhe","Liu, Yunjie","Domazet-Loso, Tomislav","Du, Yishuai","Sun, Xiaoqing","Zhang, Shoudu","Liu, Binghang","Cheng, Peizhou","Jiang, Xuanting","Li, Juan","Fan, Dingding","Wang, Wei","Fu, Wenjing","Wang, Tong","Wang, Bo","Zhang, Jibiao","Peng, Zhiyu","Li, Yingxiang","Li, Na","Wang, Jinpeng","Chen, Maoshan","He, Yan","Tan, Fengji","Song, Xiaorui","Zheng, Qiumei","Huang, Ronglian","Yang, Hailong","Du, Xuedi","Chen, Li","Yang, Mei","Gaffney, Patrick","Wang, Shan","Luo, Longhai","She, Zhicai","Ming, Yao","Huang,